-- BSB verses (1978). Requires books and chapters first.
insert into public.verses (chapter_id, number, osis_ref, text)
select c.id, x.verse, x.ref, x.body
from (values
('GAL', 3, 22, 'GAL.3.22', 'But the Scripture pronounces all things confined by sin, so that by faith in Jesus Christ the promise might be given to those who believe.'),
('GAL', 3, 23, 'GAL.3.23', 'Before this faith came, we were held in custody under the law, locked up until faith should be revealed.'),
('GAL', 3, 24, 'GAL.3.24', 'So the law became our guardian to lead us to Christ, that we might be justified by faith.'),
('GAL', 3, 25, 'GAL.3.25', 'Now that faith has come, we are no longer under a guardian.'),
('GAL', 3, 26, 'GAL.3.26', 'You are all sons of God through faith in Christ Jesus.'),
('GAL', 3, 27, 'GAL.3.27', 'For all of you who were baptized into Christ have clothed yourselves with Christ.'),
('GAL', 3, 28, 'GAL.3.28', 'There is neither Jew nor Greek, slave nor free, male nor female, for you are all one in Christ Jesus.'),
('GAL', 3, 29, 'GAL.3.29', 'And if you belong to Christ, then you are Abraham’s seed and heirs according to the promise.'),
('GAL', 4, 1, 'GAL.4.1', 'What I am saying is that as long as the heir is a child, he is no different from a slave, although he is the owner of everything.'),
('GAL', 4, 2, 'GAL.4.2', 'He is subject to guardians and trustees until the date set by his father.'),
('GAL', 4, 3, 'GAL.4.3', 'So also, when we were children, we were enslaved under the basic principles of the world.'),
('GAL', 4, 4, 'GAL.4.4', 'But when the time had fully come, God sent His Son, born of a woman, born under the law,'),
('GAL', 4, 5, 'GAL.4.5', 'to redeem those under the law, that we might receive our adoption as sons.'),
('GAL', 4, 6, 'GAL.4.6', 'And because you are sons, God sent the Spirit of His Son into our hearts, crying out, “Abba, Father!”'),
('GAL', 4, 7, 'GAL.4.7', 'So you are no longer a slave, but a son; and since you are a son, you are also an heir through God.'),
('GAL', 4, 8, 'GAL.4.8', 'Formerly, when you did not know God, you were slaves to those who by nature are not gods.'),
('GAL', 4, 9, 'GAL.4.9', 'But now that you know God, or rather are known by God, how is it that you are turning back to those weak and worthless principles? Do you wish to be enslaved by them all over again?'),
('GAL', 4, 10, 'GAL.4.10', 'You are observing special days and months and seasons and years!'),
('GAL', 4, 11, 'GAL.4.11', 'I fear for you, that my efforts for you may have been in vain.'),
('GAL', 4, 12, 'GAL.4.12', 'I beg you, brothers, become like me, for I became like you. You have done me no wrong.'),
('GAL', 4, 13, 'GAL.4.13', 'You know that it was because of an illness that I first preached the gospel to you.'),
('GAL', 4, 14, 'GAL.4.14', 'And although my illness was a trial to you, you did not despise or reject me. Instead, you welcomed me as if I were an angel of God, as if I were Christ Jesus Himself.'),
('GAL', 4, 15, 'GAL.4.15', 'What then has become of your blessing? For I can testify that, if it were possible, you would have torn out your eyes and given them to me.'),
('GAL', 4, 16, 'GAL.4.16', 'Have I now become your enemy by telling you the truth?'),
('GAL', 4, 17, 'GAL.4.17', 'Those people are zealous for you, but not in a good way. Instead, they want to isolate you from us, so that you may be zealous for them.'),
('GAL', 4, 18, 'GAL.4.18', 'Nevertheless, it is good to be zealous if it serves a noble purpose—at any time, and not only when I am with you.'),
('GAL', 4, 19, 'GAL.4.19', 'My children, for whom I am again in the pains of childbirth until Christ is formed in you,'),
('GAL', 4, 20, 'GAL.4.20', 'how I wish I could be with you now and change my tone, because I am perplexed about you.'),
('GAL', 4, 21, 'GAL.4.21', 'Tell me, you who want to be under the law, do you not understand what the law says?'),
('GAL', 4, 22, 'GAL.4.22', 'For it is written that Abraham had two sons, one by the slave woman and the other by the free woman.'),
('GAL', 4, 23, 'GAL.4.23', 'His son by the slave woman was born according to the flesh, but his son by the free woman was born through the promise.'),
('GAL', 4, 24, 'GAL.4.24', 'These things serve as illustrations, for the women represent two covenants. One covenant is from Mount Sinai and bears children into slavery: This is Hagar.'),
('GAL', 4, 25, 'GAL.4.25', 'Now Hagar stands for Mount Sinai in Arabia and corresponds to the present-day Jerusalem, because she is in slavery with her children.'),
('GAL', 4, 26, 'GAL.4.26', 'But the Jerusalem above is free, and she is our mother.'),
('GAL', 4, 27, 'GAL.4.27', 'For it is written: “Rejoice, O barren woman, who bears no children; break forth and cry aloud, you who have never travailed; because more are the children of the desolate woman than of her who has a husband.”'),
('GAL', 4, 28, 'GAL.4.28', 'Now you, brothers, like Isaac, are children of promise.'),
('GAL', 4, 29, 'GAL.4.29', 'At that time, however, the son born by the flesh persecuted the son born by the Spirit. It is the same now.'),
('GAL', 4, 30, 'GAL.4.30', 'But what does the Scripture say? “Expel the slave woman and her son, for the slave woman’s son will never share in the inheritance with the free woman’s son.”'),
('GAL', 4, 31, 'GAL.4.31', 'Therefore, brothers, we are not children of the slave woman, but of the free woman.'),
('GAL', 5, 1, 'GAL.5.1', 'It is for freedom that Christ has set us free. Stand firm, then, and do not be encumbered once more by a yoke of slavery.'),
('GAL', 5, 2, 'GAL.5.2', 'Take notice: I, Paul, tell you that if you let yourselves be circumcised, Christ will be of no value to you at all.'),
('GAL', 5, 3, 'GAL.5.3', 'Again I testify to every man who gets himself circumcised that he is obligated to obey the whole law.'),
('GAL', 5, 4, 'GAL.5.4', 'You who are trying to be justified by the law have been severed from Christ; you have fallen away from grace.'),
('GAL', 5, 5, 'GAL.5.5', 'But by faith we eagerly await through the Spirit the hope of righteousness.'),
('GAL', 5, 6, 'GAL.5.6', 'For in Christ Jesus neither circumcision nor uncircumcision has any value. What matters is faith expressing itself through love.'),
('GAL', 5, 7, 'GAL.5.7', 'You were running so well. Who has obstructed you from obeying the truth?'),
('GAL', 5, 8, 'GAL.5.8', 'Such persuasion does not come from the One who calls you.'),
('GAL', 5, 9, 'GAL.5.9', 'A little leaven works through the whole batch of dough.'),
('GAL', 5, 10, 'GAL.5.10', 'I am confident in the Lord that you will take no other view. The one who is troubling you will bear the judgment, whoever he may be.'),
('GAL', 5, 11, 'GAL.5.11', 'Now, brothers, if I am still preaching circumcision, why am I still being persecuted? In that case the offense of the cross has been abolished.'),
('GAL', 5, 12, 'GAL.5.12', 'As for those who are agitating you, I wish they would proceed to emasculate themselves!'),
('GAL', 5, 13, 'GAL.5.13', 'For you, brothers, were called to freedom; but do not use your freedom as an opportunity for the flesh. Rather, serve one another in love.'),
('GAL', 5, 14, 'GAL.5.14', 'The entire law is fulfilled in a single decree: “Love your neighbor as yourself.”'),
('GAL', 5, 15, 'GAL.5.15', 'But if you keep on biting and devouring one another, watch out, or you will be consumed by one another.'),
('GAL', 5, 16, 'GAL.5.16', 'So I say, walk by the Spirit, and you will not gratify the desires of the flesh.'),
('GAL', 5, 17, 'GAL.5.17', 'For the flesh craves what is contrary to the Spirit, and the Spirit what is contrary to the flesh. They are opposed to each other, so that you do not do what you want.'),
('GAL', 5, 18, 'GAL.5.18', 'But if you are led by the Spirit, you are not under the law.'),
('GAL', 5, 19, 'GAL.5.19', 'The acts of the flesh are obvious: sexual immorality, impurity, and debauchery;'),
('GAL', 5, 20, 'GAL.5.20', 'idolatry and sorcery; hatred, discord, jealousy, and rage; rivalries, divisions, factions,'),
('GAL', 5, 21, 'GAL.5.21', 'and envy; drunkenness, orgies, and the like. I warn you, as I did before, that those who practice such things will not inherit the kingdom of God.'),
('GAL', 5, 22, 'GAL.5.22', 'But the fruit of the Spirit is love, joy, peace, patience, kindness, goodness, faithfulness,'),
('GAL', 5, 23, 'GAL.5.23', 'gentleness, and self-control. Against such things there is no law.'),
('GAL', 5, 24, 'GAL.5.24', 'Those who belong to Christ Jesus have crucified the flesh with its passions and desires.'),
('GAL', 5, 25, 'GAL.5.25', 'Since we live by the Spirit, let us walk in step with the Spirit.'),
('GAL', 5, 26, 'GAL.5.26', 'Let us not become conceited, provoking and envying one another.'),
('GAL', 6, 1, 'GAL.6.1', 'Brothers, if someone is caught in a trespass, you who are spiritual should restore him with a spirit of gentleness. But watch yourself, or you also may be tempted.'),
('GAL', 6, 2, 'GAL.6.2', 'Carry one another’s burdens, and in this way you will fulfill the law of Christ.'),
('GAL', 6, 3, 'GAL.6.3', 'If anyone thinks he is something when he is nothing, he deceives himself.'),
('GAL', 6, 4, 'GAL.6.4', 'Each one should test his own work. Then he will have reason to boast in himself alone, and not in someone else.'),
('GAL', 6, 5, 'GAL.6.5', 'For each one should carry his own load.'),
('GAL', 6, 6, 'GAL.6.6', 'Nevertheless, the one who receives instruction in the word must share in all good things with his instructor.'),
('GAL', 6, 7, 'GAL.6.7', 'Do not be deceived: God is not to be mocked. Whatever a man sows, he will reap in return.'),
('GAL', 6, 8, 'GAL.6.8', 'The one who sows to please his flesh, from the flesh will reap destruction; but the one who sows to please the Spirit, from the Spirit will reap eternal life.'),
('GAL', 6, 9, 'GAL.6.9', 'Let us not grow weary in well-doing, for in due time we will reap a harvest if we do not give up.'),
('GAL', 6, 10, 'GAL.6.10', 'Therefore, as we have opportunity, let us do good to everyone, and especially to the family of faith.'),
('GAL', 6, 11, 'GAL.6.11', 'See what large letters I am using to write to you with my own hand!'),
('GAL', 6, 12, 'GAL.6.12', 'Those who want to make a good impression outwardly are trying to compel you to be circumcised. They only do this to avoid persecution for the cross of Christ.'),
('GAL', 6, 13, 'GAL.6.13', 'For the circumcised do not even keep the law themselves, yet they want you to be circumcised that they may boast in your flesh.'),
('GAL', 6, 14, 'GAL.6.14', 'But as for me, may I never boast, except in the cross of our Lord Jesus Christ, through which the world has been crucified to me, and I to the world.'),
('GAL', 6, 15, 'GAL.6.15', 'For neither circumcision nor uncircumcision means anything. What counts is a new creation.'),
('GAL', 6, 16, 'GAL.6.16', 'Peace and mercy to all who walk by this rule, even to the Israel of God.'),
('GAL', 6, 17, 'GAL.6.17', 'From now on let no one cause me trouble, for I bear on my body the marks of Jesus.'),
('GAL', 6, 18, 'GAL.6.18', 'The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with your spirit, brothers. Amen.'),
('EPH', 1, 1, 'EPH.1.1', 'Paul, an apostle of Christ Jesus by the will of God, To the saints in Ephesus, the faithful in Christ Jesus:'),
('EPH', 1, 2, 'EPH.1.2', 'Grace and peace to you from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.'),
('EPH', 1, 3, 'EPH.1.3', 'Blessed be the God and Father of our Lord Jesus Christ, who has blessed us in Christ with every spiritual blessing in the heavenly realms.'),
('EPH', 1, 4, 'EPH.1.4', 'For He chose us in Him before the foundation of the world to be holy and blameless in His presence. In love'),
('EPH', 1, 5, 'EPH.1.5', 'He predestined us for adoption as His sons through Jesus Christ, according to the good pleasure of His will,'),
('EPH', 1, 6, 'EPH.1.6', 'to the praise of His glorious grace, which He has freely given us in the Beloved One.'),
('EPH', 1, 7, 'EPH.1.7', 'In Him we have redemption through His blood, the forgiveness of our trespasses, according to the riches of His grace'),
('EPH', 1, 8, 'EPH.1.8', 'that He lavished on us with all wisdom and understanding.'),
('EPH', 1, 9, 'EPH.1.9', 'And He has made known to us the mystery of His will according to His good pleasure, which He purposed in Christ'),
('EPH', 1, 10, 'EPH.1.10', 'as a plan for the fullness of time, to bring all things in heaven and on earth together in Christ.'),
('EPH', 1, 11, 'EPH.1.11', 'In Him we were also chosen as God’s own, having been predestined according to the plan of Him who works out everything by the counsel of His will,'),
('EPH', 1, 12, 'EPH.1.12', 'in order that we, who were the first to hope in Christ, would be for the praise of His glory.'),
('EPH', 1, 13, 'EPH.1.13', 'And in Him, having heard and believed the word of truth—the gospel of your salvation—you were sealed with the promised Holy Spirit,'),
('EPH', 1, 14, 'EPH.1.14', 'who is the pledge of our inheritance until the redemption of those who are God’s possession, to the praise of His glory.'),
('EPH', 1, 15, 'EPH.1.15', 'For this reason, ever since I heard about your faith in the Lord Jesus and your love for all the saints,'),
('EPH', 1, 16, 'EPH.1.16', 'I have not stopped giving thanks for you, remembering you in my prayers,'),
('EPH', 1, 17, 'EPH.1.17', 'that the God of our Lord Jesus Christ, the glorious Father, may give you a spirit of wisdom and revelation in your knowledge of Him.'),
('EPH', 1, 18, 'EPH.1.18', 'I ask that the eyes of your heart may be enlightened, so that you may know the hope of His calling, the riches of His glorious inheritance in the saints,'),
('EPH', 1, 19, 'EPH.1.19', 'and the surpassing greatness of His power to us who believe. These are in accordance with the working of His mighty strength,'),
('EPH', 1, 20, 'EPH.1.20', 'which He exerted in Christ when He raised Him from the dead and seated Him at His right hand in the heavenly realms,'),
('EPH', 1, 21, 'EPH.1.21', 'far above all rule and authority, power and dominion, and every name that is named, not only in the present age but also in the one to come.'),
('EPH', 1, 22, 'EPH.1.22', 'And God put everything under His feet and made Him head over everything for the church,'),
('EPH', 1, 23, 'EPH.1.23', 'which is His body, the fullness of Him who fills all in all.'),
('EPH', 2, 1, 'EPH.2.1', 'And you were dead in your trespasses and sins,'),
('EPH', 2, 2, 'EPH.2.2', 'in which you used to walk when you conformed to the ways of this world and of the ruler of the power of the air, the spirit who is now at work in the sons of disobedience.'),
('EPH', 2, 3, 'EPH.2.3', 'All of us also lived among them at one time, fulfilling the cravings of our flesh and indulging its desires and thoughts. Like the rest, we were by nature children of wrath.'),
('EPH', 2, 4, 'EPH.2.4', 'But because of His great love for us, God, who is rich in mercy,'),
('EPH', 2, 5, 'EPH.2.5', 'made us alive with Christ even when we were dead in our trespasses. It is by grace you have been saved!'),
('EPH', 2, 6, 'EPH.2.6', 'And God raised us up with Christ and seated us with Him in the heavenly realms in Christ Jesus,'),
('EPH', 2, 7, 'EPH.2.7', 'in order that in the coming ages He might display the surpassing riches of His grace, demonstrated by His kindness to us in Christ Jesus.'),
('EPH', 2, 8, 'EPH.2.8', 'For it is by grace you have been saved through faith, and this not from yourselves; it is the gift of God,'),
('EPH', 2, 9, 'EPH.2.9', 'not by works, so that no one can boast.'),
('EPH', 2, 10, 'EPH.2.10', 'For we are God’s workmanship, created in Christ Jesus to do good works, which God prepared in advance as our way of life.'),
('EPH', 2, 11, 'EPH.2.11', 'Therefore remember that formerly you who are Gentiles in the flesh and called uncircumcised by the so-called circumcision (that done in the body by human hands)—'),
('EPH', 2, 12, 'EPH.2.12', 'remember that at that time you were separate from Christ, alienated from the commonwealth of Israel, and strangers to the covenants of the promise, without hope and without God in the world.'),
('EPH', 2, 13, 'EPH.2.13', 'But now in Christ Jesus you who once were far away have been brought near through the blood of Christ.'),
('EPH', 2, 14, 'EPH.2.14', 'For He Himself is our peace, who has made the two one and has torn down the dividing wall of hostility'),
('EPH', 2, 15, 'EPH.2.15', 'by abolishing in His flesh the law of commandments and decrees. He did this to create in Himself one new man out of the two, thus making peace'),
('EPH', 2, 16, 'EPH.2.16', 'and reconciling both of them to God in one body through the cross, by which He put to death their hostility.'),
('EPH', 2, 17, 'EPH.2.17', 'He came and preached peace to you who were far away and peace to those who were near.'),
('EPH', 2, 18, 'EPH.2.18', 'For through Him we both have access to the Father by one Spirit.'),
('EPH', 2, 19, 'EPH.2.19', 'Therefore you are no longer strangers and foreigners, but fellow citizens with the saints and members of God’s household,'),
('EPH', 2, 20, 'EPH.2.20', 'built on the foundation of the apostles and prophets, with Christ Jesus Himself as the cornerstone.'),
('EPH', 2, 21, 'EPH.2.21', 'In Him the whole building is fitted together and grows into a holy temple in the Lord.'),
('EPH', 2, 22, 'EPH.2.22', 'And in Him you too are being built together into a dwelling place for God in His Spirit.'),
('EPH', 3, 1, 'EPH.3.1', 'For this reason I, Paul, the prisoner of Christ Jesus for the sake of you Gentiles...'),
('EPH', 3, 2, 'EPH.3.2', 'Surely you have heard about the stewardship of God’s grace that was given to me for you,'),
('EPH', 3, 3, 'EPH.3.3', 'that is, the mystery made known to me by revelation, as I have already written briefly.'),
('EPH', 3, 4, 'EPH.3.4', 'In reading this, then, you will be able to understand my insight into the mystery of Christ,'),
('EPH', 3, 5, 'EPH.3.5', 'which was not made known to men in other generations as it has now been revealed by the Spirit to God’s holy apostles and prophets.'),
('EPH', 3, 6, 'EPH.3.6', 'This mystery is that through the gospel the Gentiles are fellow heirs, fellow members of the body, and fellow partakers of the promise in Christ Jesus.'),
('EPH', 3, 7, 'EPH.3.7', 'I became a servant of this gospel by the gift of God’s grace, given me through the working of His power.'),
('EPH', 3, 8, 'EPH.3.8', 'Though I am less than the least of all the saints, this grace was given me: to preach to the Gentiles the unsearchable riches of Christ,'),
('EPH', 3, 9, 'EPH.3.9', 'and to illuminate for everyone the stewardship of this mystery, which for ages past was kept hidden in God, who created all things.'),
('EPH', 3, 10, 'EPH.3.10', 'His purpose was that now, through the church, the manifold wisdom of God should be made known to the rulers and authorities in the heavenly realms,'),
('EPH', 3, 11, 'EPH.3.11', 'according to the eternal purpose that He accomplished in Christ Jesus our Lord.'),
('EPH', 3, 12, 'EPH.3.12', 'In Him and through faith in Him we may enter God’s presence with boldness and confidence.'),
('EPH', 3, 13, 'EPH.3.13', 'So I ask you not to be discouraged because of my sufferings for you, which are your glory.'),
('EPH', 3, 14, 'EPH.3.14', '... for this reason I bow my knees before the Father,'),
('EPH', 3, 15, 'EPH.3.15', 'from whom every family in heaven and on earth derives its name.'),
('EPH', 3, 16, 'EPH.3.16', 'I ask that out of the riches of His glory He may strengthen you with power through His Spirit in your inner being,'),
('EPH', 3, 17, 'EPH.3.17', 'so that Christ may dwell in your hearts through faith. Then you, being rooted and grounded in love,'),
('EPH', 3, 18, 'EPH.3.18', 'will have power, together with all the saints, to comprehend the length and width and height and depth'),
('EPH', 3, 19, 'EPH.3.19', 'of the love of Christ, and to know this love that surpasses knowledge, that you may be filled with all the fullness of God.'),
('EPH', 3, 20, 'EPH.3.20', 'Now to Him who is able to do immeasurably more than all we ask or imagine, according to His power that is at work within us,'),
('EPH', 3, 21, 'EPH.3.21', 'to Him be the glory in the church and in Christ Jesus throughout all generations, forever and ever. Amen.'),
('EPH', 4, 1, 'EPH.4.1', 'As a prisoner in the Lord, then, I urge you to walk in a manner worthy of the calling you have received:'),
('EPH', 4, 2, 'EPH.4.2', 'with all humility and gentleness, with patience, bearing with one another in love,'),
('EPH', 4, 3, 'EPH.4.3', 'and with diligence to preserve the unity of the Spirit through the bond of peace.'),
('EPH', 4, 4, 'EPH.4.4', 'There is one body and one Spirit, just as you were called to one hope when you were called;'),
('EPH', 4, 5, 'EPH.4.5', 'one Lord, one faith, one baptism;'),
('EPH', 4, 6, 'EPH.4.6', 'one God and Father of all, who is over all and through all and in all.'),
('EPH', 4, 7, 'EPH.4.7', 'Now to each one of us grace has been given according to the measure of the gift of Christ.'),
('EPH', 4, 8, 'EPH.4.8', 'This is why it says: “When He ascended on high, He led captives away, and gave gifts to men.”'),
('EPH', 4, 9, 'EPH.4.9', 'What does “He ascended” mean, except that He also descended to the lower parts of the earth?'),
('EPH', 4, 10, 'EPH.4.10', 'He who descended is the very One who ascended above all the heavens, in order to fill all things.'),
('EPH', 4, 11, 'EPH.4.11', 'And it was He who gave some to be apostles, some to be prophets, some to be evangelists, and some to be pastors and teachers,'),
('EPH', 4, 12, 'EPH.4.12', 'to equip the saints for works of ministry and to build up the body of Christ,'),
('EPH', 4, 13, 'EPH.4.13', 'until we all reach unity in the faith and in the knowledge of the Son of God, as we mature to the full measure of the stature of Christ.'),
('EPH', 4, 14, 'EPH.4.14', 'Then we will no longer be infants, tossed about by the waves and carried around by every wind of teaching and by the clever cunning of men in their deceitful scheming.'),
('EPH', 4, 15, 'EPH.4.15', 'Instead, speaking the truth in love, we will in all things grow up into Christ Himself, who is the head.'),
('EPH', 4, 16, 'EPH.4.16', 'From Him the whole body, fitted and held together by every supporting ligament, grows and builds itself up in love through the work of each individual part.'),
('EPH', 4, 17, 'EPH.4.17', 'So I tell you this, and insist on it in the Lord, that you must no longer walk as the Gentiles do, in the futility of their thinking.'),
('EPH', 4, 18, 'EPH.4.18', 'They are darkened in their understanding and alienated from the life of God because of the ignorance that is in them due to the hardness of their hearts.'),
('EPH', 4, 19, 'EPH.4.19', 'Having lost all sense of shame, they have given themselves over to sensuality for the practice of every kind of impurity, with a craving for more.'),
('EPH', 4, 20, 'EPH.4.20', 'But this is not the way you came to know Christ.'),
('EPH', 4, 21, 'EPH.4.21', 'Surely you heard of Him and were taught in Him—in keeping with the truth that is in Jesus—'),
('EPH', 4, 22, 'EPH.4.22', 'to put off your former way of life, your old self, which is being corrupted by its deceitful desires;'),
('EPH', 4, 23, 'EPH.4.23', 'to be renewed in the spirit of your minds;'),
('EPH', 4, 24, 'EPH.4.24', 'and to put on the new self, created to be like God in true righteousness and holiness.'),
('EPH', 4, 25, 'EPH.4.25', 'Therefore each of you must put off falsehood and speak truthfully to his neighbor, for we are all members of one another.'),
('EPH', 4, 26, 'EPH.4.26', '“Be angry, yet do not sin.” Do not let the sun set upon your anger,'),
('EPH', 4, 27, 'EPH.4.27', 'and do not give the devil a foothold.'),
('EPH', 4, 28, 'EPH.4.28', 'He who has been stealing must steal no longer, but must work, doing good with his own hands, that he may have something to share with the one in need.'),
('EPH', 4, 29, 'EPH.4.29', 'Let no unwholesome talk come out of your mouths, but only what is helpful for building up the one in need and bringing grace to those who listen.'),
('EPH', 4, 30, 'EPH.4.30', 'And do not grieve the Holy Spirit of God, in whom you were sealed for the day of redemption.'),
('EPH', 4, 31, 'EPH.4.31', 'Get rid of all bitterness, rage and anger, outcry and slander, along with every form of malice.'),
('EPH', 4, 32, 'EPH.4.32', 'Be kind and tenderhearted to one another, forgiving each other just as in Christ God forgave you.'),
('EPH', 5, 1, 'EPH.5.1', 'Be imitators of God, therefore, as beloved children,'),
('EPH', 5, 2, 'EPH.5.2', 'and walk in love, just as Christ loved us and gave Himself up for us as a fragrant sacrificial offering to God.'),
('EPH', 5, 3, 'EPH.5.3', 'But among you, as is proper among the saints, there must not be even a hint of sexual immorality, or of any kind of impurity, or of greed.'),
('EPH', 5, 4, 'EPH.5.4', 'Nor should there be obscenity, foolish talk, or crude joking, which are out of character, but rather thanksgiving.'),
('EPH', 5, 5, 'EPH.5.5', 'For of this you can be sure: No immoral, impure, or greedy person (that is, an idolater) has any inheritance in the kingdom of Christ and of God.'),
('EPH', 5, 6, 'EPH.5.6', 'Let no one deceive you with empty words, for because of such things the wrath of God is coming on the sons of disobedience.'),
('EPH', 5, 7, 'EPH.5.7', 'Therefore do not be partakers with them.'),
('EPH', 5, 8, 'EPH.5.8', 'For you were once darkness, but now you are light in the Lord. Walk as children of light,'),
('EPH', 5, 9, 'EPH.5.9', 'for the fruit of the light consists in all goodness, righteousness, and truth.'),
('EPH', 5, 10, 'EPH.5.10', 'Test and prove what pleases the Lord.'),
('EPH', 5, 11, 'EPH.5.11', 'Have no fellowship with the fruitless deeds of darkness, but rather expose them.'),
('EPH', 5, 12, 'EPH.5.12', 'For it is shameful even to mention what the disobedient do in secret.'),
('EPH', 5, 13, 'EPH.5.13', 'But everything exposed by the light becomes visible, for everything that is illuminated becomes a light itself.'),
('EPH', 5, 14, 'EPH.5.14', 'So it is said: “Wake up, O sleeper, rise up from the dead, and Christ will shine on you.”'),
('EPH', 5, 15, 'EPH.5.15', 'Pay careful attention, then, to how you walk, not as unwise but as wise,'),
('EPH', 5, 16, 'EPH.5.16', 'redeeming the time, because the days are evil.'),
('EPH', 5, 17, 'EPH.5.17', 'Therefore do not be foolish, but understand what the Lord’s will is.'),
('EPH', 5, 18, 'EPH.5.18', 'Do not get drunk on wine, which leads to reckless indiscretion. Instead, be filled with the Spirit.'),
('EPH', 5, 19, 'EPH.5.19', 'Speak to one another with psalms, hymns, and spiritual songs. Sing and make music in your hearts to the Lord,'),
('EPH', 5, 20, 'EPH.5.20', 'always giving thanks to God the Father for everything in the name of our Lord Jesus Christ.'),
('EPH', 5, 21, 'EPH.5.21', 'Submit to one another out of reverence for Christ.'),
('EPH', 5, 22, 'EPH.5.22', 'Wives, submit to your husbands as to the Lord.'),
('EPH', 5, 23, 'EPH.5.23', 'For the husband is the head of the wife as Christ is the head of the church, His body, of which He is the Savior.'),
('EPH', 5, 24, 'EPH.5.24', 'Now as the church submits to Christ, so also wives should submit to their husbands in everything.'),
('EPH', 5, 25, 'EPH.5.25', 'Husbands, love your wives, just as Christ loved the church and gave Himself up for her'),
('EPH', 5, 26, 'EPH.5.26', 'to sanctify her, cleansing her by the washing with water through the word,'),
('EPH', 5, 27, 'EPH.5.27', 'and to present her to Himself as a glorious church, without stain or wrinkle or any such blemish, but holy and blameless.'),
('EPH', 5, 28, 'EPH.5.28', 'In the same way, husbands ought to love their wives as their own bodies. He who loves his wife loves himself.'),
('EPH', 5, 29, 'EPH.5.29', 'Indeed, no one ever hated his own body, but he nourishes and cherishes it, just as Christ does the church.'),
('EPH', 5, 30, 'EPH.5.30', 'For we are members of His body.'),
('EPH', 5, 31, 'EPH.5.31', '“For this reason a man will leave his father and mother and be united to his wife, and the two will become one flesh.”'),
('EPH', 5, 32, 'EPH.5.32', 'This mystery is profound, but I am speaking about Christ and the church.'),
('EPH', 5, 33, 'EPH.5.33', 'Nevertheless, each one of you also must love his wife as he loves himself, and the wife must respect her husband.'),
('EPH', 6, 1, 'EPH.6.1', 'Children, obey your parents in the Lord, for this is right.'),
('EPH', 6, 2, 'EPH.6.2', '“Honor your father and mother” (which is the first commandment with a promise),'),
('EPH', 6, 3, 'EPH.6.3', '“that it may go well with you and that you may have a long life on the earth.”'),
('EPH', 6, 4, 'EPH.6.4', 'Fathers, do not provoke your children to wrath; instead, bring them up in the discipline and instruction of the Lord.'),
('EPH', 6, 5, 'EPH.6.5', 'Slaves, obey your earthly masters with respect and fear and sincerity of heart, just as you would obey Christ.'),
('EPH', 6, 6, 'EPH.6.6', 'And do this not only to please them while they are watching, but as servants of Christ, doing the will of God from your heart.'),
('EPH', 6, 7, 'EPH.6.7', 'Serve with good will, as to the Lord and not to men,'),
('EPH', 6, 8, 'EPH.6.8', 'because you know that the Lord will reward each one for whatever good he does, whether he is slave or free.'),
('EPH', 6, 9, 'EPH.6.9', 'And masters, do the same for your slaves. Give up your use of threats, because you know that He who is both their Master and yours is in heaven, and there is no favoritism with Him.'),
('EPH', 6, 10, 'EPH.6.10', 'Finally, be strong in the Lord and in His mighty power.'),
('EPH', 6, 11, 'EPH.6.11', 'Put on the full armor of God, so that you can make your stand against the devil’s schemes.'),
('EPH', 6, 12, 'EPH.6.12', 'For our struggle is not against flesh and blood, but against the rulers, against the authorities, against the powers of this world’s darkness, and against the spiritual forces of evil in the heavenly realms.'),
('EPH', 6, 13, 'EPH.6.13', 'Therefore take up the full armor of God, so that when the day of evil comes, you will be able to stand your ground, and having done everything, to stand.'),
('EPH', 6, 14, 'EPH.6.14', 'Stand firm then, with the belt of truth buckled around your waist, with the breastplate of righteousness arrayed,'),
('EPH', 6, 15, 'EPH.6.15', 'and with your feet fitted with the readiness of the gospel of peace.'),
('EPH', 6, 16, 'EPH.6.16', 'In addition to all this, take up the shield of faith, with which you can extinguish all the flaming arrows of the evil one.'),
('EPH', 6, 17, 'EPH.6.17', 'And take the helmet of salvation and the sword of the Spirit, which is the word of God.'),
('EPH', 6, 18, 'EPH.6.18', 'Pray in the Spirit at all times, with every kind of prayer and petition. To this end, stay alert with all perseverance in your prayers for all the saints.'),
('EPH', 6, 19, 'EPH.6.19', 'Pray also for me, that whenever I open my mouth, words may be given me so that I will boldly make known the mystery of the gospel,'),
('EPH', 6, 20, 'EPH.6.20', 'for which I am an ambassador in chains. Pray that I may proclaim it fearlessly, as I should.'),
('EPH', 6, 21, 'EPH.6.21', 'Tychicus, the beloved brother and faithful servant in the Lord, will tell you everything, so that you also may know about me and what I am doing.'),
('EPH', 6, 22, 'EPH.6.22', 'I have sent him to you for this very purpose, that you may know about us, and that he may encourage your hearts.'),
('EPH', 6, 23, 'EPH.6.23', 'Peace to the brothers and love with faith from God the Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.'),
('EPH', 6, 24, 'EPH.6.24', 'Grace to all who love our Lord Jesus Christ with an undying love.'),
('PHP', 1, 1, 'PHP.1.1', 'Paul and Timothy, servants of Christ Jesus, To all the saints in Christ Jesus at Philippi, together with the overseers and deacons:'),
('PHP', 1, 2, 'PHP.1.2', 'Grace and peace to you from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.'),
('PHP', 1, 3, 'PHP.1.3', 'I thank my God every time I remember you.'),
('PHP', 1, 4, 'PHP.1.4', 'In every prayer for all of you, I always pray with joy,'),
('PHP', 1, 5, 'PHP.1.5', 'because of your partnership in the gospel from the first day until now,'),
('PHP', 1, 6, 'PHP.1.6', 'being confident of this, that He who began a good work in you will carry it on to completion until the day of Christ Jesus.'),
('PHP', 1, 7, 'PHP.1.7', 'It is right for me to feel this way about all of you, since I have you in my heart. For in my chains and in my defense and confirmation of the gospel, you are all partners in grace with me.'),
('PHP', 1, 8, 'PHP.1.8', 'God is my witness how I long for all of you with the affection of Christ Jesus.'),
('PHP', 1, 9, 'PHP.1.9', 'And this is my prayer: that your love may abound more and more in knowledge and depth of insight,'),
('PHP', 1, 10, 'PHP.1.10', 'so that you may be able to test and prove what is best and may be pure and blameless for the day of Christ,'),
('PHP', 1, 11, 'PHP.1.11', 'filled with the fruit of righteousness that comes through Jesus Christ, to the glory and praise of God.'),
('PHP', 1, 12, 'PHP.1.12', 'Now I want you to know, brothers, that my circumstances have actually served to advance the gospel.'),
('PHP', 1, 13, 'PHP.1.13', 'As a result, it has become clear throughout the whole palace guard and to everyone else that I am in chains for Christ.'),
('PHP', 1, 14, 'PHP.1.14', 'And most of the brothers, confident in the Lord by my chains, now dare more greatly to speak the word without fear.'),
('PHP', 1, 15, 'PHP.1.15', 'It is true that some preach Christ out of envy and rivalry, but others out of goodwill.'),
('PHP', 1, 16, 'PHP.1.16', 'The latter do so in love, knowing that I am appointed for the defense of the gospel.'),
('PHP', 1, 17, 'PHP.1.17', 'The former, however, preach Christ out of selfish ambition, not sincerely, supposing that they can add to the distress of my chains.'),
('PHP', 1, 18, 'PHP.1.18', 'What then is the issue? Just this: that in every way, whether by false motives or true, Christ is preached. And in this I rejoice. Yes, and I will continue to rejoice,'),
('PHP', 1, 19, 'PHP.1.19', 'because I know that through your prayers and the provision of the Spirit of Jesus Christ, my distress will turn out for my deliverance.'),
('PHP', 1, 20, 'PHP.1.20', 'I eagerly expect and hope that I will in no way be ashamed, but will have complete boldness so that now as always Christ will be exalted in my body, whether by life or by death.'),
('PHP', 1, 21, 'PHP.1.21', 'For to me, to live is Christ, and to die is gain.'),
('PHP', 1, 22, 'PHP.1.22', 'But if I go on living in the body, this will mean fruitful labor for me. So what shall I choose? I do not know.'),
('PHP', 1, 23, 'PHP.1.23', 'I am torn between the two. I desire to depart and be with Christ, which is far better indeed.'),
('PHP', 1, 24, 'PHP.1.24', 'But it is more necessary for you that I remain in the body.'),
('PHP', 1, 25, 'PHP.1.25', 'Convinced of this, I know that I will remain and will continue with all of you for your progress and joy in the faith,'),
('PHP', 1, 26, 'PHP.1.26', 'so that through my coming to you again your exultation in Christ Jesus will resound on account of me.'),
('PHP', 1, 27, 'PHP.1.27', 'Nevertheless, conduct yourselves in a manner worthy of the gospel of Christ. Then, whether I come and see you or only hear about you in my absence, I will know that you stand firm in one spirit, contending together as one for the faith of the gospel,'),
('PHP', 1, 28, 'PHP.1.28', 'without being frightened in any way by those who oppose you. This is a clear sign of their destruction but of your salvation, and it is from God.'),
('PHP', 1, 29, 'PHP.1.29', 'For it has been granted to you on behalf of Christ not only to believe in Him, but also to suffer for Him,'),
('PHP', 1, 30, 'PHP.1.30', 'since you are encountering the same struggle you saw I had, and now hear that I still have.'),
('PHP', 2, 1, 'PHP.2.1', 'Therefore if you have any encouragement in Christ, if any comfort from His love, if any fellowship with the Spirit, if any affection and compassion,'),
('PHP', 2, 2, 'PHP.2.2', 'then make my joy complete by being like-minded, having the same love, being united in spirit and purpose.'),
('PHP', 2, 3, 'PHP.2.3', 'Do nothing out of selfish ambition or empty pride, but in humility consider others more important than yourselves.'),
('PHP', 2, 4, 'PHP.2.4', 'Each of you should look not only to your own interests, but also to the interests of others.'),
('PHP', 2, 5, 'PHP.2.5', 'Let this mind be in you which was also in Christ Jesus:'),
('PHP', 2, 6, 'PHP.2.6', 'Who, existing in the form of God, did not consider equality with God something to be grasped,'),
('PHP', 2, 7, 'PHP.2.7', 'but emptied Himself, taking the form of a servant, being made in human likeness.'),
('PHP', 2, 8, 'PHP.2.8', 'And being found in appearance as a man, He humbled Himself and became obedient to death—even death on a cross.'),
('PHP', 2, 9, 'PHP.2.9', 'Therefore God exalted Him to the highest place and gave Him the name above all names,'),
('PHP', 2, 10, 'PHP.2.10', 'that at the name of Jesus every knee should bow, in heaven and on earth and under the earth,'),
('PHP', 2, 11, 'PHP.2.11', 'and every tongue confess that Jesus Christ is Lord, to the glory of God the Father.'),
('PHP', 2, 12, 'PHP.2.12', 'Therefore, my beloved, just as you have always obeyed, not only in my presence, but now even more in my absence, continue to work out your salvation with fear and trembling.'),
('PHP', 2, 13, 'PHP.2.13', 'For it is God who works in you to will and to act on behalf of His good purpose.'),
('PHP', 2, 14, 'PHP.2.14', 'Do everything without complaining or arguing,'),
('PHP', 2, 15, 'PHP.2.15', 'so that you may be blameless and pure, children of God without fault in a crooked and perverse generation, in which you shine as lights in the world'),
('PHP', 2, 16, 'PHP.2.16', 'as you hold forth the word of life, in order that I may boast on the day of Christ that I did not run or labor in vain.'),
('PHP', 2, 17, 'PHP.2.17', 'But even if I am being poured out like a drink offering on the sacrifice and service of your faith, I am glad and rejoice with all of you.'),
('PHP', 2, 18, 'PHP.2.18', 'So you too should be glad and rejoice with me.'),
('PHP', 2, 19, 'PHP.2.19', 'Now I hope in the Lord Jesus to send Timothy to you soon, that I also may be cheered when I learn how you are doing.'),
('PHP', 2, 20, 'PHP.2.20', 'I have nobody else like him who will genuinely care for your needs.'),
('PHP', 2, 21, 'PHP.2.21', 'For all the others look after their own interests, not those of Jesus Christ.'),
('PHP', 2, 22, 'PHP.2.22', 'But you know Timothy’s proven worth, that as a child with his father he has served with me to advance the gospel.'),
('PHP', 2, 23, 'PHP.2.23', 'So I hope to send him as soon as I see what happens with me.'),
('PHP', 2, 24, 'PHP.2.24', 'And I trust in the Lord that I myself will come soon.'),
('PHP', 2, 25, 'PHP.2.25', 'But I thought it necessary to send back to you Epaphroditus, my brother, fellow worker, and fellow soldier, who is also your messenger and minister to my needs.'),
('PHP', 2, 26, 'PHP.2.26', 'For he has been longing for all of you and is distressed because you heard he was ill.'),
('PHP', 2, 27, 'PHP.2.27', 'He was sick indeed, nearly unto death. But God had mercy on him, and not only on him but also on me, to spare me sorrow upon sorrow.'),
('PHP', 2, 28, 'PHP.2.28', 'Therefore I am all the more eager to send him, so that when you see him again you may rejoice, and I may be less anxious.'),
('PHP', 2, 29, 'PHP.2.29', 'Welcome him in the Lord with great joy, and honor men like him,'),
('PHP', 2, 30, 'PHP.2.30', 'because he nearly died for the work of Christ, risking his life to make up for your deficit of service to me.'),
('PHP', 3, 1, 'PHP.3.1', 'Finally, my brothers, rejoice in the Lord. It is no trouble for me to write the same things to you again, and it is a safeguard for you.'),
('PHP', 3, 2, 'PHP.3.2', 'Watch out for those dogs, those workers of evil, those mutilators of the flesh!'),
('PHP', 3, 3, 'PHP.3.3', 'For it is we who are the circumcision, we who worship by the Spirit of God, who glory in Christ Jesus, and who put no confidence in the flesh—'),
('PHP', 3, 4, 'PHP.3.4', 'though I myself could have such confidence. If anyone else thinks he has grounds for confidence in the flesh, I have more:'),
('PHP', 3, 5, 'PHP.3.5', 'circumcised on the eighth day, of the people of Israel, of the tribe of Benjamin; a Hebrew of Hebrews; as to the law, a Pharisee;'),
('PHP', 3, 6, 'PHP.3.6', 'as to zeal, persecuting the church; as to righteousness in the law, faultless.'),
('PHP', 3, 7, 'PHP.3.7', 'But whatever was gain to me I count as loss for the sake of Christ.'),
('PHP', 3, 8, 'PHP.3.8', 'More than that, I count all things as loss compared to the surpassing excellence of knowing Christ Jesus my Lord, for whom I have lost all things. I consider them rubbish, that I may gain Christ'),
('PHP', 3, 9, 'PHP.3.9', 'and be found in Him, not having my own righteousness from the law, but that which is through faith in Christ, the righteousness from God on the basis of faith.'),
('PHP', 3, 10, 'PHP.3.10', 'I want to know Christ and the power of His resurrection and the fellowship of His sufferings, being conformed to Him in His death,'),
('PHP', 3, 11, 'PHP.3.11', 'and so, somehow, to attain to the resurrection from the dead.'),
('PHP', 3, 12, 'PHP.3.12', 'Not that I have already obtained all this, or have already been made perfect, but I press on to take hold of that for which Christ Jesus took hold of me.'),
('PHP', 3, 13, 'PHP.3.13', 'Brothers, I do not consider myself yet to have taken hold of it. But one thing I do: Forgetting what is behind and straining toward what is ahead,'),
('PHP', 3, 14, 'PHP.3.14', 'I press on toward the goal to win the prize of God’s heavenly calling in Christ Jesus.'),
('PHP', 3, 15, 'PHP.3.15', 'All of us who are mature should embrace this point of view. And if you think differently about some issue, God will reveal this to you as well.'),
('PHP', 3, 16, 'PHP.3.16', 'Nevertheless, we must live up to what we have already attained.'),
('PHP', 3, 17, 'PHP.3.17', 'Join one another in following my example, brothers, and carefully observe those who walk according to the pattern we set for you.'),
('PHP', 3, 18, 'PHP.3.18', 'For as I have often told you before, and now say again even with tears: Many live as enemies of the cross of Christ.'),
('PHP', 3, 19, 'PHP.3.19', 'Their end is destruction, their god is their belly, and their glory is in their shame. Their minds are set on earthly things.'),
('PHP', 3, 20, 'PHP.3.20', 'But our citizenship is in heaven, and we eagerly await a Savior from there, the Lord Jesus Christ,'),
('PHP', 3, 21, 'PHP.3.21', 'who, by the power that enables Him to subject all things to Himself, will transform our lowly bodies to be like His glorious body.'),
('PHP', 4, 1, 'PHP.4.1', 'Therefore, my brothers, whom I love and long for, my joy and crown, that is how you must stand firm in the Lord, my beloved.'),
('PHP', 4, 2, 'PHP.4.2', 'I urge Euodia and Syntyche to agree with each other in the Lord.'),
('PHP', 4, 3, 'PHP.4.3', 'Yes, and I ask you, my true yokefellow, to help these women who have contended at my side for the gospel, along with Clement and the rest of my fellow workers, whose names are in the Book of Life.'),
('PHP', 4, 4, 'PHP.4.4', 'Rejoice in the Lord always. I will say it again: Rejoice!'),
('PHP', 4, 5, 'PHP.4.5', 'Let your gentleness be apparent to all. The Lord is near.'),
('PHP', 4, 6, 'PHP.4.6', 'Be anxious for nothing, but in everything, by prayer and petition, with thanksgiving, present your requests to God.'),
('PHP', 4, 7, 'PHP.4.7', 'And the peace of God, which surpasses all understanding, will guard your hearts and your minds in Christ Jesus.'),
('PHP', 4, 8, 'PHP.4.8', 'Finally, brothers, whatever is true, whatever is honorable, whatever is right, whatever is pure, whatever is lovely, whatever is admirable—if anything is excellent or praiseworthy—think on these things.'),
('PHP', 4, 9, 'PHP.4.9', 'Whatever you have learned or received or heard from me, or seen in me, put it into practice. And the God of peace will be with you.'),
('PHP', 4, 10, 'PHP.4.10', 'Now I rejoice greatly in the Lord that at last you have revived your concern for me. You were indeed concerned, but you had no opportunity to show it.'),
('PHP', 4, 11, 'PHP.4.11', 'I am not saying this out of need, for I have learned to be content regardless of my circumstances.'),
('PHP', 4, 12, 'PHP.4.12', 'I know how to live humbly, and I know how to abound. In any and every situation I have learned the secret of being filled and being hungry, of having plenty and having need.'),
('PHP', 4, 13, 'PHP.4.13', 'I can do all things through Christ who gives me strength.'),
('PHP', 4, 14, 'PHP.4.14', 'Nevertheless, you have done well to share in my affliction.'),
('PHP', 4, 15, 'PHP.4.15', 'And as you Philippians know, in the early days of the gospel, when I left Macedonia, no church but you partnered with me in the matter of giving and receiving.'),
('PHP', 4, 16, 'PHP.4.16', 'For even while I was in Thessalonica, you provided for my needs again and again.'),
('PHP', 4, 17, 'PHP.4.17', 'Not that I am seeking a gift, but I am looking for the fruit that may be credited to your account.'),
('PHP', 4, 18, 'PHP.4.18', 'I have all I need and more, now that I have received your gifts from Epaphroditus. They are a fragrant offering, an acceptable sacrifice, well-pleasing to God.'),
('PHP', 4, 19, 'PHP.4.19', 'And my God will supply all your needs according to His glorious riches in Christ Jesus.'),
('PHP', 4, 20, 'PHP.4.20', 'To our God and Father be glory forever and ever. Amen.'),
('PHP', 4, 21, 'PHP.4.21', 'Greet all the saints in Christ Jesus. The brothers who are with me send you greetings.'),
('PHP', 4, 22, 'PHP.4.22', 'All the saints send you greetings, especially those from the household of Caesar.'),
('PHP', 4, 23, 'PHP.4.23', 'The grace of the Lord Jesus Christ be with your spirit.'),
('COL', 1, 1, 'COL.1.1', 'Paul, an apostle of Christ Jesus by the will of God, and Timothy our brother,'),
('COL', 1, 2, 'COL.1.2', 'To the saints and faithful brothers in Christ at Colossae: Grace and peace to you from God our Father.'),
('COL', 1, 3, 'COL.1.3', 'We always thank God, the Father of our Lord Jesus Christ, when we pray for you,'),
('COL', 1, 4, 'COL.1.4', 'because we have heard about your faith in Christ Jesus and your love for all the saints—'),
('COL', 1, 5, 'COL.1.5', 'the faith and love proceeding from the hope stored up for you in heaven, of which you have already heard in the word of truth, the gospel'),
('COL', 1, 6, 'COL.1.6', 'that has come to you. All over the world this gospel is bearing fruit and growing, just as it has been doing among you since the day you heard it and truly understood the grace of God.'),
('COL', 1, 7, 'COL.1.7', 'You learned it from Epaphras, our beloved fellow servant, who is a faithful minister of Christ on our behalf,'),
('COL', 1, 8, 'COL.1.8', 'and who also informed us of your love in the Spirit.'),
('COL', 1, 9, 'COL.1.9', 'For this reason, since the day we heard about you, we have not stopped praying for you and asking God to fill you with the knowledge of His will in all spiritual wisdom and understanding,'),
('COL', 1, 10, 'COL.1.10', 'so that you may walk in a manner worthy of the Lord and may please Him in every way: bearing fruit in every good work, growing in the knowledge of God,'),
('COL', 1, 11, 'COL.1.11', 'being strengthened with all power according to His glorious might so that you may have full endurance and patience, and joyfully'),
('COL', 1, 12, 'COL.1.12', 'giving thanks to the Father, who has qualified you to share in the inheritance of the saints in the light.'),
('COL', 1, 13, 'COL.1.13', 'He has rescued us from the dominion of darkness and brought us into the kingdom of His beloved Son,'),
('COL', 1, 14, 'COL.1.14', 'in whom we have redemption, the forgiveness of sins.'),
('COL', 1, 15, 'COL.1.15', 'The Son is the image of the invisible God, the firstborn over all creation.'),
('COL', 1, 16, 'COL.1.16', 'For in Him all things were created, things in heaven and on earth, visible and invisible, whether thrones or dominions or rulers or authorities. All things were created through Him and for Him.'),
('COL', 1, 17, 'COL.1.17', 'He is before all things, and in Him all things hold together.'),
('COL', 1, 18, 'COL.1.18', 'And He is the head of the body, the church; He is the beginning and firstborn from among the dead, so that in all things He may have preeminence.'),
('COL', 1, 19, 'COL.1.19', 'For God was pleased to have all His fullness dwell in Him,'),
('COL', 1, 20, 'COL.1.20', 'and through Him to reconcile to Himself all things, whether things on earth or things in heaven, by making peace through the blood of His cross.'),
('COL', 1, 21, 'COL.1.21', 'Once you were alienated from God and were hostile in your minds, engaging in evil deeds.'),
('COL', 1, 22, 'COL.1.22', 'But now He has reconciled you by Christ’s physical body through death to present you holy, unblemished, and blameless in His presence—'),
('COL', 1, 23, 'COL.1.23', 'if indeed you continue in your faith, established and firm, not moved from the hope of the gospel you heard, which has been proclaimed to every creature under heaven, and of which I, Paul, have become a servant.'),
('COL', 1, 24, 'COL.1.24', 'Now I rejoice in my sufferings for you, and I fill up in my flesh what is lacking in regard to Christ’s afflictions for the sake of His body, which is the church.'),
('COL', 1, 25, 'COL.1.25', 'I became its servant by the commission God gave me to fully proclaim to you the word of God,'),
('COL', 1, 26, 'COL.1.26', 'the mystery that was hidden for ages and generations but is now revealed to His saints.'),
('COL', 1, 27, 'COL.1.27', 'To them God has chosen to make known among the Gentiles the glorious riches of this mystery, which is Christ in you, the hope of glory.'),
('COL', 1, 28, 'COL.1.28', 'We proclaim Him, admonishing and teaching everyone with all wisdom, so that we may present everyone perfect in Christ.'),
('COL', 1, 29, 'COL.1.29', 'To this end I also labor, striving with all His energy working powerfully within me.'),
('COL', 2, 1, 'COL.2.1', 'For I want you to know how much I am struggling for you and for those at Laodicea, and for all who have not met me face to face,'),
('COL', 2, 2, 'COL.2.2', 'that they may be encouraged in heart, knit together in love, and filled with the full riches of complete understanding, so that they may know the mystery of God, namely Christ,'),
('COL', 2, 3, 'COL.2.3', 'in whom are hidden all the treasures of wisdom and knowledge.'),
('COL', 2, 4, 'COL.2.4', 'I say this so that no one will deceive you by smooth rhetoric.'),
('COL', 2, 5, 'COL.2.5', 'For although I am absent from you in body, I am present with you in spirit, and I delight to see your orderly condition and firm faith in Christ.'),
('COL', 2, 6, 'COL.2.6', 'Therefore, just as you have received Christ Jesus as Lord, continue to walk in Him,'),
('COL', 2, 7, 'COL.2.7', 'rooted and built up in Him, established in the faith as you were taught, and overflowing with thankfulness.'),
('COL', 2, 8, 'COL.2.8', 'See to it that no one takes you captive through philosophy and empty deception, which are based on human tradition and the spiritual forces of the world rather than on Christ.'),
('COL', 2, 9, 'COL.2.9', 'For in Christ all the fullness of the Deity dwells in bodily form.'),
('COL', 2, 10, 'COL.2.10', 'And you have been made complete in Christ, who is the head over every ruler and authority.'),
('COL', 2, 11, 'COL.2.11', 'In Him you were also circumcised, in the putting off of your sinful nature, with the circumcision performed by Christ and not by human hands.'),
('COL', 2, 12, 'COL.2.12', 'And having been buried with Him in baptism, you were raised with Him through your faith in the power of God, who raised Him from the dead.'),
('COL', 2, 13, 'COL.2.13', 'When you were dead in your trespasses and in the uncircumcision of your sinful nature, God made you alive with Christ. He forgave us all our trespasses,'),
('COL', 2, 14, 'COL.2.14', 'having canceled the debt ascribed to us in the decrees that stood against us. He took it away, nailing it to the cross!'),
('COL', 2, 15, 'COL.2.15', 'And having disarmed the powers and authorities, He made a public spectacle of them, triumphing over them by the cross.'),
('COL', 2, 16, 'COL.2.16', 'Therefore let no one judge you by what you eat or drink, or with regard to a feast, a New Moon, or a Sabbath.'),
('COL', 2, 17, 'COL.2.17', 'These are a shadow of the things to come, but the body that casts it belongs to Christ.'),
('COL', 2, 18, 'COL.2.18', 'Do not let anyone who delights in false humility and the worship of angels disqualify you with speculation about what he has seen. Such a person is puffed up without basis by his unspiritual mind.'),
('COL', 2, 19, 'COL.2.19', 'He has lost connection to the head, from whom the whole body, supported and knit together by its joints and ligaments, grows as God causes it to grow.'),
('COL', 2, 20, 'COL.2.20', 'If you have died with Christ to the spiritual forces of the world, why, as though you still belonged to the world, do you submit to its regulations:'),
('COL', 2, 21, 'COL.2.21', '“Do not handle, do not taste, do not touch!”?'),
('COL', 2, 22, 'COL.2.22', 'These will all perish with use, because they are based on human commands and teachings.'),
('COL', 2, 23, 'COL.2.23', 'Such restrictions indeed have an appearance of wisdom, with their self-prescribed worship, their false humility, and their harsh treatment of the body; but they are of no value against the indulgence of the flesh.'),
('COL', 3, 1, 'COL.3.1', 'Therefore, since you have been raised with Christ, strive for the things above, where Christ is seated at the right hand of God.'),
('COL', 3, 2, 'COL.3.2', 'Set your minds on things above, not on earthly things.'),
('COL', 3, 3, 'COL.3.3', 'For you died, and your life is now hidden with Christ in God.'),
('COL', 3, 4, 'COL.3.4', 'When Christ, who is your life, appears, then you also will appear with Him in glory.'),
('COL', 3, 5, 'COL.3.5', 'Put to death, therefore, the components of your earthly nature: sexual immorality, impurity, lust, evil desires, and greed, which is idolatry.'),
('COL', 3, 6, 'COL.3.6', 'Because of these, the wrath of God is coming on the sons of disobedience.'),
('COL', 3, 7, 'COL.3.7', 'When you lived among them, you also used to walk in these ways.'),
('COL', 3, 8, 'COL.3.8', 'But now you must put aside all such things as these: anger, rage, malice, slander, and filthy language from your lips.'),
('COL', 3, 9, 'COL.3.9', 'Do not lie to one another, since you have taken off the old self with its practices,'),
('COL', 3, 10, 'COL.3.10', 'and have put on the new self, which is being renewed in knowledge in the image of its Creator.'),
('COL', 3, 11, 'COL.3.11', 'Here there is no Greek or Jew, circumcised or uncircumcised, barbarian, Scythian, slave, or free, but Christ is all and is in all.'),
('COL', 3, 12, 'COL.3.12', 'Therefore, as the elect of God, holy and beloved, clothe yourselves with hearts of compassion, kindness, humility, gentleness, and patience.'),
('COL', 3, 13, 'COL.3.13', 'Bear with one another and forgive any complaint you may have against someone else. Forgive as the Lord forgave you.'),
('COL', 3, 14, 'COL.3.14', 'And over all these virtues put on love, which is the bond of perfect unity.'),
('COL', 3, 15, 'COL.3.15', 'Let the peace of Christ rule in your hearts, for to this you were called as members of one body. And be thankful.'),
('COL', 3, 16, 'COL.3.16', 'Let the word of Christ richly dwell within you as you teach and admonish one another with all wisdom, and as you sing psalms, hymns, and spiritual songs with gratitude in your hearts to God.'),
('COL', 3, 17, 'COL.3.17', 'And whatever you do, in word or deed, do it all in the name of the Lord Jesus, giving thanks to God the Father through Him.'),
('COL', 3, 18, 'COL.3.18', 'Wives, submit to your husbands, as is fitting in the Lord.'),
('COL', 3, 19, 'COL.3.19', 'Husbands, love your wives and do not be harsh with them.'),
('COL', 3, 20, 'COL.3.20', 'Children, obey your parents in everything, for this is pleasing to the Lord.'),
('COL', 3, 21, 'COL.3.21', 'Fathers, do not provoke your children, so they will not become discouraged.'),
('COL', 3, 22, 'COL.3.22', 'Slaves, obey your earthly masters in everything, not only to please them while they are watching, but with sincerity of heart and fear of the Lord.'),
('COL', 3, 23, 'COL.3.23', 'Whatever you do, work at it with your whole being, as for the Lord and not for men,'),
('COL', 3, 24, 'COL.3.24', 'because you know that you will receive an inheritance from the Lord as your reward. It is the Lord Christ you are serving.'),
('COL', 3, 25, 'COL.3.25', 'Whoever does wrong will be repaid for his wrong, and there is no favoritism.'),
('COL', 4, 1, 'COL.4.1', 'Masters, supply your slaves with what is right and fair, since you know that you also have a Master in heaven.'),
('COL', 4, 2, 'COL.4.2', 'Devote yourselves to prayer, being watchful and thankful,'),
('COL', 4, 3, 'COL.4.3', 'as you pray also for us, that God may open to us a door for the word, so that we may proclaim the mystery of Christ, for which I am in chains.'),
('COL', 4, 4, 'COL.4.4', 'Pray that I may declare it clearly, as I should.'),
('COL', 4, 5, 'COL.4.5', 'Act wisely toward outsiders, redeeming the time.'),
('COL', 4, 6, 'COL.4.6', 'Let your speech always be gracious, seasoned with salt, so that you may know how to answer everyone.'),
('COL', 4, 7, 'COL.4.7', 'Tychicus will tell you all the news about me. He is a beloved brother, a faithful minister, and a fellow servant in the Lord.'),
('COL', 4, 8, 'COL.4.8', 'I have sent him to you for this very purpose, that you may know about us, and that he may encourage your hearts.'),
('COL', 4, 9, 'COL.4.9', 'With him I am sending Onesimus, our faithful and beloved brother, who is one of you. They will tell you about everything here.'),
('COL', 4, 10, 'COL.4.10', 'My fellow prisoner Aristarchus sends you greetings, as does Mark the cousin of Barnabas. You have already received instructions about him: If he comes to you, welcome him.'),
('COL', 4, 11, 'COL.4.11', 'Jesus, who is called Justus, also sends greetings. These are the only Jews among my fellow workers for the kingdom of God, and they have been a comfort to me.'),
('COL', 4, 12, 'COL.4.12', 'Epaphras, who is one of you and a servant of Christ Jesus, sends you greetings. He is always wrestling in prayer for you, so that you may stand mature and fully assured in the full will of God.'),
('COL', 4, 13, 'COL.4.13', 'For I testify about him that he goes to great pains for you and for those at Laodicea and Hierapolis.'),
('COL', 4, 14, 'COL.4.14', 'Luke, the beloved physician, and Demas send you greetings.'),
('COL', 4, 15, 'COL.4.15', 'Greet the brothers in Laodicea, as well as Nympha and the church that meets at her house.'),
('COL', 4, 16, 'COL.4.16', 'After this letter has been read among you, make sure that it is also read in the church of the Laodiceans, and that you in turn read the letter from Laodicea.'),
('COL', 4, 17, 'COL.4.17', 'Tell Archippus: “See to it that you complete the ministry you have received in the Lord.”'),
('COL', 4, 18, 'COL.4.18', 'This greeting is in my own hand—Paul. Remember my chains. Grace be with you.'),
('1TH', 1, 1, '1TH.1.1', 'Paul, Silvanus, and Timothy, To the church of the Thessalonians in God the Father and the Lord Jesus Christ: Grace and peace to you.'),
('1TH', 1, 2, '1TH.1.2', 'We always thank God for all of you, remembering you in our prayers'),
('1TH', 1, 3, '1TH.1.3', 'and continually recalling before our God and Father your work of faith, your labor of love, and your enduring hope in our Lord Jesus Christ.'),
('1TH', 1, 4, '1TH.1.4', 'Brothers who are beloved by God, we know that He has chosen you,'),
('1TH', 1, 5, '1TH.1.5', 'because our gospel came to you not only in word, but also in power, in the Holy Spirit, and with great conviction—just as you know we lived among you for your sake.'),
('1TH', 1, 6, '1TH.1.6', 'And you became imitators of us and of the Lord when you welcomed the message with the joy of the Holy Spirit, in spite of your great suffering.'),
('1TH', 1, 7, '1TH.1.7', 'As a result, you have become an example to all the believers in Macedonia and Achaia.'),
('1TH', 1, 8, '1TH.1.8', 'For not only did the message of the Lord ring out from you to Macedonia and Achaia, but your faith in God has gone out to every place, so that we have no need to say anything more.'),
('1TH', 1, 9, '1TH.1.9', 'For they themselves report what kind of welcome you gave us, and how you turned to God from idols to serve the living and true God'),
('1TH', 1, 10, '1TH.1.10', 'and to await His Son from heaven, whom He raised from the dead—Jesus our deliverer from the coming wrath.'),
('1TH', 2, 1, '1TH.2.1', 'You yourselves know, brothers, that our visit to you was not in vain.'),
('1TH', 2, 2, '1TH.2.2', 'As you are aware, we had already endured suffering and shameful treatment in Philippi. But in the face of strong opposition, we were bold in our God to speak to you the gospel of God.'),
('1TH', 2, 3, '1TH.2.3', 'For our appeal does not arise from deceit or ulterior motives or trickery.'),
('1TH', 2, 4, '1TH.2.4', 'Instead, we speak as those approved by God to be entrusted with the gospel, not in order to please men but God, who examines our hearts.'),
('1TH', 2, 5, '1TH.2.5', 'As you know, we never used words of flattery or any pretext for greed. God is our witness!'),
('1TH', 2, 6, '1TH.2.6', 'Nor did we seek praise from you or from anyone else, although as apostles of Christ we had authority to demand it.'),
('1TH', 2, 7, '1TH.2.7', 'On the contrary, we were gentle among you, like a nursing mother caring for her children.'),
('1TH', 2, 8, '1TH.2.8', 'We cared so deeply that we were delighted to share with you not only the gospel of God, but our own lives as well. That is how beloved you have become to us.'),
('1TH', 2, 9, '1TH.2.9', 'Surely you recall, brothers, our labor and toil. We worked night and day so that we would not be a burden to anyone while we proclaimed to you the gospel of God.'),
('1TH', 2, 10, '1TH.2.10', 'You are witnesses, and so is God, of how holy, righteous, and blameless our conduct was among you who believed.'),
('1TH', 2, 11, '1TH.2.11', 'For you know that we treated each of you as a father treats his own children—'),
('1TH', 2, 12, '1TH.2.12', 'encouraging you, comforting you, and urging you to walk in a manner worthy of God, who calls you into His own kingdom and glory.'),
('1TH', 2, 13, '1TH.2.13', 'And we continually thank God because, when you received the word of God that you heard from us, you accepted it not as the word of men, but as it truly is, the word of God, which is also now at work in you who believe.'),
('1TH', 2, 14, '1TH.2.14', 'For you, brothers, became imitators of the churches of God in Judea that are in Christ Jesus. You suffered from your own countrymen the very things they suffered from the Jews,'),
('1TH', 2, 15, '1TH.2.15', 'who killed both the Lord Jesus and their own prophets and drove us out as well. They are displeasing to God and hostile to all men,'),
('1TH', 2, 16, '1TH.2.16', 'hindering us from telling the Gentiles how they may be saved. As a result, they continue to heap up their sins to full capacity; the utmost wrath has come upon them.'),
('1TH', 2, 17, '1TH.2.17', 'Brothers, although we were torn away from you for a short time (in person, not in heart), our desire to see you face to face was even more intense.'),
('1TH', 2, 18, '1TH.2.18', 'For we wanted to come to you—indeed I, Paul, tried again and again—but Satan obstructed us.'),
('1TH', 2, 19, '1TH.2.19', 'After all, who is our hope, our joy, our crown of boasting, if it is not you yourselves in the presence of our Lord Jesus at His coming?'),
('1TH', 2, 20, '1TH.2.20', 'You are indeed our glory and our joy.'),
('1TH', 3, 1, '1TH.3.1', 'So when we could bear it no longer, we were willing to be left on our own in Athens.'),
('1TH', 3, 2, '1TH.3.2', 'We sent Timothy, our brother and fellow worker for God in the gospel of Christ, to strengthen and encourage you in your faith,'),
('1TH', 3, 3, '1TH.3.3', 'so that none of you would be shaken by these trials. For you know that we are destined for this.'),
('1TH', 3, 4, '1TH.3.4', 'Indeed, when we were with you, we kept warning you that we would suffer persecution; and as you know, it has come to pass.'),
('1TH', 3, 5, '1TH.3.5', 'For this reason, when I could bear it no longer, I sent to find out about your faith, for fear that the tempter had somehow tempted you and that our labor might have been in vain.'),
('1TH', 3, 6, '1TH.3.6', 'But just now, Timothy has returned from his visit with the good news about your faith, your love, and the fond memories you have preserved, longing to see us just as we long to see you.'),
('1TH', 3, 7, '1TH.3.7', 'For this reason, brothers, in all our distress and persecution, we have been reassured about you, because of your faith.'),
('1TH', 3, 8, '1TH.3.8', 'For now we can go on living, as long as you are standing firm in the Lord.'),
('1TH', 3, 9, '1TH.3.9', 'How can we adequately thank God for you in return for our great joy over you in His presence?'),
('1TH', 3, 10, '1TH.3.10', 'Night and day we pray most earnestly that we may see you face to face and supply what is lacking in your faith.'),
('1TH', 3, 11, '1TH.3.11', 'Now may our God and Father Himself, and our Lord Jesus, direct our way to you.'),
('1TH', 3, 12, '1TH.3.12', 'And may the Lord cause you to increase and overflow with love for one another and for everyone else, just as our love for you overflows,'),
('1TH', 3, 13, '1TH.3.13', 'so that He may establish your hearts in blamelessness and holiness before our God and Father at the coming of our Lord Jesus with all His saints. Amen.'),
('1TH', 4, 1, '1TH.4.1', 'Finally, brothers, we ask and encourage you in the Lord Jesus to live in a way that is pleasing to God, just as you have received from us. This is how you already live, so you should do so all the more.'),
('1TH', 4, 2, '1TH.4.2', 'For you know the instructions we gave you by the authority of the Lord Jesus.'),
('1TH', 4, 3, '1TH.4.3', 'For it is God’s will that you should be holy: You must abstain from sexual immorality;'),
('1TH', 4, 4, '1TH.4.4', 'each of you must know how to control his own body in holiness and honor,'),
('1TH', 4, 5, '1TH.4.5', 'not in lustful passion like the Gentiles who do not know God;'),
('1TH', 4, 6, '1TH.4.6', 'and no one should ever violate or exploit his brother in this regard, because the Lord will avenge all such acts, as we have already told you and solemnly warned you.'),
('1TH', 4, 7, '1TH.4.7', 'For God has not called us to impurity, but to holiness.'),
('1TH', 4, 8, '1TH.4.8', 'Anyone, then, who rejects this command does not reject man but God, the very One who gives you His Holy Spirit.'),
('1TH', 4, 9, '1TH.4.9', 'Now about brotherly love, you do not need anyone to write to you, because you yourselves have been taught by God to love one another.'),
('1TH', 4, 10, '1TH.4.10', 'And you are indeed showing this love to all the brothers throughout Macedonia. But we urge you, brothers, to excel more and more'),
('1TH', 4, 11, '1TH.4.11', 'and to aspire to live quietly, to attend to your own matters, and to work with your own hands, as we instructed you.'),
('1TH', 4, 12, '1TH.4.12', 'Then you will behave properly toward outsiders, without being dependent on anyone.'),
('1TH', 4, 13, '1TH.4.13', 'Brothers, we do not want you to be uninformed about those who sleep in death, so that you will not grieve like the rest, who are without hope.'),
('1TH', 4, 14, '1TH.4.14', 'For since we believe that Jesus died and rose again, we also believe that God will bring with Jesus those who have fallen asleep in Him.'),
('1TH', 4, 15, '1TH.4.15', 'By the word of the Lord, we declare to you that we who are alive and remain until the coming of the Lord will by no means precede those who have fallen asleep.'),
('1TH', 4, 16, '1TH.4.16', 'For the Lord Himself will descend from heaven with a loud command, with the voice of an archangel, and with the trumpet of God, and the dead in Christ will be the first to rise.'),
('1TH', 4, 17, '1TH.4.17', 'After that, we who are alive and remain will be caught up together with them in the clouds to meet the Lord in the air. And so we will always be with the Lord.'),
('1TH', 4, 18, '1TH.4.18', 'Therefore encourage one another with these words.'),
('1TH', 5, 1, '1TH.5.1', 'Now about the times and seasons, brothers, we do not need to write to you.'),
('1TH', 5, 2, '1TH.5.2', 'For you are fully aware that the Day of the Lord will come like a thief in the night.'),
('1TH', 5, 3, '1TH.5.3', 'While people are saying, “Peace and security,” destruction will come upon them suddenly, like labor pains on a pregnant woman, and they will not escape.'),
('1TH', 5, 4, '1TH.5.4', 'But you, brothers, are not in the darkness so that this day should overtake you like a thief.'),
('1TH', 5, 5, '1TH.5.5', 'For you are all sons of the light and sons of the day; we do not belong to the night or to the darkness.'),
('1TH', 5, 6, '1TH.5.6', 'So then, let us not sleep as the others do, but let us remain awake and sober.'),
('1TH', 5, 7, '1TH.5.7', 'For those who sleep, sleep at night, and those who get drunk, get drunk at night.'),
('1TH', 5, 8, '1TH.5.8', 'But since we belong to the day, let us be sober, putting on the breastplate of faith and love, and the helmet of our hope of salvation.'),
('1TH', 5, 9, '1TH.5.9', 'For God has not appointed us to suffer wrath, but to obtain salvation through our Lord Jesus Christ.'),
('1TH', 5, 10, '1TH.5.10', 'He died for us so that, whether we are awake or asleep, we may live together with Him.'),
('1TH', 5, 11, '1TH.5.11', 'Therefore encourage and build one another up, just as you are already doing.'),
('1TH', 5, 12, '1TH.5.12', 'But we ask you, brothers, to acknowledge those who work diligently among you, who care for you in the Lord and who admonish you.'),
('1TH', 5, 13, '1TH.5.13', 'In love, hold them in highest regard because of their work. Live in peace with one another.'),
('1TH', 5, 14, '1TH.5.14', 'And we urge you, brothers, to admonish the unruly, encourage the fainthearted, help the weak, and be patient with everyone.'),
('1TH', 5, 15, '1TH.5.15', 'Make sure that no one repays evil for evil. Always pursue what is good for one another and for all people.'),
('1TH', 5, 16, '1TH.5.16', 'Rejoice at all times.'),
('1TH', 5, 17, '1TH.5.17', 'Pray without ceasing.'),
('1TH', 5, 18, '1TH.5.18', 'Give thanks in every circumstance, for this is God’s will for you in Christ Jesus.'),
('1TH', 5, 19, '1TH.5.19', 'Do not extinguish the Spirit.'),
('1TH', 5, 20, '1TH.5.20', 'Do not treat prophecies with contempt,'),
('1TH', 5, 21, '1TH.5.21', 'but test all things. Hold fast to what is good.'),
('1TH', 5, 22, '1TH.5.22', 'Abstain from every form of evil.'),
('1TH', 5, 23, '1TH.5.23', 'Now may the God of peace Himself sanctify you completely, and may your entire spirit, soul, and body be kept blameless at the coming of our Lord Jesus Christ.'),
('1TH', 5, 24, '1TH.5.24', 'The One who calls you is faithful, and He will do it.'),
('1TH', 5, 25, '1TH.5.25', 'Brothers, pray for us as well.'),
('1TH', 5, 26, '1TH.5.26', 'Greet all the brothers with a holy kiss.'),
('1TH', 5, 27, '1TH.5.27', 'I charge you before the Lord to have this letter read to all the brothers.'),
('1TH', 5, 28, '1TH.5.28', 'The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with you.'),
('2TH', 1, 1, '2TH.1.1', 'Paul, Silvanus, and Timothy, To the church of the Thessalonians in God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ:'),
('2TH', 1, 2, '2TH.1.2', 'Grace and peace to you from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.'),
('2TH', 1, 3, '2TH.1.3', 'We are obligated to thank God for you all the time, brothers, as is fitting, because your faith is growing more and more, and your love for one another is increasing.'),
('2TH', 1, 4, '2TH.1.4', 'That is why we boast among God’s churches about your perseverance and faith in the face of all the persecution and affliction you are enduring.'),
('2TH', 1, 5, '2TH.1.5', 'All this is clear evidence of God’s righteous judgment. And so you will be counted worthy of the kingdom of God, for which you are suffering.'),
('2TH', 1, 6, '2TH.1.6', 'After all, it is only right for God to repay with affliction those who afflict you,'),
('2TH', 1, 7, '2TH.1.7', 'and to grant relief to you who are oppressed and to us as well. This will take place when the Lord Jesus is revealed from heaven with His mighty angels'),
('2TH', 1, 8, '2TH.1.8', 'in blazing fire, inflicting vengeance on those who do not know God and do not obey the gospel of our Lord Jesus.'),
('2TH', 1, 9, '2TH.1.9', 'They will suffer the penalty of eternal destruction, separated from the presence of the Lord and the glory of His might,'),
('2TH', 1, 10, '2TH.1.10', 'on the day He comes to be glorified in His saints and regarded with wonder by all who have believed, including you who have believed our testimony.'),
('2TH', 1, 11, '2TH.1.11', 'To this end, we always pray for you, that our God will count you worthy of His calling, and that He will powerfully fulfill your every good desire and work of faith,'),
('2TH', 1, 12, '2TH.1.12', 'so that the name of our Lord Jesus will be glorified in you, and you in Him, according to the grace of our God and of the Lord Jesus Christ.'),
('2TH', 2, 1, '2TH.2.1', 'Now concerning the coming of our Lord Jesus Christ and our being gathered together to Him, we ask you, brothers,'),
('2TH', 2, 2, '2TH.2.2', 'not to be easily disconcerted or alarmed by any spirit or message or letter seeming to be from us, alleging that the Day of the Lord has already come.'),
('2TH', 2, 3, '2TH.2.3', 'Let no one deceive you in any way, for it will not come until the rebellion occurs and the man of lawlessness—the son of destruction—is revealed.'),
('2TH', 2, 4, '2TH.2.4', 'He will oppose and exalt himself above every so-called god or object of worship. So he will seat himself in the temple of God, proclaiming himself to be God.'),
('2TH', 2, 5, '2TH.2.5', 'Do you not remember that I told you these things while I was still with you?'),
('2TH', 2, 6, '2TH.2.6', 'And you know what is now restraining him, so that he may be revealed at the proper time.'),
('2TH', 2, 7, '2TH.2.7', 'For the mystery of lawlessness is already at work, but the one who now restrains it will continue until he is taken out of the way.'),
('2TH', 2, 8, '2TH.2.8', 'And then the lawless one will be revealed, whom the Lord Jesus will slay with the breath of His mouth and annihilate by the majesty of His arrival.'),
('2TH', 2, 9, '2TH.2.9', 'The coming of the lawless one will be accompanied by the working of Satan, with every kind of power, sign, and false wonder,'),
('2TH', 2, 10, '2TH.2.10', 'and with every wicked deception directed against those who are perishing, because they refused the love of the truth that would have saved them.'),
('2TH', 2, 11, '2TH.2.11', 'For this reason God will send them a powerful delusion so that they believe the lie,'),
('2TH', 2, 12, '2TH.2.12', 'in order that judgment may come upon all who have disbelieved the truth and delighted in wickedness.'),
('2TH', 2, 13, '2TH.2.13', 'But we should always thank God for you, brothers who are loved by the Lord, because God chose you from the beginning to be saved by the sanctification of the Spirit and by faith in the truth.'),
('2TH', 2, 14, '2TH.2.14', 'To this He called you through our gospel, so that you may share in the glory of our Lord Jesus Christ.'),
('2TH', 2, 15, '2TH.2.15', 'Therefore, brothers, stand firm and cling to the traditions we taught you, whether by speech or by letter.'),
('2TH', 2, 16, '2TH.2.16', 'Now may our Lord Jesus Christ Himself and God our Father, who by grace has loved us and given us eternal comfort and good hope,'),
('2TH', 2, 17, '2TH.2.17', 'encourage your hearts and strengthen you in every good word and deed.'),
('2TH', 3, 1, '2TH.3.1', 'Finally, brothers, pray for us, that the word of the Lord may spread quickly and be held in honor, just as it was with you.'),
('2TH', 3, 2, '2TH.3.2', 'And pray that we may be delivered from wicked and evil men; for not everyone holds to the faith.'),
('2TH', 3, 3, '2TH.3.3', 'But the Lord is faithful, and He will strengthen you and guard you from the evil one.'),
('2TH', 3, 4, '2TH.3.4', 'And we have confidence in the Lord that you are doing and will continue to do what we command.'),
('2TH', 3, 5, '2TH.3.5', 'May the Lord direct your hearts into God’s love and Christ’s perseverance.'),
('2TH', 3, 6, '2TH.3.6', 'Now we command you, brothers, in the name of our Lord Jesus Christ, to keep away from any brother who leads an undisciplined life that is not in keeping with the tradition you received from us.'),
('2TH', 3, 7, '2TH.3.7', 'For you yourselves know how you ought to imitate us, because we were not undisciplined among you,'),
('2TH', 3, 8, '2TH.3.8', 'nor did we eat anyone’s food without paying for it. Instead, in labor and toil, we worked night and day so that we would not be a burden to any of you.'),
('2TH', 3, 9, '2TH.3.9', 'Not that we lack this right, but we wanted to offer ourselves as an example for you to imitate.'),
('2TH', 3, 10, '2TH.3.10', 'For even while we were with you, we gave you this command: “If anyone is unwilling to work, he shall not eat.”'),
('2TH', 3, 11, '2TH.3.11', 'For we hear that some of you are leading undisciplined lives, accomplishing nothing, but being busybodies.'),
('2TH', 3, 12, '2TH.3.12', 'We command and urge such people by our Lord Jesus Christ to begin working quietly to earn their own living.'),
('2TH', 3, 13, '2TH.3.13', 'But as for you, brothers, do not grow weary in well-doing.'),
('2TH', 3, 14, '2TH.3.14', 'Take note of anyone who does not obey the instructions we have given in this letter. Do not associate with him, so that he may be ashamed.'),
('2TH', 3, 15, '2TH.3.15', 'Yet do not regard him as an enemy, but admonish him as a brother.'),
('2TH', 3, 16, '2TH.3.16', 'Now may the Lord of peace Himself give you peace at all times and in every way. The Lord be with all of you.'),
('2TH', 3, 17, '2TH.3.17', 'This greeting is in my own hand—Paul. This is my mark in every letter; it is the way I write.'),
('2TH', 3, 18, '2TH.3.18', 'The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with all of you.'),
('1TI', 1, 1, '1TI.1.1', 'Paul, an apostle of Christ Jesus by the command of God our Savior and of Christ Jesus our hope,'),
('1TI', 1, 2, '1TI.1.2', 'To Timothy, my true child in the faith: Grace, mercy, and peace from God the Father and Christ Jesus our Lord.'),
('1TI', 1, 3, '1TI.1.3', 'As I urged you on my departure to Macedonia, you should stay on at Ephesus to instruct certain men not to teach false doctrines'),
('1TI', 1, 4, '1TI.1.4', 'or devote themselves to myths and endless genealogies, which promote speculation rather than the stewardship of God’s work, which is by faith.'),
('1TI', 1, 5, '1TI.1.5', 'The goal of our instruction is the love that comes from a pure heart, a clear conscience, and a sincere faith.'),
('1TI', 1, 6, '1TI.1.6', 'Some have strayed from these ways and turned aside to empty talk.'),
('1TI', 1, 7, '1TI.1.7', 'They want to be teachers of the law, but they do not understand what they are saying or that which they so confidently assert.'),
('1TI', 1, 8, '1TI.1.8', 'Now we know that the law is good, if one uses it legitimately.'),
('1TI', 1, 9, '1TI.1.9', 'We realize that law is not enacted for the righteous, but for the lawless and rebellious, for the ungodly and sinful, for the unholy and profane, for killers of father or mother, for murderers,'),
('1TI', 1, 10, '1TI.1.10', 'for the sexually immoral, for homosexuals, for slave traders and liars and perjurers, and for anyone else who is averse to sound teaching'),
('1TI', 1, 11, '1TI.1.11', 'that agrees with the glorious gospel of the blessed God, with which I have been entrusted.'),
('1TI', 1, 12, '1TI.1.12', 'I thank Christ Jesus our Lord, who has strengthened me, that He considered me faithful and appointed me to service.'),
('1TI', 1, 13, '1TI.1.13', 'I was formerly a blasphemer, a persecutor, and a violent man; yet because I had acted in ignorance and unbelief, I was shown mercy.'),
('1TI', 1, 14, '1TI.1.14', 'And the grace of our Lord overflowed to me, along with the faith and love that are in Christ Jesus.'),
('1TI', 1, 15, '1TI.1.15', 'This is a trustworthy saying, worthy of full acceptance: Christ Jesus came into the world to save sinners, of whom I am the worst.'),
('1TI', 1, 16, '1TI.1.16', 'But for this very reason I was shown mercy, so that in me, the worst of sinners, Christ Jesus might display His perfect patience as an example to those who would believe in Him for eternal life.'),
('1TI', 1, 17, '1TI.1.17', 'Now to the King eternal, immortal, and invisible, the only God, be honor and glory forever and ever. Amen.'),
('1TI', 1, 18, '1TI.1.18', 'Timothy, my child, I entrust you with this command in keeping with the previous prophecies about you, so that by them you may fight the good fight,'),
('1TI', 1, 19, '1TI.1.19', 'holding on to faith and a good conscience, which some have rejected and thereby shipwrecked their faith.'),
('1TI', 1, 20, '1TI.1.20', 'Among them are Hymenaeus and Alexander, whom I have handed over to Satan to be taught not to blaspheme.'),
('1TI', 2, 1, '1TI.2.1', 'First of all, then, I urge that petitions, prayers, intercessions, and thanksgiving be offered for everyone—'),
('1TI', 2, 2, '1TI.2.2', 'for kings and all those in authority—so that we may lead tranquil and quiet lives in all godliness and dignity.'),
('1TI', 2, 3, '1TI.2.3', 'This is good and pleasing in the sight of God our Savior,'),
('1TI', 2, 4, '1TI.2.4', 'who wants everyone to be saved and to come to the knowledge of the truth.'),
('1TI', 2, 5, '1TI.2.5', 'For there is one God, and there is one mediator between God and men, the man Christ Jesus,'),
('1TI', 2, 6, '1TI.2.6', 'who gave Himself as a ransom for all—the testimony that was given at just the right time.'),
('1TI', 2, 7, '1TI.2.7', 'For this reason I was appointed as a preacher, an apostle, and a faithful and true teacher of the Gentiles. I am telling the truth; I am not lying about anything.'),
('1TI', 2, 8, '1TI.2.8', 'Therefore I want the men everywhere to pray, lifting up holy hands, without anger or dissension.'),
('1TI', 2, 9, '1TI.2.9', 'Likewise, I want the women to adorn themselves with respectable apparel, with modesty, and with self-control, not with braided hair or gold or pearls or expensive clothes,'),
('1TI', 2, 10, '1TI.2.10', 'but with good deeds, as is proper for women who profess to worship God.'),
('1TI', 2, 11, '1TI.2.11', 'A woman must learn in quietness and full submissiveness.'),
('1TI', 2, 12, '1TI.2.12', 'I do not permit a woman to teach or to exercise authority over a man; she is to remain quiet.'),
('1TI', 2, 13, '1TI.2.13', 'For Adam was formed first, and then Eve.'),
('1TI', 2, 14, '1TI.2.14', 'And it was not Adam who was deceived, but the woman who was deceived and fell into transgression.'),
('1TI', 2, 15, '1TI.2.15', 'Women, however, will be saved through childbearing, if they continue in faith, love, and holiness, with self-control.'),
('1TI', 3, 1, '1TI.3.1', 'This is a trustworthy saying: If anyone aspires to be an overseer, he desires a noble task.'),
('1TI', 3, 2, '1TI.3.2', 'An overseer, then, must be above reproach, the husband of but one wife, temperate, self-controlled, respectable, hospitable, able to teach,'),
('1TI', 3, 3, '1TI.3.3', 'not dependent on wine, not violent but gentle, peaceable, and free of the love of money.'),
('1TI', 3, 4, '1TI.3.4', 'An overseer must manage his own household well and keep his children under control, with complete dignity.'),
('1TI', 3, 5, '1TI.3.5', 'For if someone does not know how to manage his own household, how can he care for the church of God?'),
('1TI', 3, 6, '1TI.3.6', 'He must not be a recent convert, or he may become conceited and fall under the same condemnation as the devil.'),
('1TI', 3, 7, '1TI.3.7', 'Furthermore, he must have a good reputation with outsiders, so that he will not fall into disgrace and into the snare of the devil.'),
('1TI', 3, 8, '1TI.3.8', 'Deacons likewise must be dignified, not double-tongued or given to much wine or greedy for money.'),
('1TI', 3, 9, '1TI.3.9', 'They must hold to the mystery of the faith with a clear conscience.'),
('1TI', 3, 10, '1TI.3.10', 'Additionally, they must first be tested. Then, if they are above reproach, let them serve as deacons.'),
('1TI', 3, 11, '1TI.3.11', 'In the same way, the women must be dignified, not slanderers, but temperate and faithful in all things.'),
('1TI', 3, 12, '1TI.3.12', 'A deacon must be the husband of but one wife, a good manager of his children and of his own household.'),
('1TI', 3, 13, '1TI.3.13', 'For those who have served well as deacons acquire for themselves a high standing and great confidence in the faith that is in Christ Jesus.'),
('1TI', 3, 14, '1TI.3.14', 'Although I hope to come to you soon, I am writing you these things'),
('1TI', 3, 15, '1TI.3.15', 'in case I am delayed, so that you will know how each one must conduct himself in God’s household, which is the church of the living God, the pillar and foundation of the truth.'),
('1TI', 3, 16, '1TI.3.16', 'By common confession, the mystery of godliness is great: He appeared in the flesh, was vindicated by the Spirit, was seen by angels, was proclaimed among the nations, was believed in throughout the world, was taken up in glory.'),
('1TI', 4, 1, '1TI.4.1', 'Now the Spirit expressly states that in later times some will abandon the faith to follow deceitful spirits and the teachings of demons,'),
('1TI', 4, 2, '1TI.4.2', 'influenced by the hypocrisy of liars, whose consciences are seared with a hot iron.'),
('1TI', 4, 3, '1TI.4.3', 'They will prohibit marriage and require abstinence from certain foods that God has created to be received with thanksgiving by those who believe and know the truth.'),
('1TI', 4, 4, '1TI.4.4', 'For every creation of God is good, and nothing that is received with thanksgiving should be rejected,'),
('1TI', 4, 5, '1TI.4.5', 'because it is sanctified by the word of God and prayer.'),
('1TI', 4, 6, '1TI.4.6', 'By pointing out these things to the brothers, you will be a good servant of Christ Jesus, nourished by the words of faith and sound instruction that you have followed.'),
('1TI', 4, 7, '1TI.4.7', 'But reject irreverent, silly myths. Instead, train yourself for godliness.'),
('1TI', 4, 8, '1TI.4.8', 'For physical exercise is of limited value, but godliness is valuable in every way, holding promise for the present life and for the one to come.'),
('1TI', 4, 9, '1TI.4.9', 'This is a trustworthy saying, worthy of full acceptance.'),
('1TI', 4, 10, '1TI.4.10', 'To this end we labor and strive, because we have set our hope on the living God, who is the Savior of everyone, and especially of those who believe.'),
('1TI', 4, 11, '1TI.4.11', 'Command and teach these things.'),
('1TI', 4, 12, '1TI.4.12', 'Let no one despise your youth, but set an example for the believers in speech, in conduct, in love, in faith, in purity.'),
('1TI', 4, 13, '1TI.4.13', 'Until I come, devote yourself to the public reading of Scripture, to exhortation, and to teaching.'),
('1TI', 4, 14, '1TI.4.14', 'Do not neglect the gift that is in you, which was given you through the prophecy spoken over you at the laying on of the hands of the elders.'),
('1TI', 4, 15, '1TI.4.15', 'Be diligent in these matters and absorbed in them, so that your progress will be evident to all.'),
('1TI', 4, 16, '1TI.4.16', 'Pay close attention to your life and to your teaching. Persevere in these things, for by so doing you will save both yourself and those who hear you.'),
('1TI', 5, 1, '1TI.5.1', 'Do not rebuke an older man, but appeal to him as to a father. Treat younger men as brothers,'),
('1TI', 5, 2, '1TI.5.2', 'older women as mothers, and younger women as sisters, with absolute purity.'),
('1TI', 5, 3, '1TI.5.3', 'Honor the widows who are truly widows.'),
('1TI', 5, 4, '1TI.5.4', 'But if a widow has children or grandchildren, they must first learn to show godliness to their own family and repay their parents, for this is pleasing in the sight of God.'),
('1TI', 5, 5, '1TI.5.5', 'The widow who is truly in need and left all alone puts her hope in God and continues night and day in her petitions and prayers.'),
('1TI', 5, 6, '1TI.5.6', 'But she who lives for pleasure is dead even while she is still alive.'),
('1TI', 5, 7, '1TI.5.7', 'Give these instructions to the believers, so that they will be above reproach.'),
('1TI', 5, 8, '1TI.5.8', 'If anyone does not provide for his own, and especially his own household, he has denied the faith and is worse than an unbeliever.'),
('1TI', 5, 9, '1TI.5.9', 'A widow should be enrolled if she is at least sixty years old, faithful to her husband,'),
('1TI', 5, 10, '1TI.5.10', 'and well known for good deeds such as bringing up children, entertaining strangers, washing the feet of the saints, imparting relief to the afflicted, and devoting herself to every good work.'),
('1TI', 5, 11, '1TI.5.11', 'But refuse to enroll younger widows. For when their passions draw them away from Christ, they will want to marry,'),
('1TI', 5, 12, '1TI.5.12', 'and thus will incur judgment because they are setting aside their first faith.'),
('1TI', 5, 13, '1TI.5.13', 'At the same time they will also learn to be idle, going from house to house and being not only idle, but also gossips and busybodies, discussing things they should not mention.'),
('1TI', 5, 14, '1TI.5.14', 'So I advise the younger widows to marry, have children, and manage their households, denying the adversary occasion for slander.'),
('1TI', 5, 15, '1TI.5.15', 'For some have already turned aside to follow Satan.'),
('1TI', 5, 16, '1TI.5.16', 'If any believing woman has dependent widows, she must assist them and not allow the church to be burdened, so that it can help the widows who are truly in need.'),
('1TI', 5, 17, '1TI.5.17', 'Elders who lead effectively are worthy of double honor, especially those who work hard at preaching and teaching.'),
('1TI', 5, 18, '1TI.5.18', 'For the Scripture says, “Do not muzzle an ox while it is treading out the grain,” and, “The worker is worthy of his wages.”'),
('1TI', 5, 19, '1TI.5.19', 'Do not entertain an accusation against an elder, except on the testimony of two or three witnesses.'),
('1TI', 5, 20, '1TI.5.20', 'But those who persist in sin should be rebuked in front of everyone, so that the others will stand in fear of sin.'),
('1TI', 5, 21, '1TI.5.21', 'I solemnly charge you before God and Christ Jesus and the elect angels to maintain these principles without bias, and to do nothing out of partiality.'),
('1TI', 5, 22, '1TI.5.22', 'Do not be too quick in the laying on of hands and thereby share in the sins of others. Keep yourself pure.'),
('1TI', 5, 23, '1TI.5.23', 'Stop drinking only water and use a little wine instead, because of your stomach and your frequent ailments.'),
('1TI', 5, 24, '1TI.5.24', 'The sins of some men are obvious, going ahead of them to judgment; but the sins of others do not surface until later.'),
('1TI', 5, 25, '1TI.5.25', 'In the same way, good deeds are obvious, and even the ones that are inconspicuous cannot remain hidden.'),
('1TI', 6, 1, '1TI.6.1', 'All who are under the yoke of slavery should regard their masters as fully worthy of honor, so that God’s name and our teaching will not be discredited.'),
('1TI', 6, 2, '1TI.6.2', 'Those who have believing masters should not show disrespect because they are brothers, but should serve them all the more, since those receiving their good service are beloved believers. Teach and encourage these principles.'),
('1TI', 6, 3, '1TI.6.3', 'If anyone teaches another doctrine and disagrees with the sound words of our Lord Jesus Christ and with godly teaching,'),
('1TI', 6, 4, '1TI.6.4', 'he is conceited and understands nothing. Instead, he has an unhealthy interest in controversies and disputes about words, out of which come envy, strife, abusive talk, evil suspicions,'),
('1TI', 6, 5, '1TI.6.5', 'and constant friction between men of depraved mind who are devoid of the truth. These men regard godliness as a means of gain.'),
('1TI', 6, 6, '1TI.6.6', 'Of course, godliness with contentment is great gain.'),
('1TI', 6, 7, '1TI.6.7', 'For we brought nothing into the world, so we cannot carry anything out of it.'),
('1TI', 6, 8, '1TI.6.8', 'But if we have food and clothing, we will be content with these.'),
('1TI', 6, 9, '1TI.6.9', 'Those who want to be rich, however, fall into temptation and become ensnared by many foolish and harmful desires that plunge them into ruin and destruction.'),
('1TI', 6, 10, '1TI.6.10', 'For the love of money is the root of all kinds of evil. By craving it, some have wandered away from the faith and pierced themselves with many sorrows.'),
('1TI', 6, 11, '1TI.6.11', 'But you, O man of God, flee from these things and pursue righteousness, godliness, faith, love, perseverance, and gentleness.'),
('1TI', 6, 12, '1TI.6.12', 'Fight the good fight of the faith. Take hold of the eternal life to which you were called when you made the good confession before many witnesses.'),
('1TI', 6, 13, '1TI.6.13', 'I charge you in the presence of God, who gives life to all things, and of Christ Jesus, who made the good confession in His testimony before Pontius Pilate:'),
('1TI', 6, 14, '1TI.6.14', 'Keep this commandment without stain or reproach until the appearance of our Lord Jesus Christ,'),
('1TI', 6, 15, '1TI.6.15', 'which the blessed and only Sovereign One—the King of kings and Lord of lords—will bring about in His own time.'),
('1TI', 6, 16, '1TI.6.16', 'He alone is immortal and dwells in unapproachable light. No one has ever seen Him, nor can anyone see Him. To Him be honor and eternal dominion! Amen.'),
('1TI', 6, 17, '1TI.6.17', 'Instruct those who are rich in the present age not to be conceited and not to put their hope in the uncertainty of wealth, but in God, who richly provides all things for us to enjoy.'),
('1TI', 6, 18, '1TI.6.18', 'Instruct them to do good, to be rich in good works, and to be generous and ready to share,'),
('1TI', 6, 19, '1TI.6.19', 'treasuring up for themselves a firm foundation for the future, so that they may take hold of that which is truly life.'),
('1TI', 6, 20, '1TI.6.20', 'O Timothy, guard what has been entrusted to you. Avoid irreverent, empty chatter and the opposing arguments of so-called “knowledge,”'),
('1TI', 6, 21, '1TI.6.21', 'which some have professed and thus swerved away from the faith. Grace be with you all.'),
('2TI', 1, 1, '2TI.1.1', 'Paul, an apostle of Christ Jesus by the will of God, according to the promise of life in Christ Jesus,'),
('2TI', 1, 2, '2TI.1.2', 'To Timothy, my beloved child: Grace, mercy, and peace from God the Father and Christ Jesus our Lord.'),
('2TI', 1, 3, '2TI.1.3', 'I thank God, whom I serve with a clear conscience as did my forefathers, as I constantly remember you night and day in my prayers.'),
('2TI', 1, 4, '2TI.1.4', 'Recalling your tears, I long to see you so that I may be filled with joy.'),
('2TI', 1, 5, '2TI.1.5', 'I am reminded of your sincere faith, which first dwelt in your grandmother Lois and your mother Eunice, and I am convinced is in you as well.'),
('2TI', 1, 6, '2TI.1.6', 'For this reason I remind you to fan into flame the gift of God, which is in you through the laying on of my hands.'),
('2TI', 1, 7, '2TI.1.7', 'For God has not given us a spirit of fear, but of power, love, and self-control.'),
('2TI', 1, 8, '2TI.1.8', 'So do not be ashamed of the testimony of our Lord, or of me, His prisoner. Instead, join me in suffering for the gospel by the power of God.'),
('2TI', 1, 9, '2TI.1.9', 'He has saved us and called us to a holy calling, not because of our works, but by His own purpose and by the grace He granted us in Christ Jesus before time began.'),
('2TI', 1, 10, '2TI.1.10', 'And now He has revealed this grace through the appearing of our Savior, Christ Jesus, who has abolished death and illuminated the way to life and immortality through the gospel,'),
('2TI', 1, 11, '2TI.1.11', 'to which I was appointed as a preacher, an apostle, and a teacher.'),
('2TI', 1, 12, '2TI.1.12', 'For this reason, even though I suffer as I do, I am not ashamed; for I know whom I have believed, and I am convinced that He is able to guard what I have entrusted to Him for that day.'),
('2TI', 1, 13, '2TI.1.13', 'Hold on to the pattern of sound teaching you have heard from me, with the faith and love that are in Christ Jesus.'),
('2TI', 1, 14, '2TI.1.14', 'Guard the treasure entrusted to you, with the help of the Holy Spirit who dwells in us.'),
('2TI', 1, 15, '2TI.1.15', 'You know that everyone in the province of Asia has deserted me, including Phygelus and Hermogenes.'),
('2TI', 1, 16, '2TI.1.16', 'May the Lord grant mercy to the household of Onesiphorus, because he has often refreshed me and was unashamed of my chains.'),
('2TI', 1, 17, '2TI.1.17', 'Indeed, when he arrived in Rome, he searched diligently until he found me.'),
('2TI', 1, 18, '2TI.1.18', 'May the Lord grant Onesiphorus His mercy on that day. You know very well how much he ministered to me in Ephesus.'),
('2TI', 2, 1, '2TI.2.1', 'You therefore, my child, be strong in the grace that is in Christ Jesus.'),
('2TI', 2, 2, '2TI.2.2', 'And the things that you have heard me say among many witnesses, entrust these to faithful men who will be qualified to teach others as well.'),
('2TI', 2, 3, '2TI.2.3', 'Join me in suffering, like a good soldier of Christ Jesus.'),
('2TI', 2, 4, '2TI.2.4', 'A soldier refrains from entangling himself in civilian affairs, in order to please the one who enlisted him.'),
('2TI', 2, 5, '2TI.2.5', 'Likewise, a competitor does not receive the crown unless he competes according to the rules.'),
('2TI', 2, 6, '2TI.2.6', 'The hardworking farmer should be the first to partake of the crops.'),
('2TI', 2, 7, '2TI.2.7', 'Consider what I am saying, for the Lord will give you insight into all things.'),
('2TI', 2, 8, '2TI.2.8', 'Remember Jesus Christ, raised from the dead, descended from David, as proclaimed by my gospel,'),
('2TI', 2, 9, '2TI.2.9', 'for which I suffer to the extent of being chained like a criminal. But the word of God cannot be chained!'),
('2TI', 2, 10, '2TI.2.10', 'For this reason I endure all things for the sake of the elect, so that they too may obtain the salvation that is in Christ Jesus, with eternal glory.'),
('2TI', 2, 11, '2TI.2.11', 'This is a trustworthy saying: If we died with Him, we will also live with Him;'),
('2TI', 2, 12, '2TI.2.12', 'if we endure, we will also reign with Him; if we deny Him, He will also deny us;'),
('2TI', 2, 13, '2TI.2.13', 'if we are faithless, He remains faithful, for He cannot deny Himself.'),
('2TI', 2, 14, '2TI.2.14', 'Remind the believers of these things, charging them before God to avoid quarreling over words, which succeeds only in leading the listeners to ruin.'),
('2TI', 2, 15, '2TI.2.15', 'Make every effort to present yourself approved to God, an unashamed workman who accurately handles the word of truth.'),
('2TI', 2, 16, '2TI.2.16', 'But avoid irreverent, empty chatter, which will only lead to more ungodliness,'),
('2TI', 2, 17, '2TI.2.17', 'and the talk of such men will spread like gangrene. Among them are Hymenaeus and Philetus,'),
('2TI', 2, 18, '2TI.2.18', 'who have deviated from the truth. They say that the resurrection has already occurred, and they undermine the faith of some.'),
('2TI', 2, 19, '2TI.2.19', 'Nevertheless, God’s firm foundation stands, bearing this seal: “The Lord knows those who are His,” and, “Everyone who calls on the name of the Lord must turn away from iniquity.”'),
('2TI', 2, 20, '2TI.2.20', 'A large house contains not only vessels of gold and silver, but also of wood and clay. Some indeed are for honorable use, but others are for common use.'),
('2TI', 2, 21, '2TI.2.21', 'So if anyone cleanses himself of what is unfit, he will be a vessel for honor: sanctified, useful to the Master, and prepared for every good work.'),
('2TI', 2, 22, '2TI.2.22', 'Flee from youthful passions and pursue righteousness, faith, love, and peace, together with those who call on the Lord out of a pure heart.'),
('2TI', 2, 23, '2TI.2.23', 'But reject foolish and ignorant speculation, for you know that it breeds quarreling.'),
('2TI', 2, 24, '2TI.2.24', 'And a servant of the Lord must not be quarrelsome, but must be kind to everyone, able to teach, and forbearing.'),
('2TI', 2, 25, '2TI.2.25', 'He must gently reprove those who oppose him, in the hope that God may grant them repentance leading to a knowledge of the truth.'),
('2TI', 2, 26, '2TI.2.26', 'Then they will come to their senses and escape the snare of the devil, who has taken them captive to his will.'),
('2TI', 3, 1, '2TI.3.1', 'But understand this: In the last days terrible times will come.'),
('2TI', 3, 2, '2TI.3.2', 'For men will be lovers of themselves, lovers of money, boastful, arrogant, abusive, disobedient to their parents, ungrateful, unholy,'),
('2TI', 3, 3, '2TI.3.3', 'unloving, unforgiving, slanderous, without self-control, brutal, without love of good,'),
('2TI', 3, 4, '2TI.3.4', 'traitorous, reckless, conceited, lovers of pleasure rather than lovers of God,'),
('2TI', 3, 5, '2TI.3.5', 'having a form of godliness but denying its power. Turn away from such as these!'),
('2TI', 3, 6, '2TI.3.6', 'They are the kind who worm their way into households and captivate vulnerable women who are weighed down with sins and led astray by various passions,'),
('2TI', 3, 7, '2TI.3.7', 'who are always learning but never able to come to a knowledge of the truth.'),
('2TI', 3, 8, '2TI.3.8', 'Just as Jannes and Jambres opposed Moses, so also these men oppose the truth. They are depraved in mind and disqualified from the faith.'),
('2TI', 3, 9, '2TI.3.9', 'But they will not advance much further. For just like Jannes and Jambres, their folly will be plain to everyone.'),
('2TI', 3, 10, '2TI.3.10', 'You, however, have observed my teaching, my conduct, my purpose, my faith, my patience, my love, my perseverance,'),
('2TI', 3, 11, '2TI.3.11', 'my persecutions, and the sufferings that came upon me in Antioch, Iconium, and Lystra. What persecutions I endured! Yet the Lord rescued me from all of them.'),
('2TI', 3, 12, '2TI.3.12', 'Indeed, all who desire to live godly lives in Christ Jesus will be persecuted,'),
('2TI', 3, 13, '2TI.3.13', 'while evil men and imposters go from bad to worse, deceiving and being deceived.'),
('2TI', 3, 14, '2TI.3.14', 'But as for you, continue in the things you have learned and firmly believed, since you know from whom you have learned them.'),
('2TI', 3, 15, '2TI.3.15', 'From infancy you have known the Holy Scriptures, which are able to make you wise for salvation through faith in Christ Jesus.'),
('2TI', 3, 16, '2TI.3.16', 'All Scripture is God-breathed and is useful for instruction, for conviction, for correction, and for training in righteousness,'),
('2TI', 3, 17, '2TI.3.17', 'so that the man of God may be complete, fully equipped for every good work.'),
('2TI', 4, 1, '2TI.4.1', 'I charge you in the presence of God and of Christ Jesus, who will judge the living and the dead, and in view of His appearing and His kingdom:'),
('2TI', 4, 2, '2TI.4.2', 'Preach the word; be prepared in season and out of season; reprove, rebuke, and encourage with every form of patient instruction.'),
('2TI', 4, 3, '2TI.4.3', 'For the time will come when men will not tolerate sound doctrine, but with itching ears they will gather around themselves teachers to suit their own desires.'),
('2TI', 4, 4, '2TI.4.4', 'So they will turn their ears away from the truth and turn aside to myths.'),
('2TI', 4, 5, '2TI.4.5', 'But you, be sober in all things, endure hardship, do the work of an evangelist, fulfill your ministry.'),
('2TI', 4, 6, '2TI.4.6', 'For I am already being poured out like a drink offering, and the time of my departure is at hand.'),
('2TI', 4, 7, '2TI.4.7', 'I have fought the good fight, I have finished the race, I have kept the faith.'),
('2TI', 4, 8, '2TI.4.8', 'From now on there is laid up for me the crown of righteousness, which the Lord, the righteous Judge, will award to me on that day—and not only to me, but to all who crave His appearing.'),
('2TI', 4, 9, '2TI.4.9', 'Make every effort to come to me quickly,'),
('2TI', 4, 10, '2TI.4.10', 'because Demas, in his love of this world, has deserted me and gone to Thessalonica. Crescens has gone to Galatia, and Titus to Dalmatia.'),
('2TI', 4, 11, '2TI.4.11', 'Only Luke is with me. Get Mark and bring him with you, because he is useful to me in the ministry.'),
('2TI', 4, 12, '2TI.4.12', 'Tychicus, however, I have sent to Ephesus.'),
('2TI', 4, 13, '2TI.4.13', 'When you come, bring the cloak that I left with Carpus at Troas, and my scrolls, especially the parchments.'),
('2TI', 4, 14, '2TI.4.14', 'Alexander the coppersmith did great harm to me. The Lord will repay him according to his deeds.'),
('2TI', 4, 15, '2TI.4.15', 'You too should beware of him, for he has vigorously opposed our message.'),
('2TI', 4, 16, '2TI.4.16', 'At my first defense, no one stood with me, but everyone deserted me. May it not be charged against them.'),
('2TI', 4, 17, '2TI.4.17', 'But the Lord stood by me and strengthened me, so that through me the message would be fully proclaimed, and all the Gentiles would hear it. So I was delivered from the mouth of the lion.'),
('2TI', 4, 18, '2TI.4.18', 'And the Lord will rescue me from every evil action and bring me safely into His heavenly kingdom. To Him be the glory forever and ever. Amen.'),
('2TI', 4, 19, '2TI.4.19', 'Greet Prisca and Aquila, as well as the household of Onesiphorus.'),
('2TI', 4, 20, '2TI.4.20', 'Erastus has remained at Corinth, and Trophimus I left sick in Miletus.'),
('2TI', 4, 21, '2TI.4.21', 'Make every effort to come to me before winter. Eubulus sends you greetings, as do Pudens, Linus, Claudia, and all the brothers.'),
('2TI', 4, 22, '2TI.4.22', 'The Lord be with your spirit. Grace be with you all.'),
('TIT', 1, 1, 'TIT.1.1', 'Paul, a servant of God and an apostle of Jesus Christ for the faith of God’s elect and their knowledge of the truth that leads to godliness,'),
('TIT', 1, 2, 'TIT.1.2', 'in the hope of eternal life, which God, who cannot lie, promised before time began.'),
('TIT', 1, 3, 'TIT.1.3', 'In His own time He has made His word evident in the proclamation entrusted to me by the command of God our Savior.'),
('TIT', 1, 4, 'TIT.1.4', 'To Titus, my true child in our common faith: Grace and peace from God the Father and Christ Jesus our Savior.'),
('TIT', 1, 5, 'TIT.1.5', 'The reason I left you in Crete was that you would set in order what was unfinished and appoint elders in every town, as I directed you.'),
('TIT', 1, 6, 'TIT.1.6', 'An elder must be blameless, the husband of but one wife, having children who are believers and who are not open to accusation of indiscretion or insubordination.'),
('TIT', 1, 7, 'TIT.1.7', 'As God’s steward, an overseer must be above reproach—not self-willed, not quick-tempered, not given to drunkenness, not violent, not greedy for money.'),
('TIT', 1, 8, 'TIT.1.8', 'Instead, he must be hospitable, a lover of good, self-controlled, upright, holy, and disciplined.'),
('TIT', 1, 9, 'TIT.1.9', 'He must hold firmly to the faithful word as it was taught, so that he can encourage others by sound teaching and refute those who contradict it.'),
('TIT', 1, 10, 'TIT.1.10', 'For many are rebellious and full of empty talk and deception, especially those of the circumcision,'),
('TIT', 1, 11, 'TIT.1.11', 'who must be silenced. For the sake of dishonorable gain, they undermine entire households and teach things they should not.'),
('TIT', 1, 12, 'TIT.1.12', 'As one of their own prophets has said, “Cretans are always liars, evil beasts, lazy gluttons.”'),
('TIT', 1, 13, 'TIT.1.13', 'This testimony is true. Therefore rebuke them sternly, so that they will be sound in the faith'),
('TIT', 1, 14, 'TIT.1.14', 'and will pay no attention to Jewish myths or to the commands of men who have rejected the truth.'),
('TIT', 1, 15, 'TIT.1.15', 'To the pure, all things are pure; but to the defiled and unbelieving, nothing is pure. Indeed, both their minds and their consciences are defiled.'),
('TIT', 1, 16, 'TIT.1.16', 'They profess to know God, but by their actions they deny Him. They are detestable, disobedient, and unfit for any good deed.'),
('TIT', 2, 1, 'TIT.2.1', 'But as for you, speak the things that are consistent with sound doctrine.'),
('TIT', 2, 2, 'TIT.2.2', 'Older men are to be temperate, dignified, self-controlled, and sound in faith, love, and perseverance.'),
('TIT', 2, 3, 'TIT.2.3', 'Older women, likewise, are to be reverent in their behavior, not slanderers or addicted to much wine, but teachers of good.'),
('TIT', 2, 4, 'TIT.2.4', 'In this way they can train the young women to love their husbands and children,'),
('TIT', 2, 5, 'TIT.2.5', 'to be self-controlled, pure, managers of their households, kind, and submissive to their own husbands, so that the word of God will not be discredited.'),
('TIT', 2, 6, 'TIT.2.6', 'In the same way, urge the younger men to be self-controlled.'),
('TIT', 2, 7, 'TIT.2.7', 'In everything, show yourself to be an example by doing good works. In your teaching show integrity, dignity,'),
('TIT', 2, 8, 'TIT.2.8', 'and wholesome speech that is above reproach, so that anyone who opposes us will be ashamed, having nothing bad to say about us.'),
('TIT', 2, 9, 'TIT.2.9', 'Slaves are to submit to their own masters in everything, to be well-pleasing, not argumentative,'),
('TIT', 2, 10, 'TIT.2.10', 'not stealing from them, but showing all good faith, so that in every respect they will adorn the teaching about God our Savior.'),
('TIT', 2, 11, 'TIT.2.11', 'For the grace of God has appeared, bringing salvation to everyone.'),
('TIT', 2, 12, 'TIT.2.12', 'It instructs us to renounce ungodliness and worldly passions, and to live sensible, upright, and godly lives in the present age,'),
('TIT', 2, 13, 'TIT.2.13', 'as we await the blessed hope and glorious appearance of our great God and Savior Jesus Christ.'),
('TIT', 2, 14, 'TIT.2.14', 'He gave Himself for us to redeem us from all lawlessness and to purify for Himself a people for His own possession, zealous for good deeds.'),
('TIT', 2, 15, 'TIT.2.15', 'Speak these things as you encourage and rebuke with all authority. Let no one despise you.'),
('TIT', 3, 1, 'TIT.3.1', 'Remind the believers to submit to rulers and authorities, to be obedient and ready for every good work,'),
('TIT', 3, 2, 'TIT.3.2', 'to malign no one, and to be peaceable and gentle, showing full consideration to everyone.'),
('TIT', 3, 3, 'TIT.3.3', 'For at one time we too were foolish, disobedient, misled, and enslaved to all sorts of desires and pleasures—living in malice and envy, being hated and hating one another.'),
('TIT', 3, 4, 'TIT.3.4', 'But when the kindness of God our Savior and His love for mankind appeared,'),
('TIT', 3, 5, 'TIT.3.5', 'He saved us, not by the righteous deeds we had done, but according to His mercy, through the washing of new birth and renewal by the Holy Spirit.'),
('TIT', 3, 6, 'TIT.3.6', 'This is the Spirit He poured out on us abundantly through Jesus Christ our Savior,'),
('TIT', 3, 7, 'TIT.3.7', 'so that, having been justified by His grace, we would become heirs with the hope of eternal life.'),
('TIT', 3, 8, 'TIT.3.8', 'This saying is trustworthy. And I want you to emphasize these things, so that those who have believed God will take care to devote themselves to good deeds. These things are excellent and profitable for the people.'),
('TIT', 3, 9, 'TIT.3.9', 'But avoid foolish controversies, genealogies, arguments, and quarrels about the law, because these things are pointless and worthless.'),
('TIT', 3, 10, 'TIT.3.10', 'Reject a divisive man after a first and second admonition,'),
('TIT', 3, 11, 'TIT.3.11', 'knowing that such a man is corrupt and sinful; he is self-condemned.'),
('TIT', 3, 12, 'TIT.3.12', 'As soon as I send Artemas or Tychicus to you, make every effort to come to me at Nicopolis, because I have decided to winter there.'),
('TIT', 3, 13, 'TIT.3.13', 'Do your best to equip Zenas the lawyer and Apollos, so that they will have everything they need.'),
('TIT', 3, 14, 'TIT.3.14', 'And our people must also learn to devote themselves to good works in order to meet the pressing needs of others, so that they will not be unfruitful.'),
('TIT', 3, 15, 'TIT.3.15', 'All who are with me send you greetings. Greet those who love us in the faith. Grace be with all of you.'),
('PHM', 1, 1, 'PHM.1.1', 'Paul, a prisoner of Christ Jesus, and Timothy our brother, To Philemon our beloved fellow worker,'),
('PHM', 1, 2, 'PHM.1.2', 'to Apphia our sister, to Archippus our fellow soldier, and to the church that meets at your house:'),
('PHM', 1, 3, 'PHM.1.3', 'Grace and peace to you from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.'),
('PHM', 1, 4, 'PHM.1.4', 'I always thank my God, remembering you in my prayers,'),
('PHM', 1, 5, 'PHM.1.5', 'because I hear about your faith in the Lord Jesus and your love for all the saints.'),
('PHM', 1, 6, 'PHM.1.6', 'I pray that your partnership in the faith may become effective as you fully acknowledge every good thing that is ours in Christ.'),
('PHM', 1, 7, 'PHM.1.7', 'I take great joy and encouragement in your love, because you, brother, have refreshed the hearts of the saints.'),
('PHM', 1, 8, 'PHM.1.8', 'So although in Christ I am bold enough to order you to do what is proper,'),
('PHM', 1, 9, 'PHM.1.9', 'I prefer to appeal on the basis of love. For I, Paul, am now aged, and a prisoner of Christ Jesus as well.'),
('PHM', 1, 10, 'PHM.1.10', 'I appeal to you for my child Onesimus, whose father I became while I was in chains.'),
('PHM', 1, 11, 'PHM.1.11', 'Formerly he was useless to you, but now he has become useful both to you and to me.'),
('PHM', 1, 12, 'PHM.1.12', 'I am sending back to you him who is my very heart.'),
('PHM', 1, 13, 'PHM.1.13', 'I would have liked to keep him with me, so that on your behalf he could minister to me in my chains for the gospel.'),
('PHM', 1, 14, 'PHM.1.14', 'But I did not want to do anything without your consent, so that your goodness will not be out of compulsion, but by your own free will.'),
('PHM', 1, 15, 'PHM.1.15', 'For perhaps this is why he was separated from you for a while, so that you might have him back for good—'),
('PHM', 1, 16, 'PHM.1.16', 'no longer as a slave, but better than a slave, as a beloved brother. He is especially beloved to me, but even more so to you, both in person and in the Lord.'),
('PHM', 1, 17, 'PHM.1.17', 'So if you consider me a partner, receive him as you would receive me.'),
('PHM', 1, 18, 'PHM.1.18', 'But if he has wronged you in any way or owes you anything, charge it to my account.'),
('PHM', 1, 19, 'PHM.1.19', 'I, Paul, write this with my own hand. I will repay it—not to mention that you owe me your very self.'),
('PHM', 1, 20, 'PHM.1.20', 'Yes, brother, let me have some benefit from you in the Lord. Refresh my heart in Christ.'),
('PHM', 1, 21, 'PHM.1.21', 'Confident of your obedience, I write to you, knowing that you will do even more than I ask.'),
('PHM', 1, 22, 'PHM.1.22', 'In the meantime, prepare a guest room for me, because I hope that through your prayers I will be restored to you.'),
('PHM', 1, 23, 'PHM.1.23', 'Epaphras, my fellow prisoner in Christ Jesus, sends you greetings,'),
('PHM', 1, 24, 'PHM.1.24', 'as do Mark, Aristarchus, Demas, and Luke, my fellow workers.'),
('PHM', 1, 25, 'PHM.1.25', 'The grace of the Lord Jesus Christ be with your spirit.'),
('HEB', 1, 1, 'HEB.1.1', 'On many past occasions and in many different ways, God spoke to our fathers through the prophets.'),
('HEB', 1, 2, 'HEB.1.2', 'But in these last days He has spoken to us by His Son, whom He appointed heir of all things, and through whom He made the universe.'),
('HEB', 1, 3, 'HEB.1.3', 'The Son is the radiance of God’s glory and the exact representation of His nature, upholding all things by His powerful word. After He had provided purification for sins, He sat down at the right hand of the Majesty on high.'),
('HEB', 1, 4, 'HEB.1.4', 'So He became as far superior to the angels as the name He has inherited is excellent beyond theirs.'),
('HEB', 1, 5, 'HEB.1.5', 'For to which of the angels did God ever say: “You are My Son; today I have become Your Father”? Or again: “I will be His Father, and He will be My Son”?'),
('HEB', 1, 6, 'HEB.1.6', 'And again, when God brings His firstborn into the world, He says: “Let all God’s angels worship Him.”'),
('HEB', 1, 7, 'HEB.1.7', 'Now about the angels He says: “He makes His angels winds, His servants flames of fire.”'),
('HEB', 1, 8, 'HEB.1.8', 'But about the Son He says: “Your throne, O God, endures forever and ever, and justice is the scepter of Your kingdom.'),
('HEB', 1, 9, 'HEB.1.9', 'You have loved righteousness and hated wickedness; therefore God, Your God, has anointed You above Your companions with the oil of joy.”'),
('HEB', 1, 10, 'HEB.1.10', 'And: “In the beginning, O Lord, You laid the foundations of the earth, and the heavens are the work of Your hands.'),
('HEB', 1, 11, 'HEB.1.11', 'They will perish, but You remain; they will all wear out like a garment.'),
('HEB', 1, 12, 'HEB.1.12', 'You will roll them up like a robe; like a garment they will be changed; but You remain the same, and Your years will never end.”'),
('HEB', 1, 13, 'HEB.1.13', 'Yet to which of the angels did God ever say: “Sit at My right hand until I make Your enemies a footstool for Your feet”?'),
('HEB', 1, 14, 'HEB.1.14', 'Are not the angels ministering spirits sent to serve those who will inherit salvation?'),
('HEB', 2, 1, 'HEB.2.1', 'We must pay closer attention, therefore, to what we have heard, so that we do not drift away.'),
('HEB', 2, 2, 'HEB.2.2', 'For if the message spoken by angels was binding, and every transgression and disobedience received its just punishment,'),
('HEB', 2, 3, 'HEB.2.3', 'how shall we escape if we neglect such a great salvation? This salvation was first announced by the Lord, was confirmed to us by those who heard Him,'),
('HEB', 2, 4, 'HEB.2.4', 'and was affirmed by God through signs, wonders, various miracles, and gifts of the Holy Spirit distributed according to His will.'),
('HEB', 2, 5, 'HEB.2.5', 'For it is not to angels that He has subjected the world to come, about which we are speaking.'),
('HEB', 2, 6, 'HEB.2.6', 'But somewhere it is testified in these words: “What is man that You are mindful of him, or the son of man that You care for him?'),
('HEB', 2, 7, 'HEB.2.7', 'You made him a little lower than the angels; You crowned him with glory and honor'),
('HEB', 2, 8, 'HEB.2.8', 'and placed everything under his feet.” When God subjected all things to him, He left nothing outside of his control. Yet at present we do not see everything subject to him.'),
('HEB', 2, 9, 'HEB.2.9', 'But we see Jesus, who was made a little lower than the angels, now crowned with glory and honor because He suffered death, so that by the grace of God He might taste death for everyone.'),
('HEB', 2, 10, 'HEB.2.10', 'In bringing many sons to glory, it was fitting for God, for whom and through whom all things exist, to make the author of their salvation perfect through suffering.'),
('HEB', 2, 11, 'HEB.2.11', 'For both the One who sanctifies and those who are sanctified are of the same family. So Jesus is not ashamed to call them brothers.'),
('HEB', 2, 12, 'HEB.2.12', 'He says: “I will proclaim Your name to My brothers; I will sing Your praises in the assembly.”'),
('HEB', 2, 13, 'HEB.2.13', 'And again: “I will put My trust in Him.” And once again: “Here am I, and the children God has given Me.”'),
('HEB', 2, 14, 'HEB.2.14', 'Now since the children have flesh and blood, He too shared in their humanity, so that by His death He might destroy him who holds the power of death, that is, the devil,'),
('HEB', 2, 15, 'HEB.2.15', 'and free those who all their lives were held in slavery by their fear of death.'),
('HEB', 2, 16, 'HEB.2.16', 'For surely it is not the angels He helps, but the descendants of Abraham.'),
('HEB', 2, 17, 'HEB.2.17', 'For this reason He had to be made like His brothers in every way, so that He might become a merciful and faithful high priest in service to God, in order to make atonement for the sins of the people.'),
('HEB', 2, 18, 'HEB.2.18', 'Because He Himself suffered when He was tempted, He is able to help those who are being tempted.'),
('HEB', 3, 1, 'HEB.3.1', 'Therefore, holy brothers, who share in the heavenly calling, set your focus on Jesus, the apostle and high priest whom we confess.'),
('HEB', 3, 2, 'HEB.3.2', 'He was faithful to the One who appointed Him, just as Moses was faithful in all God’s house.'),
('HEB', 3, 3, 'HEB.3.3', 'For Jesus has been counted worthy of greater glory than Moses, just as the builder of a house has greater honor than the house itself.'),
('HEB', 3, 4, 'HEB.3.4', 'And every house is built by someone, but God is the builder of everything.'),
('HEB', 3, 5, 'HEB.3.5', 'Now Moses was faithful as a servant in all God’s house, testifying to what would be spoken later.'),
('HEB', 3, 6, 'HEB.3.6', 'But Christ is faithful as the Son over God’s house. And we are His house, if we hold firmly to our confidence and the hope of which we boast.'),
('HEB', 3, 7, 'HEB.3.7', 'Therefore, as the Holy Spirit says: “Today, if you hear His voice,'),
('HEB', 3, 8, 'HEB.3.8', 'do not harden your hearts, as you did in the rebellion, in the day of testing in the wilderness,'),
('HEB', 3, 9, 'HEB.3.9', 'where your fathers tested and tried Me, and for forty years saw My works.'),
('HEB', 3, 10, 'HEB.3.10', 'Therefore I was angry with that generation, and I said, ‘Their hearts are always going astray, and they have not known My ways.’'),
('HEB', 3, 11, 'HEB.3.11', 'So I swore on oath in My anger, ‘They shall never enter My rest.’”'),
('HEB', 3, 12, 'HEB.3.12', 'See to it, brothers, that none of you has a wicked heart of unbelief that turns away from the living God.'),
('HEB', 3, 13, 'HEB.3.13', 'But exhort one another daily, as long as it is called today, so that none of you may be hardened by sin’s deceitfulness.'),
('HEB', 3, 14, 'HEB.3.14', 'We have come to share in Christ if we hold firmly to the end the assurance we had at first.'),
('HEB', 3, 15, 'HEB.3.15', 'As it has been said: “Today, if you hear His voice, do not harden your hearts, as you did in the rebellion.”'),
('HEB', 3, 16, 'HEB.3.16', 'For who were the ones who heard and rebelled? Were they not all those Moses led out of Egypt?'),
('HEB', 3, 17, 'HEB.3.17', 'And with whom was God angry for forty years? Was it not with those who sinned, whose bodies fell in the wilderness?'),
('HEB', 3, 18, 'HEB.3.18', 'And to whom did He swear that they would never enter His rest? Was it not to those who disobeyed?'),
('HEB', 3, 19, 'HEB.3.19', 'So we see that it was because of their unbelief that they were unable to enter.'),
('HEB', 4, 1, 'HEB.4.1', 'Therefore, while the promise of entering His rest still stands, let us be careful that none of you be deemed to have fallen short of it.'),
('HEB', 4, 2, 'HEB.4.2', 'For we also received the good news just as they did; but the message they heard was of no value to them, since they did not share the faith of those who comprehended it.'),
('HEB', 4, 3, 'HEB.4.3', 'Now we who have believed enter that rest. As for the others, it is just as God has said: “So I swore on oath in My anger, ‘They shall never enter My rest.’” And yet His works have been finished since the foundation of the world.'),
('HEB', 4, 4, 'HEB.4.4', 'For somewhere He has spoken about the seventh day in this manner: “And on the seventh day God rested from all His works.”'),
('HEB', 4, 5, 'HEB.4.5', 'And again, as He says in the passage above: “They shall never enter My rest.”'),
('HEB', 4, 6, 'HEB.4.6', 'Since, then, it remains for some to enter His rest, and since those who formerly heard the good news did not enter because of their disobedience,'),
('HEB', 4, 7, 'HEB.4.7', 'God again designated a certain day as “Today,” when a long time later He spoke through David as was just stated: “Today, if you hear His voice, do not harden your hearts.”'),
('HEB', 4, 8, 'HEB.4.8', 'For if Joshua had given them rest, God would not have spoken later about another day.'),
('HEB', 4, 9, 'HEB.4.9', 'There remains, then, a Sabbath rest for the people of God.'),
('HEB', 4, 10, 'HEB.4.10', 'For whoever enters God’s rest also rests from his own work, just as God did from His.'),
('HEB', 4, 11, 'HEB.4.11', 'Let us, therefore, make every effort to enter that rest, so that no one will fall by following the same pattern of disobedience.'),
('HEB', 4, 12, 'HEB.4.12', 'For the word of God is living and active. Sharper than any double-edged sword, it pierces even to dividing soul and spirit, joints and marrow. It judges the thoughts and intentions of the heart.'),
('HEB', 4, 13, 'HEB.4.13', 'Nothing in all creation is hidden from God’s sight; everything is uncovered and exposed before the eyes of Him to whom we must give account.'),
('HEB', 4, 14, 'HEB.4.14', 'Therefore, since we have a great high priest who has passed through the heavens, Jesus the Son of God, let us hold firmly to what we profess.'),
('HEB', 4, 15, 'HEB.4.15', 'For we do not have a high priest who is unable to sympathize with our weaknesses, but we have one who was tempted in every way that we are, yet was without sin.'),
('HEB', 4, 16, 'HEB.4.16', 'Let us then approach the throne of grace with confidence, so that we may receive mercy and find grace to help us in our time of need.'),
('HEB', 5, 1, 'HEB.5.1', 'Every high priest is appointed from among men to represent them in matters relating to God, to offer gifts and sacrifices for sins.'),
('HEB', 5, 2, 'HEB.5.2', 'He is able to deal gently with those who are ignorant and misguided, since he himself is subject to weakness.'),
('HEB', 5, 3, 'HEB.5.3', 'That is why he is obligated to offer sacrifices for his own sins, as well as for the sins of the people.'),
('HEB', 5, 4, 'HEB.5.4', 'No one takes this honor upon himself; he must be called by God, just as Aaron was.'),
('HEB', 5, 5, 'HEB.5.5', 'So also Christ did not take upon Himself the glory of becoming a high priest, but He was called by the One who said to Him: “You are My Son; today I have become Your Father.”'),
('HEB', 5, 6, 'HEB.5.6', 'And in another passage God says: “You are a priest forever in the order of Melchizedek.”'),
('HEB', 5, 7, 'HEB.5.7', 'During the days of Jesus’ earthly life, He offered up prayers and petitions with loud cries and tears to the One who could save Him from death, and He was heard because of His reverence.'),
('HEB', 5, 8, 'HEB.5.8', 'Although He was a Son, He learned obedience from what He suffered.'),
('HEB', 5, 9, 'HEB.5.9', 'And having been made perfect, He became the source of eternal salvation to all who obey Him'),
('HEB', 5, 10, 'HEB.5.10', 'and was designated by God as high priest in the order of Melchizedek.'),
('HEB', 5, 11, 'HEB.5.11', 'We have much to say about this, but it is hard to explain, because you are dull of hearing.'),
('HEB', 5, 12, 'HEB.5.12', 'Although by this time you ought to be teachers, you need someone to reteach you the basic principles of God’s word. You need milk, not solid food!'),
('HEB', 5, 13, 'HEB.5.13', 'For everyone who lives on milk is still an infant, inexperienced in the message of righteousness.'),
('HEB', 5, 14, 'HEB.5.14', 'But solid food is for the mature, who by constant use have trained their senses to distinguish good from evil.'),
('HEB', 6, 1, 'HEB.6.1', 'Therefore let us leave the elementary teachings about Christ and go on to maturity, not laying again the foundation of repentance from dead works, and of faith in God,'),
('HEB', 6, 2, 'HEB.6.2', 'instruction about baptisms, the laying on of hands, the resurrection of the dead, and eternal judgment.'),
('HEB', 6, 3, 'HEB.6.3', 'And this we will do, if God permits.'),
('HEB', 6, 4, 'HEB.6.4', 'It is impossible for those who have once been enlightened, who have tasted the heavenly gift, who have shared in the Holy Spirit,'),
('HEB', 6, 5, 'HEB.6.5', 'who have tasted the goodness of the word of God and the powers of the coming age—'),
('HEB', 6, 6, 'HEB.6.6', 'and then have fallen away—to be restored to repentance, because they themselves are crucifying the Son of God all over again and subjecting Him to open shame.'),
('HEB', 6, 7, 'HEB.6.7', 'For land that drinks in the rain often falling on it and that produces a crop useful to those for whom it is tended receives the blessing of God.'),
('HEB', 6, 8, 'HEB.6.8', 'But land that produces thorns and thistles is worthless, and its curse is imminent. In the end it will be burned.'),
('HEB', 6, 9, 'HEB.6.9', 'Even though we speak like this, beloved, we are convinced of better things in your case—things that accompany salvation.'),
('HEB', 6, 10, 'HEB.6.10', 'For God is not unjust. He will not forget your work and the love you have shown for His name as you have ministered to the saints and continue to do so.'),
('HEB', 6, 11, 'HEB.6.11', 'We want each of you to show this same diligence to the very end, in order to make your hope sure.'),
('HEB', 6, 12, 'HEB.6.12', 'Then you will not be sluggish, but will imitate those who through faith and patience inherit what has been promised.'),
('HEB', 6, 13, 'HEB.6.13', 'When God made His promise to Abraham, since He had no one greater to swear by, He swore by Himself,'),
('HEB', 6, 14, 'HEB.6.14', 'saying, “I will surely bless you and multiply your descendants.”'),
('HEB', 6, 15, 'HEB.6.15', 'And so Abraham, after waiting patiently, obtained the promise.'),
('HEB', 6, 16, 'HEB.6.16', 'Men swear by someone greater than themselves, and their oath serves as a confirmation to end all argument.'),
('HEB', 6, 17, 'HEB.6.17', 'So when God wanted to make the unchanging nature of His purpose very clear to the heirs of the promise, He guaranteed it with an oath.'),
('HEB', 6, 18, 'HEB.6.18', 'Thus by two unchangeable things in which it is impossible for God to lie, we who have fled to take hold of the hope set before us may be strongly encouraged.'),
('HEB', 6, 19, 'HEB.6.19', 'We have this hope as an anchor for the soul, firm and secure. It enters the inner sanctuary behind the curtain,'),
('HEB', 6, 20, 'HEB.6.20', 'where Jesus our forerunner has entered on our behalf. He has become a high priest forever in the order of Melchizedek.'),
('HEB', 7, 1, 'HEB.7.1', 'This Melchizedek was king of Salem and priest of God Most High. He met Abraham returning from the slaughter of the kings and blessed him,'),
('HEB', 7, 2, 'HEB.7.2', 'and Abraham apportioned to him a tenth of everything. First, his name means “king of righteousness.” Then also, “king of Salem” means “king of peace.”'),
('HEB', 7, 3, 'HEB.7.3', 'Without father or mother or genealogy, without beginning of days or end of life, like the Son of God, he remains a priest for all time.'),
('HEB', 7, 4, 'HEB.7.4', 'Consider how great Melchizedek was: Even the patriarch Abraham gave him a tenth of the plunder.'),
('HEB', 7, 5, 'HEB.7.5', 'Now the law commands the sons of Levi who become priests to collect a tenth from the people—that is, from their brothers—though they too are descended from Abraham.'),
('HEB', 7, 6, 'HEB.7.6', 'But Melchizedek, who did not trace his descent from Levi, collected a tenth from Abraham and blessed him who had the promises.'),
('HEB', 7, 7, 'HEB.7.7', 'And indisputably, the lesser is blessed by the greater.'),
('HEB', 7, 8, 'HEB.7.8', 'In the case of the Levites, mortal men collect the tenth; but in the case of Melchizedek, it is affirmed that he lives on.'),
('HEB', 7, 9, 'HEB.7.9', 'And so to speak, Levi, who collects the tenth, paid the tenth through Abraham.'),
('HEB', 7, 10, 'HEB.7.10', 'For when Melchizedek met Abraham, Levi was still in the loin of his ancestor.'),
('HEB', 7, 11, 'HEB.7.11', 'Now if perfection could have been attained through the Levitical priesthood (for on this basis the people received the law), why was there still need for another priest to appear—one in the order of Melchizedek and not in the order of Aaron?'),
('HEB', 7, 12, 'HEB.7.12', 'For when the priesthood is changed, the law must be changed as well.'),
('HEB', 7, 13, 'HEB.7.13', 'He of whom these things are said belonged to a different tribe, from which no one has ever served at the altar.'),
('HEB', 7, 14, 'HEB.7.14', 'For it is clear that our Lord descended from Judah, a tribe as to which Moses said nothing about priests.'),
('HEB', 7, 15, 'HEB.7.15', 'And this point is even more clear if another priest like Melchizedek appears,'),
('HEB', 7, 16, 'HEB.7.16', 'one who has become a priest not by a law of succession, but by the power of an indestructible life.'),
('HEB', 7, 17, 'HEB.7.17', 'For it is testified: “You are a priest forever in the order of Melchizedek.”'),
('HEB', 7, 18, 'HEB.7.18', 'So the former commandment is set aside because it was weak and useless'),
('HEB', 7, 19, 'HEB.7.19', '(for the law made nothing perfect), and a better hope is introduced, by which we draw near to God.'),
('HEB', 7, 20, 'HEB.7.20', 'And none of this happened without an oath. For others became priests without an oath,'),
('HEB', 7, 21, 'HEB.7.21', 'but Jesus became a priest with an oath by the One who said to Him: “The Lord has sworn and will not change His mind: ‘You are a priest forever.’”'),
('HEB', 7, 22, 'HEB.7.22', 'Because of this oath, Jesus has become the guarantee of a better covenant.'),
('HEB', 7, 23, 'HEB.7.23', 'Now there have been many other priests, since death prevented them from continuing in office.'),
('HEB', 7, 24, 'HEB.7.24', 'But because Jesus lives forever, He has a permanent priesthood.'),
('HEB', 7, 25, 'HEB.7.25', 'Therefore He is able to save completely those who draw near to God through Him, since He always lives to intercede for them.'),
('HEB', 7, 26, 'HEB.7.26', 'Such a high priest truly befits us—One who is holy, innocent, undefiled, set apart from sinners, and exalted above the heavens.'),
('HEB', 7, 27, 'HEB.7.27', 'Unlike the other high priests, He does not need to offer daily sacrifices, first for His own sins and then for the sins of the people; He sacrificed for sin once for all when He offered up Himself.'),
('HEB', 7, 28, 'HEB.7.28', 'For the law appoints as high priests men who are weak; but the oath, which came after the law, appointed the Son, who has been made perfect forever.'),
('HEB', 8, 1, 'HEB.8.1', 'The point of what we are saying is this: We do have such a high priest, who sat down at the right hand of the throne of the Majesty in heaven,'),
('HEB', 8, 2, 'HEB.8.2', 'and who ministers in the sanctuary and true tabernacle set up by the Lord, not by man.'),
('HEB', 8, 3, 'HEB.8.3', 'And since every high priest is appointed to offer both gifts and sacrifices, it was necessary for this One also to have something to offer.'),
('HEB', 8, 4, 'HEB.8.4', 'Now if He were on earth, He would not be a priest, since there are already priests who offer gifts according to the law.'),
('HEB', 8, 5, 'HEB.8.5', 'The place where they serve is a copy and shadow of what is in heaven. This is why Moses was warned when he was about to build the tabernacle: “See to it that you make everything according to the pattern shown you on the mountain.”'),
('HEB', 8, 6, 'HEB.8.6', 'Now, however, Jesus has received a much more excellent ministry, just as the covenant He mediates is better and is founded on better promises.'),
('HEB', 8, 7, 'HEB.8.7', 'For if that first covenant had been without fault, no place would have been sought for a second.'),
('HEB', 8, 8, 'HEB.8.8', 'But God found fault with the people and said: “Behold, the days are coming, declares the Lord, when I will make a new covenant with the house of Israel and with the house of Judah.'),
('HEB', 8, 9, 'HEB.8.9', 'It will not be like the covenant I made with their fathers when I took them by the hand to lead them out of the land of Egypt, because they did not abide by My covenant, and I disregarded them, declares the Lord.'),
('HEB', 8, 10, 'HEB.8.10', 'For this is the covenant I will make with the house of Israel after those days, declares the Lord. I will put My laws in their minds and inscribe them on their hearts. And I will be their God, and they will be My people.'),
('HEB', 8, 11, 'HEB.8.11', 'No longer will each one teach his neighbor or his brother, saying, ‘Know the Lord,’ because they will all know Me, from the least of them to the greatest.'),
('HEB', 8, 12, 'HEB.8.12', 'For I will forgive their iniquities and will remember their sins no more.”'),
('HEB', 8, 13, 'HEB.8.13', 'By speaking of a new covenant, He has made the first one obsolete; and what is obsolete and aging will soon disappear.'),
('HEB', 9, 1, 'HEB.9.1', 'Now the first covenant had regulations for worship and also an earthly sanctuary.'),
('HEB', 9, 2, 'HEB.9.2', 'A tabernacle was prepared. In its first room were the lampstand, the table, and the consecrated bread. This was called the Holy Place.'),
('HEB', 9, 3, 'HEB.9.3', 'Behind the second curtain was a room called the Most Holy Place,'),
('HEB', 9, 4, 'HEB.9.4', 'containing the golden altar of incense and the gold-covered ark of the covenant. Inside the ark were the gold jar of manna, Aaron’s staff that had budded, and the stone tablets of the covenant.'),
('HEB', 9, 5, 'HEB.9.5', 'Above the ark were the cherubim of glory, overshadowing the mercy seat. But we cannot discuss these things in detail now.'),
('HEB', 9, 6, 'HEB.9.6', 'When everything had been prepared in this way, the priests entered regularly into the first room to perform their sacred duties.'),
('HEB', 9, 7, 'HEB.9.7', 'But only the high priest entered the second room, and then only once a year, and never without blood, which he offered for himself and for the sins the people had committed in ignorance.'),
('HEB', 9, 8, 'HEB.9.8', 'By this arrangement the Holy Spirit was showing that the way into the Most Holy Place had not yet been disclosed as long as the first tabernacle was still standing.'),
('HEB', 9, 9, 'HEB.9.9', 'It is an illustration for the present time, because the gifts and sacrifices being offered were unable to cleanse the conscience of the worshiper.'),
('HEB', 9, 10, 'HEB.9.10', 'They consist only in food and drink and special washings—external regulations imposed until the time of reform.'),
('HEB', 9, 11, 'HEB.9.11', 'But when Christ came as high priest of the good things that have come, He went through the greater and more perfect tabernacle that is not made by hands and is not a part of this creation.'),
('HEB', 9, 12, 'HEB.9.12', 'He did not enter by the blood of goats and calves, but He entered the Most Holy Place once for all by His own blood, thus securing eternal redemption.'),
('HEB', 9, 13, 'HEB.9.13', 'For if the blood of goats and bulls and the ashes of a heifer sprinkled on those who are ceremonially unclean sanctify them so that their bodies are clean,'),
('HEB', 9, 14, 'HEB.9.14', 'how much more will the blood of Christ, who through the eternal Spirit offered Himself unblemished to God, purify our consciences from works of death, so that we may serve the living God!'),
('HEB', 9, 15, 'HEB.9.15', 'Therefore Christ is the mediator of a new covenant, so that those who are called may receive the promised eternal inheritance, now that He has died to redeem them from the transgressions committed under the first covenant.'),
('HEB', 9, 16, 'HEB.9.16', 'In the case of a will, it is necessary to establish the death of the one who made it,'),
('HEB', 9, 17, 'HEB.9.17', 'because a will does not take effect until the one who made it has died; it cannot be executed while he is still alive.'),
('HEB', 9, 18, 'HEB.9.18', 'That is why even the first covenant was not put into effect without blood.'),
('HEB', 9, 19, 'HEB.9.19', 'For when Moses had proclaimed every commandment of the law to all the people, he took the blood of calves and goats, along with water, scarlet wool, and hyssop, and sprinkled the scroll and all the people,'),
('HEB', 9, 20, 'HEB.9.20', 'saying, “This is the blood of the covenant, which God has commanded you to keep.”'),
('HEB', 9, 21, 'HEB.9.21', 'In the same way, he sprinkled with blood the tabernacle and all the vessels used in worship.'),
('HEB', 9, 22, 'HEB.9.22', 'According to the law, in fact, nearly everything must be purified with blood, and without the shedding of blood there is no forgiveness.'),
('HEB', 9, 23, 'HEB.9.23', 'So it was necessary for the copies of the heavenly things to be purified with these sacrifices, but the heavenly things themselves with better sacrifices than these.'),
('HEB', 9, 24, 'HEB.9.24', 'For Christ did not enter a man-made copy of the true sanctuary, but He entered heaven itself, now to appear on our behalf in the presence of God.'),
('HEB', 9, 25, 'HEB.9.25', 'Nor did He enter heaven to offer Himself again and again, as the high priest enters the Most Holy Place every year with blood that is not his own.'),
('HEB', 9, 26, 'HEB.9.26', 'Otherwise, Christ would have had to suffer repeatedly since the foundation of the world. But now He has appeared once for all at the end of the ages to do away with sin by the sacrifice of Himself.'),
('HEB', 9, 27, 'HEB.9.27', 'Just as man is appointed to die once, and after that to face judgment,'),
('HEB', 9, 28, 'HEB.9.28', 'so also Christ was offered once to bear the sins of many; and He will appear a second time, not to bear sin, but to bring salvation to those who eagerly await Him.'),
('HEB', 10, 1, 'HEB.10.1', 'For the law is only a shadow of the good things to come, not the realities themselves. It can never, by the same sacrifices offered year after year, make perfect those who draw near to worship.'),
('HEB', 10, 2, 'HEB.10.2', 'If it could, would not the offerings have ceased? For the worshipers would have been cleansed once for all, and would no longer have felt the guilt of their sins.'),
('HEB', 10, 3, 'HEB.10.3', 'Instead, those sacrifices are an annual reminder of sins,'),
('HEB', 10, 4, 'HEB.10.4', 'because it is impossible for the blood of bulls and goats to take away sins.'),
('HEB', 10, 5, 'HEB.10.5', 'Therefore, when Christ came into the world, He said: “Sacrifice and offering You did not desire, but a body You prepared for Me.'),
('HEB', 10, 6, 'HEB.10.6', 'In burnt offerings and sin offerings You took no delight.'),
('HEB', 10, 7, 'HEB.10.7', 'Then I said, ‘Here I am, it is written about Me in the scroll: I have come to do Your will, O God.’”'),
('HEB', 10, 8, 'HEB.10.8', 'In the passage above He says, “Sacrifices and offerings, burnt offerings and sin offerings You did not desire, nor did You delight in them” (although they are offered according to the law).'),
('HEB', 10, 9, 'HEB.10.9', 'Then He adds, “Here I am, I have come to do Your will.” He takes away the first to establish the second.'),
('HEB', 10, 10, 'HEB.10.10', 'And by that will, we have been sanctified through the sacrifice of the body of Jesus Christ once for all.'),
('HEB', 10, 11, 'HEB.10.11', 'Day after day every priest stands to minister and to offer again and again the same sacrifices, which can never take away sins.'),
('HEB', 10, 12, 'HEB.10.12', 'But when this Priest had offered for all time one sacrifice for sins, He sat down at the right hand of God.'),
('HEB', 10, 13, 'HEB.10.13', 'Since that time, He waits for His enemies to be made a footstool for His feet,'),
('HEB', 10, 14, 'HEB.10.14', 'because by a single offering He has made perfect for all time those who are being sanctified.'),
('HEB', 10, 15, 'HEB.10.15', 'The Holy Spirit also testifies to us about this. First He says:'),
('HEB', 10, 16, 'HEB.10.16', '“This is the covenant I will make with them after those days, declares the Lord. I will put My laws in their hearts and inscribe them on their minds.”'),
('HEB', 10, 17, 'HEB.10.17', 'Then He adds: “Their sins and lawless acts I will remember no more.”'),
('HEB', 10, 18, 'HEB.10.18', 'And where these have been forgiven, an offering for sin is no longer needed.'),
('HEB', 10, 19, 'HEB.10.19', 'Therefore, brothers, since we have confidence to enter the Most Holy Place by the blood of Jesus,'),
('HEB', 10, 20, 'HEB.10.20', 'by the new and living way opened for us through the curtain of His body,'),
('HEB', 10, 21, 'HEB.10.21', 'and since we have a great priest over the house of God,'),
('HEB', 10, 22, 'HEB.10.22', 'let us draw near with a sincere heart in full assurance of faith, having our hearts sprinkled to cleanse us from a guilty conscience and our bodies washed with pure water.'),
('HEB', 10, 23, 'HEB.10.23', 'Let us hold resolutely to the hope we profess, for He who promised is faithful.'),
('HEB', 10, 24, 'HEB.10.24', 'And let us consider how to spur one another on to love and good deeds.'),
('HEB', 10, 25, 'HEB.10.25', 'Let us not neglect meeting together, as some have made a habit, but let us encourage one another, and all the more as you see the Day approaching.'),
('HEB', 10, 26, 'HEB.10.26', 'If we deliberately go on sinning after we have received the knowledge of the truth, no further sacrifice for sins remains,'),
('HEB', 10, 27, 'HEB.10.27', 'but only a fearful expectation of judgment and of raging fire that will consume all adversaries.'),
('HEB', 10, 28, 'HEB.10.28', 'Anyone who rejected the law of Moses died without mercy on the testimony of two or three witnesses.'),
('HEB', 10, 29, 'HEB.10.29', 'How much more severely do you think one deserves to be punished who has trampled on the Son of God, profaned the blood of the covenant that sanctified him, and insulted the Spirit of grace?'),
('HEB', 10, 30, 'HEB.10.30', 'For we know Him who said, “Vengeance is Mine; I will repay,” and again, “The Lord will judge His people.”'),
('HEB', 10, 31, 'HEB.10.31', 'It is a fearful thing to fall into the hands of the living God.'),
('HEB', 10, 32, 'HEB.10.32', 'Remember the early days that you were in the light. In those days, you endured a great conflict in the face of suffering.'),
('HEB', 10, 33, 'HEB.10.33', 'Sometimes you were publicly exposed to ridicule and persecution; at other times you were partners with those who were so treated.'),
('HEB', 10, 34, 'HEB.10.34', 'You sympathized with those in prison and joyfully accepted the confiscation of your property, knowing that you yourselves had a better and permanent possession.'),
('HEB', 10, 35, 'HEB.10.35', 'So do not throw away your confidence; it holds a great reward.'),
('HEB', 10, 36, 'HEB.10.36', 'You need to persevere, so that after you have done the will of God, you will receive what He has promised.'),
('HEB', 10, 37, 'HEB.10.37', 'For, “In just a little while, He who is coming will come and will not delay.'),
('HEB', 10, 38, 'HEB.10.38', 'But My righteous one will live by faith; and if he shrinks back, I will take no pleasure in him.”'),
('HEB', 10, 39, 'HEB.10.39', 'But we are not of those who shrink back and are destroyed, but of those who have faith and preserve their souls.'),
('HEB', 11, 1, 'HEB.11.1', 'Now faith is the assurance of what we hope for and the certainty of what we do not see.'),
('HEB', 11, 2, 'HEB.11.2', 'This is why the ancients were commended.'),
('HEB', 11, 3, 'HEB.11.3', 'By faith we understand that the universe was formed at God’s command, so that what is seen was not made out of what was visible.'),
('HEB', 11, 4, 'HEB.11.4', 'By faith Abel offered God a better sacrifice than Cain did. By faith he was commended as righteous when God gave approval to his gifts. And by faith he still speaks, even though he is dead.'),
('HEB', 11, 5, 'HEB.11.5', 'By faith Enoch was taken up so that he did not see death: “He could not be found, because God had taken him away.” For before he was taken, he was commended as one who pleased God.'),
('HEB', 11, 6, 'HEB.11.6', 'And without faith it is impossible to please God. For anyone who approaches Him must believe that He exists and that He rewards those who earnestly seek Him.'),
('HEB', 11, 7, 'HEB.11.7', 'By faith Noah, when warned about things not yet seen, in godly fear built an ark to save his family. By faith he condemned the world and became heir of the righteousness that comes by faith.'),
('HEB', 11, 8, 'HEB.11.8', 'By faith Abraham, when called to go to a place he would later receive as his inheritance, obeyed and went, without knowing where he was going.'),
('HEB', 11, 9, 'HEB.11.9', 'By faith he dwelt in the promised land as a stranger in a foreign country. He lived in tents, as did Isaac and Jacob, who were heirs with him of the same promise.'),
('HEB', 11, 10, 'HEB.11.10', 'For he was looking forward to the city with foundations, whose architect and builder is God.'),
('HEB', 11, 11, 'HEB.11.11', 'By faith Sarah, even though she was barren and beyond the proper age, was enabled to conceive a child, because she considered Him faithful who had promised.'),
('HEB', 11, 12, 'HEB.11.12', 'And so from one man, and he as good as dead, came descendants as numerous as the stars in the sky and as countless as the sand on the seashore.'),
('HEB', 11, 13, 'HEB.11.13', 'All these people died in faith, without having received the things they were promised. However, they saw them and welcomed them from afar. And they acknowledged that they were strangers and exiles on the earth.'),
('HEB', 11, 14, 'HEB.11.14', 'Now those who say such things show that they are seeking a country of their own.'),
('HEB', 11, 15, 'HEB.11.15', 'If they had been thinking of the country they had left, they would have had opportunity to return.'),
('HEB', 11, 16, 'HEB.11.16', 'Instead, they were longing for a better country, a heavenly one. Therefore God is not ashamed to be called their God, for He has prepared a city for them.'),
('HEB', 11, 17, 'HEB.11.17', 'By faith Abraham, when he was tested, offered up Isaac on the altar. He who had received the promises was ready to offer his one and only son,'),
('HEB', 11, 18, 'HEB.11.18', 'even though God had said to him, “Through Isaac your offspring will be reckoned.”'),
('HEB', 11, 19, 'HEB.11.19', 'Abraham reasoned that God could raise the dead, and in a sense, he did receive Isaac back from death.'),
('HEB', 11, 20, 'HEB.11.20', 'By faith Isaac blessed Jacob and Esau concerning the future.'),
('HEB', 11, 21, 'HEB.11.21', 'By faith Jacob, when he was dying, blessed each of Joseph’s sons and worshiped as he leaned on the top of his staff.'),
('HEB', 11, 22, 'HEB.11.22', 'By faith Joseph, when his end was near, spoke about the exodus of the Israelites and gave instructions about his bones.'),
('HEB', 11, 23, 'HEB.11.23', 'By faith Moses’ parents hid him for three months after his birth, because they saw that he was a beautiful child, and they were unafraid of the king’s edict.'),
('HEB', 11, 24, 'HEB.11.24', 'By faith Moses, when he was grown, refused to be called the son of Pharaoh’s daughter.'),
('HEB', 11, 25, 'HEB.11.25', 'He chose to suffer oppression with God’s people rather than to experience the fleeting enjoyment of sin.'),
('HEB', 11, 26, 'HEB.11.26', 'He valued disgrace for Christ above the treasures of Egypt, for he was looking ahead to his reward.'),
('HEB', 11, 27, 'HEB.11.27', 'By faith Moses left Egypt, not fearing the king’s anger; he persevered because he saw Him who is invisible.'),
('HEB', 11, 28, 'HEB.11.28', 'By faith he kept the Passover and the sprinkling of blood, so that the destroyer of the firstborn would not touch Israel’s own firstborn.'),
('HEB', 11, 29, 'HEB.11.29', 'By faith the people passed through the Red Sea as on dry land; but when the Egyptians tried to follow, they were drowned.'),
('HEB', 11, 30, 'HEB.11.30', 'By faith the walls of Jericho fell, after the people had marched around them for seven days.'),
('HEB', 11, 31, 'HEB.11.31', 'By faith the prostitute Rahab, because she welcomed the spies in peace, did not perish with those who were disobedient.'),
('HEB', 11, 32, 'HEB.11.32', 'And what more shall I say? Time will not allow me to tell of Gideon, Barak, Samson, Jephthah, David, Samuel, and the prophets,'),
('HEB', 11, 33, 'HEB.11.33', 'who through faith conquered kingdoms, administered justice, and gained what was promised; who shut the mouths of lions,'),
('HEB', 11, 34, 'HEB.11.34', 'quenched the raging fire, and escaped the edge of the sword; who gained strength from weakness, became mighty in battle, and put foreign armies to flight.'),
('HEB', 11, 35, 'HEB.11.35', 'Women received back their dead, raised to life again. Others were tortured and refused their release, so that they might gain a better resurrection.'),
('HEB', 11, 36, 'HEB.11.36', 'Still others endured mocking and flogging, and even chains and imprisonment.'),
('HEB', 11, 37, 'HEB.11.37', 'They were stoned, they were sawed in two, they were put to death by the sword. They went around in sheepskins and goatskins, destitute, oppressed, and mistreated.'),
('HEB', 11, 38, 'HEB.11.38', 'The world was not worthy of them. They wandered in deserts and mountains, and hid in caves and holes in the ground.'),
('HEB', 11, 39, 'HEB.11.39', 'These were all commended for their faith, yet they did not receive what was promised.'),
('HEB', 11, 40, 'HEB.11.40', 'God had planned something better for us, so that together with us they would be made perfect.'),
('HEB', 12, 1, 'HEB.12.1', 'Therefore, since we are surrounded by such a great cloud of witnesses, let us throw off every encumbrance and the sin that so easily entangles, and let us run with endurance the race set out for us.'),
('HEB', 12, 2, 'HEB.12.2', 'Let us fix our eyes on Jesus, the author and perfecter of our faith, who for the joy set before Him endured the cross, scorning its shame, and sat down at the right hand of the throne of God.'),
('HEB', 12, 3, 'HEB.12.3', 'Consider Him who endured such hostility from sinners, so that you will not grow weary and lose heart.'),
('HEB', 12, 4, 'HEB.12.4', 'In your struggle against sin, you have not yet resisted to the point of shedding your blood.'),
('HEB', 12, 5, 'HEB.12.5', 'And you have forgotten the exhortation that addresses you as sons: “My son, do not take lightly the discipline of the Lord, and do not lose heart when He rebukes you.'),
('HEB', 12, 6, 'HEB.12.6', 'For the Lord disciplines the one He loves, and He chastises every son He receives.”'),
('HEB', 12, 7, 'HEB.12.7', 'Endure suffering as discipline; God is treating you as sons. For what son is not disciplined by his father?'),
('HEB', 12, 8, 'HEB.12.8', 'If you do not experience discipline like everyone else, then you are illegitimate children and not true sons.'),
('HEB', 12, 9, 'HEB.12.9', 'Furthermore, we have all had earthly fathers who disciplined us, and we respected them. Should we not much more submit to the Father of our spirits and live?'),
('HEB', 12, 10, 'HEB.12.10', 'Our fathers disciplined us for a short time as they thought best, but God disciplines us for our good, so that we may share in His holiness.'),
('HEB', 12, 11, 'HEB.12.11', 'No discipline seems enjoyable at the time, but painful. Later on, however, it yields a harvest of righteousness and peace to those who have been trained by it.'),
('HEB', 12, 12, 'HEB.12.12', 'Therefore strengthen your limp hands and weak knees.'),
('HEB', 12, 13, 'HEB.12.13', 'Make straight paths for your feet, so that the lame may not be disabled, but rather healed.'),
('HEB', 12, 14, 'HEB.12.14', 'Pursue peace with everyone, as well as holiness, without which no one will see the Lord.'),
('HEB', 12, 15, 'HEB.12.15', 'See to it that no one falls short of the grace of God, and that no root of bitterness springs up to cause trouble and defile many.'),
('HEB', 12, 16, 'HEB.12.16', 'See to it that no one is sexually immoral, or is godless like Esau, who for a single meal sold his birthright.'),
('HEB', 12, 17, 'HEB.12.17', 'For you know that afterward, when he wanted to inherit the blessing, he was rejected. He could find no ground for repentance, though he sought the blessing with tears.'),
('HEB', 12, 18, 'HEB.12.18', 'For you have not come to a mountain that can be touched and that is burning with fire; to darkness, gloom, and storm;'),
('HEB', 12, 19, 'HEB.12.19', 'to a trumpet blast or to a voice that made its hearers beg that no further word be spoken.'),
('HEB', 12, 20, 'HEB.12.20', 'For they could not bear what was commanded: “If even an animal touches the mountain, it must be stoned.”'),
('HEB', 12, 21, 'HEB.12.21', 'The sight was so terrifying that even Moses said, “I am trembling with fear.”'),
('HEB', 12, 22, 'HEB.12.22', 'Instead, you have come to Mount Zion, to the city of the living God, the heavenly Jerusalem. You have come to myriads of angels'),
('HEB', 12, 23, 'HEB.12.23', 'in joyful assembly, to the congregation of the firstborn, enrolled in heaven. You have come to God the Judge of all, to the spirits of the righteous made perfect,'),
('HEB', 12, 24, 'HEB.12.24', 'to Jesus the mediator of a new covenant, and to the sprinkled blood that speaks a better word than the blood of Abel.'),
('HEB', 12, 25, 'HEB.12.25', 'See to it that you do not refuse Him who speaks. For if the people did not escape when they refused Him who warned them on earth, how much less will we escape if we reject Him who warns us from heaven?'),
('HEB', 12, 26, 'HEB.12.26', 'At that time His voice shook the earth, but now He has promised, “Once more I will shake not only the earth, but heaven as well.”'),
('HEB', 12, 27, 'HEB.12.27', 'The words “Once more” signify the removal of what can be shaken—that is, created things—so that the unshakable may remain.'),
('HEB', 12, 28, 'HEB.12.28', 'Therefore, since we are receiving an unshakable kingdom, let us be filled with gratitude, and so worship God acceptably with reverence and awe.'),
('HEB', 12, 29, 'HEB.12.29', '“For our God is a consuming fire.”'),
('HEB', 13, 1, 'HEB.13.1', 'Continue in brotherly love.'),
('HEB', 13, 2, 'HEB.13.2', 'Do not neglect to show hospitality to strangers, for by so doing some people have entertained angels without knowing it.'),
('HEB', 13, 3, 'HEB.13.3', 'Remember those in prison as if you were bound with them, and those who are mistreated as if you were suffering with them.'),
('HEB', 13, 4, 'HEB.13.4', 'Marriage should be honored by all and the marriage bed kept undefiled, for God will judge the sexually immoral and adulterers.'),
('HEB', 13, 5, 'HEB.13.5', 'Keep your lives free from the love of money and be content with what you have, for God has said: “Never will I leave you, never will I forsake you.”'),
('HEB', 13, 6, 'HEB.13.6', 'So we say with confidence: “The Lord is my helper; I will not be afraid. What can man do to me?”'),
('HEB', 13, 7, 'HEB.13.7', 'Remember your leaders who spoke the word of God to you. Consider the outcome of their way of life and imitate their faith.'),
('HEB', 13, 8, 'HEB.13.8', 'Jesus Christ is the same yesterday and today and forever.'),
('HEB', 13, 9, 'HEB.13.9', 'Do not be carried away by all kinds of strange teachings, for it is good for the heart to be strengthened by grace and not by foods of no value to those devoted to them.'),
('HEB', 13, 10, 'HEB.13.10', 'We have an altar from which those who serve at the tabernacle have no right to eat.'),
('HEB', 13, 11, 'HEB.13.11', 'Although the high priest brings the blood of animals into the Holy Place as a sacrifice for sin, the bodies are burned outside the camp.'),
('HEB', 13, 12, 'HEB.13.12', 'And so Jesus also suffered outside the city gate, to sanctify the people by His own blood.'),
('HEB', 13, 13, 'HEB.13.13', 'Therefore let us go to Him outside the camp, bearing the disgrace He bore.'),
('HEB', 13, 14, 'HEB.13.14', 'For here we do not have a permanent city, but we are looking for the city that is to come.'),
('HEB', 13, 15, 'HEB.13.15', 'Through Jesus, therefore, let us continually offer to God a sacrifice of praise, the fruit of lips that confess His name.'),
('HEB', 13, 16, 'HEB.13.16', 'And do not neglect to do good and to share with others, for with such sacrifices God is pleased.'),
('HEB', 13, 17, 'HEB.13.17', 'Obey your leaders and submit to them, for they watch over your souls as those who must give an account. To this end, allow them to lead with joy and not with grief, for that would be of no advantage to you.'),
('HEB', 13, 18, 'HEB.13.18', 'Pray for us; we are convinced that we have a clear conscience and desire to live honorably in every way.'),
('HEB', 13, 19, 'HEB.13.19', 'And I especially urge you to pray that I may be restored to you soon.'),
('HEB', 13, 20, 'HEB.13.20', 'Now may the God of peace, who through the blood of the eternal covenant brought back from the dead our Lord Jesus, that great Shepherd of the sheep,'),
('HEB', 13, 21, 'HEB.13.21', 'equip you with every good thing to do His will. And may He accomplish in us what is pleasing in His sight through Jesus Christ, to whom be glory forever and ever. Amen.'),
('HEB', 13, 22, 'HEB.13.22', 'I urge you, brothers, to bear with my word of exhortation, for I have only written to you briefly.'),
('HEB', 13, 23, 'HEB.13.23', 'Be aware that our brother Timothy has been released. If he arrives soon, I will come with him to see you.'),
('HEB', 13, 24, 'HEB.13.24', 'Greet all your leaders and all the saints. Those from Italy send you greetings.'),
('HEB', 13, 25, 'HEB.13.25', 'Grace be with all of you.'),
('JAS', 1, 1, 'JAS.1.1', 'James, a servant of God and of the Lord Jesus Christ, To the twelve tribes of the Dispersion: Greetings.'),
('JAS', 1, 2, 'JAS.1.2', 'Consider it pure joy, my brothers, when you encounter trials of many kinds,'),
('JAS', 1, 3, 'JAS.1.3', 'because you know that the testing of your faith develops perseverance.'),
('JAS', 1, 4, 'JAS.1.4', 'Allow perseverance to finish its work, so that you may be mature and complete, not lacking anything.'),
('JAS', 1, 5, 'JAS.1.5', 'Now if any of you lacks wisdom, he should ask God, who gives generously to all without finding fault, and it will be given to him.'),
('JAS', 1, 6, 'JAS.1.6', 'But he must ask in faith, without doubting, because he who doubts is like a wave of the sea, blown and tossed by the wind.'),
('JAS', 1, 7, 'JAS.1.7', 'That man should not expect to receive anything from the Lord.'),
('JAS', 1, 8, 'JAS.1.8', 'He is a double-minded man, unstable in all his ways.'),
('JAS', 1, 9, 'JAS.1.9', 'The brother in humble circumstances should exult in his high position.'),
('JAS', 1, 10, 'JAS.1.10', 'But the one who is rich should exult in his low position, because he will pass away like a flower of the field.'),
('JAS', 1, 11, 'JAS.1.11', 'For the sun rises with scorching heat and withers the plant; its flower falls and its beauty is lost. So too, the rich man will fade away in the midst of his pursuits.'),
('JAS', 1, 12, 'JAS.1.12', 'Blessed is the man who perseveres under trial, because when he has stood the test, he will receive the crown of life that God has promised to those who love Him.'),
('JAS', 1, 13, 'JAS.1.13', 'When tempted, no one should say, “God is tempting me.” For God cannot be tempted by evil, nor does He tempt anyone.'),
('JAS', 1, 14, 'JAS.1.14', 'But each one is tempted when by his own evil desires he is lured away and enticed.'),
('JAS', 1, 15, 'JAS.1.15', 'Then after desire has conceived, it gives birth to sin; and sin, when it is full-grown, gives birth to death.'),
('JAS', 1, 16, 'JAS.1.16', 'Do not be deceived, my beloved brothers.'),
('JAS', 1, 17, 'JAS.1.17', 'Every good and perfect gift is from above, coming down from the Father of the heavenly lights, with whom there is no change or shifting shadow.'),
('JAS', 1, 18, 'JAS.1.18', 'He chose to give us birth through the word of truth, that we would be a kind of firstfruits of His creation.'),
('JAS', 1, 19, 'JAS.1.19', 'My beloved brothers, understand this: Everyone should be quick to listen, slow to speak, and slow to anger,'),
('JAS', 1, 20, 'JAS.1.20', 'for man’s anger does not bring about the righteousness that God desires.'),
('JAS', 1, 21, 'JAS.1.21', 'Therefore, get rid of all moral filth and every expression of evil, and humbly accept the word planted in you, which can save your souls.'),
('JAS', 1, 22, 'JAS.1.22', 'Be doers of the word, and not hearers only. Otherwise, you are deceiving yourselves.'),
('JAS', 1, 23, 'JAS.1.23', 'For anyone who hears the word but does not carry it out is like a man who looks at his face in a mirror,'),
('JAS', 1, 24, 'JAS.1.24', 'and after observing himself goes away and immediately forgets what he looks like.'),
('JAS', 1, 25, 'JAS.1.25', 'But the one who looks intently into the perfect law of freedom, and continues to do so—not being a forgetful hearer, but an effective doer—he will be blessed in what he does.'),
('JAS', 1, 26, 'JAS.1.26', 'If anyone considers himself religious and yet does not bridle his tongue, he deceives his heart and his religion is worthless.'),
('JAS', 1, 27, 'JAS.1.27', 'Pure and undefiled religion before our God and Father is this: to care for orphans and widows in their distress, and to keep oneself from being polluted by the world.'),
('JAS', 2, 1, 'JAS.2.1', 'My brothers, as you hold out your faith in our glorious Lord Jesus Christ, do not show favoritism.'),
('JAS', 2, 2, 'JAS.2.2', 'Suppose a man comes into your meeting wearing a gold ring and fine clothes, and a poor man in shabby clothes also comes in.'),
('JAS', 2, 3, 'JAS.2.3', 'If you lavish attention on the man in fine clothes and say, “Here is a seat of honor,” but say to the poor man, “You must stand” or “Sit at my feet,”'),
('JAS', 2, 4, 'JAS.2.4', 'have you not discriminated among yourselves and become judges with evil thoughts?'),
('JAS', 2, 5, 'JAS.2.5', 'Listen, my beloved brothers: Has not God chosen the poor of this world to be rich in faith and to inherit the kingdom He promised those who love Him?'),
('JAS', 2, 6, 'JAS.2.6', 'But you have dishonored the poor. Is it not the rich who oppress you and drag you into court?'),
('JAS', 2, 7, 'JAS.2.7', 'Are they not the ones who blaspheme the noble name by which you have been called?'),
('JAS', 2, 8, 'JAS.2.8', 'If you really fulfill the royal law stated in Scripture, “Love your neighbor as yourself,” you are doing well.'),
('JAS', 2, 9, 'JAS.2.9', 'But if you show favoritism, you sin and are convicted by the law as transgressors.'),
('JAS', 2, 10, 'JAS.2.10', 'Whoever keeps the whole law but stumbles at just one point is guilty of breaking all of it.'),
('JAS', 2, 11, 'JAS.2.11', 'For He who said, “Do not commit adultery,” also said, “Do not murder.” If you do not commit adultery, but do commit murder, you have become a lawbreaker.'),
('JAS', 2, 12, 'JAS.2.12', 'Speak and act as those who are going to be judged by the law that gives freedom.'),
('JAS', 2, 13, 'JAS.2.13', 'For judgment without mercy will be shown to anyone who has not been merciful. Mercy triumphs over judgment.'),
('JAS', 2, 14, 'JAS.2.14', 'What good is it, my brothers, if someone claims to have faith, but has no deeds? Can such faith save him?'),
('JAS', 2, 15, 'JAS.2.15', 'Suppose a brother or sister is without clothes and daily food.'),
('JAS', 2, 16, 'JAS.2.16', 'If one of you tells him, “Go in peace; stay warm and well fed,” but does not provide for his physical needs, what good is that?'),
('JAS', 2, 17, 'JAS.2.17', 'So too, faith by itself, if it does not result in action, is dead.'),
('JAS', 2, 18, 'JAS.2.18', 'But someone will say, “You have faith and I have deeds.” Show me your faith without deeds, and I will show you my faith by my deeds.'),
('JAS', 2, 19, 'JAS.2.19', 'You believe that God is one. Good for you! Even the demons believe that—and shudder.'),
('JAS', 2, 20, 'JAS.2.20', 'O foolish man, do you want evidence that faith without deeds is worthless?'),
('JAS', 2, 21, 'JAS.2.21', 'Was not our father Abraham justified by what he did when he offered his son Isaac on the altar?'),
('JAS', 2, 22, 'JAS.2.22', 'You see that his faith was working with his actions, and his faith was perfected by what he did.'),
('JAS', 2, 23, 'JAS.2.23', 'And the Scripture was fulfilled that says, “Abraham believed God, and it was credited to him as righteousness,” and he was called a friend of God.'),
('JAS', 2, 24, 'JAS.2.24', 'As you can see, a man is justified by his deeds and not by faith alone.'),
('JAS', 2, 25, 'JAS.2.25', 'In the same way, was not even Rahab the prostitute justified by her actions when she welcomed the spies and sent them off on another route?'),
('JAS', 2, 26, 'JAS.2.26', 'As the body without the spirit is dead, so faith without deeds is dead.'),
('JAS', 3, 1, 'JAS.3.1', 'Not many of you should become teachers, my brothers, because you know that we who teach will be judged more strictly.'),
('JAS', 3, 2, 'JAS.3.2', 'We all stumble in many ways. If anyone is never at fault in what he says, he is a perfect man, able to control his whole body.'),
('JAS', 3, 3, 'JAS.3.3', 'When we put bits into the mouths of horses to make them obey us, we can guide the whole animal.'),
('JAS', 3, 4, 'JAS.3.4', 'Consider ships as well. Although they are so large and are driven by strong winds, they are steered by a very small rudder wherever the pilot is inclined.'),
('JAS', 3, 5, 'JAS.3.5', 'In the same way, the tongue is a small part of the body, but it boasts of great things. Consider how small a spark sets a great forest ablaze.'),
('JAS', 3, 6, 'JAS.3.6', 'The tongue also is a fire, a world of wickedness among the parts of the body. It pollutes the whole person, sets the course of his life on fire, and is itself set on fire by hell.'),
('JAS', 3, 7, 'JAS.3.7', 'All kinds of animals, birds, reptiles, and creatures of the sea are being tamed and have been tamed by man,'),
('JAS', 3, 8, 'JAS.3.8', 'but no man can tame the tongue. It is a restless evil, full of deadly poison.'),
('JAS', 3, 9, 'JAS.3.9', 'With the tongue we bless our Lord and Father, and with it we curse men, who have been made in God’s likeness.'),
('JAS', 3, 10, 'JAS.3.10', 'Out of the same mouth come blessing and cursing. My brothers, this should not be!'),
('JAS', 3, 11, 'JAS.3.11', 'Can both fresh water and salt water flow from the same spring?'),
('JAS', 3, 12, 'JAS.3.12', 'My brothers, can a fig tree grow olives, or a grapevine bear figs? Neither can a salt spring produce fresh water.'),
('JAS', 3, 13, 'JAS.3.13', 'Who is wise and understanding among you? Let him show it by his good conduct, by deeds done in the humility that comes from wisdom.'),
('JAS', 3, 14, 'JAS.3.14', 'But if you harbor bitter jealousy and selfish ambition in your hearts, do not boast in it or deny the truth.'),
('JAS', 3, 15, 'JAS.3.15', 'Such wisdom does not come from above, but is earthly, unspiritual, demonic.'),
('JAS', 3, 16, 'JAS.3.16', 'For where jealousy and selfish ambition exist, there will be disorder and every evil practice.'),
('JAS', 3, 17, 'JAS.3.17', 'But the wisdom from above is first of all pure, then peace-loving, gentle, accommodating, full of mercy and good fruit, impartial, and sincere.'),
('JAS', 3, 18, 'JAS.3.18', 'Peacemakers who sow in peace reap the fruit of righteousness.'),
('JAS', 4, 1, 'JAS.4.1', 'What causes conflicts and quarrels among you? Don’t they come from the passions at war within you?'),
('JAS', 4, 2, 'JAS.4.2', 'You crave what you do not have; you kill and covet, but are unable to obtain it. You quarrel and fight. You do not have, because you do not ask.'),
('JAS', 4, 3, 'JAS.4.3', 'And when you do ask, you do not receive, because you ask with wrong motives, that you may squander it on your pleasures.'),
('JAS', 4, 4, 'JAS.4.4', 'You adulteresses! Do you not know that friendship with the world is hostility toward God? Therefore, whoever chooses to be a friend of the world renders himself an enemy of God.'),
('JAS', 4, 5, 'JAS.4.5', 'Or do you think the Scripture says without reason that the Spirit He caused to dwell in us yearns with envy?'),
('JAS', 4, 6, 'JAS.4.6', 'But He gives us more grace. This is why it says: “God opposes the proud, but gives grace to the humble.”'),
('JAS', 4, 7, 'JAS.4.7', 'Submit yourselves, then, to God. Resist the devil, and he will flee from you.'),
('JAS', 4, 8, 'JAS.4.8', 'Draw near to God, and He will draw near to you. Cleanse your hands, you sinners, and purify your hearts, you double-minded.'),
('JAS', 4, 9, 'JAS.4.9', 'Grieve, mourn, and weep. Turn your laughter to mourning, and your joy to gloom.'),
('JAS', 4, 10, 'JAS.4.10', 'Humble yourselves before the Lord, and He will exalt you.'),
('JAS', 4, 11, 'JAS.4.11', 'Brothers, do not slander one another. Anyone who speaks against his brother or judges him speaks against the law and judges it. And if you judge the law, you are not a practitioner of the law, but a judge of it.'),
('JAS', 4, 12, 'JAS.4.12', 'There is only one Lawgiver and Judge, the One who is able to save and destroy. But who are you to judge your neighbor?'),
('JAS', 4, 13, 'JAS.4.13', 'Come now, you who say, “Today or tomorrow we will go to this or that city, spend a year there, carry on business, and make a profit.”'),
('JAS', 4, 14, 'JAS.4.14', 'You do not even know what will happen tomorrow! What is your life? You are a mist that appears for a little while and then vanishes.'),
('JAS', 4, 15, 'JAS.4.15', 'Instead, you ought to say, “If the Lord is willing, we will live and do this or that.”'),
('JAS', 4, 16, 'JAS.4.16', 'As it is, you boast in your proud intentions. All such boasting is evil.'),
('JAS', 4, 17, 'JAS.4.17', 'Anyone, then, who knows the right thing to do, yet fails to do it, is guilty of sin.'),
('JAS', 5, 1, 'JAS.5.1', 'Come now, you who are rich, weep and wail over the misery to come upon you.'),
('JAS', 5, 2, 'JAS.5.2', 'Your riches have rotted and moths have eaten your clothes.'),
('JAS', 5, 3, 'JAS.5.3', 'Your gold and silver are corroded. Their corrosion will testify against you and consume your flesh like fire. You have hoarded treasure in the last days.'),
('JAS', 5, 4, 'JAS.5.4', 'Look, the wages you withheld from the workmen who mowed your fields are crying out against you. The cries of the harvesters have reached the ears of the Lord of Hosts.'),
('JAS', 5, 5, 'JAS.5.5', 'You have lived on earth in luxury and self-indulgence. You have fattened your hearts in the day of slaughter.'),
('JAS', 5, 6, 'JAS.5.6', 'You have condemned and murdered the righteous, who did not resist you.'),
('JAS', 5, 7, 'JAS.5.7', 'Be patient, then, brothers, until the Lord’s coming. See how the farmer awaits the precious fruit of the soil—how patient he is for the fall and spring rains.'),
('JAS', 5, 8, 'JAS.5.8', 'You, too, be patient and strengthen your hearts, because the Lord’s coming is near.'),
('JAS', 5, 9, 'JAS.5.9', 'Do not complain about one another, brothers, so that you will not be judged. Look, the Judge is standing at the door!'),
('JAS', 5, 10, 'JAS.5.10', 'Brothers, as an example of patience in affliction, take the prophets who spoke in the name of the Lord.'),
('JAS', 5, 11, 'JAS.5.11', 'See how blessed we consider those who have persevered. You have heard of Job’s perseverance and have seen the outcome from the Lord. The Lord is full of compassion and mercy.'),
('JAS', 5, 12, 'JAS.5.12', 'Above all, my brothers, do not swear, not by heaven or earth or by any other oath. Simply let your “Yes” be yes, and your “No,” no, so that you will not fall under judgment.'),
('JAS', 5, 13, 'JAS.5.13', 'Is any one of you suffering? He should pray. Is anyone cheerful? He should sing praises.'),
('JAS', 5, 14, 'JAS.5.14', 'Is any one of you sick? He should call the elders of the church to pray over him and anoint him with oil in the name of the Lord.'),
('JAS', 5, 15, 'JAS.5.15', 'And the prayer offered in faith will restore the one who is sick. The Lord will raise him up. If he has sinned, he will be forgiven.'),
('JAS', 5, 16, 'JAS.5.16', 'Therefore confess your sins to each other and pray for each other so that you may be healed. The prayer of a righteous man has great power to prevail.'),
('JAS', 5, 17, 'JAS.5.17', 'Elijah was a man just like us. He prayed earnestly that it would not rain, and it did not rain on the land for three and a half years.'),
('JAS', 5, 18, 'JAS.5.18', 'Again he prayed, and the heavens gave rain, and the earth yielded its crops.'),
('JAS', 5, 19, 'JAS.5.19', 'My brothers, if one of you should wander from the truth and someone should bring him back,'),
('JAS', 5, 20, 'JAS.5.20', 'consider this: Whoever turns a sinner from the error of his way will save his soul from death and cover over a multitude of sins.'),
('1PE', 1, 1, '1PE.1.1', 'Peter, an apostle of Jesus Christ, To the elect who are exiles of the Dispersion throughout Pontus, Galatia, Cappadocia, Asia, and Bithynia, chosen'),
('1PE', 1, 2, '1PE.1.2', 'according to the foreknowledge of God the Father and sanctified by the Spirit for obedience to Jesus Christ and sprinkling by His blood: Grace and peace be yours in abundance.'),
('1PE', 1, 3, '1PE.1.3', 'Blessed be the God and Father of our Lord Jesus Christ! By His great mercy He has given us new birth into a living hope through the resurrection of Jesus Christ from the dead,'),
('1PE', 1, 4, '1PE.1.4', 'and into an inheritance that is imperishable, undefiled, and unfading, reserved in heaven for you,'),
('1PE', 1, 5, '1PE.1.5', 'who through faith are shielded by God’s power for the salvation that is ready to be revealed in the last time.'),
('1PE', 1, 6, '1PE.1.6', 'In this you greatly rejoice, though now for a little while you may have had to suffer grief in various trials'),
('1PE', 1, 7, '1PE.1.7', 'so that the proven character of your faith—more precious than gold, which perishes even though refined by fire—may result in praise, glory, and honor at the revelation of Jesus Christ.'),
('1PE', 1, 8, '1PE.1.8', 'Though you have not seen Him, you love Him; and though you do not see Him now, you believe in Him and rejoice with an inexpressible and glorious joy,'),
('1PE', 1, 9, '1PE.1.9', 'now that you are receiving the goal of your faith, the salvation of your souls.'),
('1PE', 1, 10, '1PE.1.10', 'Concerning this salvation, the prophets who foretold the grace to come to you searched and investigated carefully,'),
('1PE', 1, 11, '1PE.1.11', 'trying to determine the time and setting to which the Spirit of Christ in them was pointing when He predicted the sufferings of Christ and the glories to follow.'),
('1PE', 1, 12, '1PE.1.12', 'It was revealed to them that they were not serving themselves, but you, when they foretold the things now announced by those who preached the gospel to you by the Holy Spirit sent from heaven. Even angels long to look into these things.'),
('1PE', 1, 13, '1PE.1.13', 'Therefore prepare your minds for action. Be sober-minded. Set your hope fully on the grace to be given you at the revelation of Jesus Christ.'),
('1PE', 1, 14, '1PE.1.14', 'As obedient children, do not conform to the passions of your former ignorance.'),
('1PE', 1, 15, '1PE.1.15', 'But just as He who called you is holy, so be holy in all you do,'),
('1PE', 1, 16, '1PE.1.16', 'for it is written: “Be holy, because I am holy.”'),
('1PE', 1, 17, '1PE.1.17', 'Since you call on a Father who judges each one’s work impartially, conduct yourselves in reverent fear during your stay as foreigners.'),
('1PE', 1, 18, '1PE.1.18', 'For you know that it was not with perishable things such as silver or gold that you were redeemed from the empty way of life you inherited from your forefathers,'),
('1PE', 1, 19, '1PE.1.19', 'but with the precious blood of Christ, a lamb without blemish or spot.'),
('1PE', 1, 20, '1PE.1.20', 'He was known before the foundation of the world, but was revealed in the last times for your sake.'),
('1PE', 1, 21, '1PE.1.21', 'Through Him you believe in God, who raised Him from the dead and glorified Him; and so your faith and hope are in God.'),
('1PE', 1, 22, '1PE.1.22', 'Since you have purified your souls by obedience to the truth so that you have a genuine love for your brothers, love one another deeply, from a pure heart.'),
('1PE', 1, 23, '1PE.1.23', 'For you have been born again, not of perishable seed, but of imperishable, through the living and enduring word of God.'),
('1PE', 1, 24, '1PE.1.24', 'For, “All flesh is like grass, and all its glory like the flowers of the field; the grass withers and the flowers fall,'),
('1PE', 1, 25, '1PE.1.25', 'but the word of the Lord stands forever.” And this is the word that was proclaimed to you.'),
('1PE', 2, 1, '1PE.2.1', 'Rid yourselves, therefore, of all malice, deceit, hypocrisy, envy, and slander.'),
('1PE', 2, 2, '1PE.2.2', 'Like newborn babies, crave pure spiritual milk, so that by it you may grow up in your salvation,'),
('1PE', 2, 3, '1PE.2.3', 'now that you have tasted that the Lord is good.'),
('1PE', 2, 4, '1PE.2.4', 'As you come to Him, the living stone, rejected by men but chosen and precious in God’s sight,'),
('1PE', 2, 5, '1PE.2.5', 'you also, like living stones, are being built into a spiritual house to be a holy priesthood, offering spiritual sacrifices acceptable to God through Jesus Christ.'),
('1PE', 2, 6, '1PE.2.6', 'For it stands in Scripture: “See, I lay in Zion a stone, a chosen and precious cornerstone; and the one who believes in Him will never be put to shame.”'),
('1PE', 2, 7, '1PE.2.7', 'To you who believe, then, this stone is precious. But to those who do not believe, “The stone the builders rejected has become the cornerstone,”'),
('1PE', 2, 8, '1PE.2.8', 'and, “A stone of stumbling and a rock of offense.” They stumble because they disobey the word—and to this they were appointed.'),
('1PE', 2, 9, '1PE.2.9', 'But you are a chosen people, a royal priesthood, a holy nation, a people for God’s own possession, to proclaim the virtues of Him who called you out of darkness into His marvelous light.'),
('1PE', 2, 10, '1PE.2.10', 'Once you were not a people, but now you are the people of God; once you had not received mercy, but now you have received mercy.'),
('1PE', 2, 11, '1PE.2.11', 'Beloved, I urge you, as foreigners and exiles, to abstain from the desires of the flesh, which war against your soul.'),
('1PE', 2, 12, '1PE.2.12', 'Conduct yourselves with such honor among the Gentiles that, though they slander you as evildoers, they may see your good deeds and glorify God on the day He visits us.'),
('1PE', 2, 13, '1PE.2.13', 'Submit yourselves for the Lord’s sake to every human institution, whether to the king as the supreme authority,'),
('1PE', 2, 14, '1PE.2.14', 'or to governors as those sent by him to punish those who do wrong and to praise those who do right.'),
('1PE', 2, 15, '1PE.2.15', 'For it is God’s will that by doing good you should silence the ignorance of foolish men.'),
('1PE', 2, 16, '1PE.2.16', 'Live in freedom, but do not use your freedom as a cover-up for evil; live as servants of God.'),
('1PE', 2, 17, '1PE.2.17', 'Treat everyone with high regard: Love the brotherhood of believers, fear God, honor the king.'),
('1PE', 2, 18, '1PE.2.18', 'Servants, submit yourselves to your masters with all respect, not only to those who are good and gentle, but even to those who are unreasonable.'),
('1PE', 2, 19, '1PE.2.19', 'For if anyone endures the pain of unjust suffering because he is conscious of God, this is to be commended.'),
('1PE', 2, 20, '1PE.2.20', 'How is it to your credit if you are beaten for doing wrong and you endure it? But if you suffer for doing good and you endure it, this is commendable before God.'),
('1PE', 2, 21, '1PE.2.21', 'For to this you were called, because Christ also suffered for you, leaving you an example, that you should follow in His footsteps:'),
('1PE', 2, 22, '1PE.2.22', '“He committed no sin, and no deceit was found in His mouth.”'),
('1PE', 2, 23, '1PE.2.23', 'When they heaped abuse on Him, He did not retaliate; when He suffered, He made no threats, but entrusted Himself to Him who judges justly.'),
('1PE', 2, 24, '1PE.2.24', 'He Himself bore our sins in His body on the tree, so that we might die to sin and live to righteousness. “By His stripes you are healed.”'),
('1PE', 2, 25, '1PE.2.25', 'For “you were like sheep going astray,” but now you have returned to the Shepherd and Overseer of your souls.'),
('1PE', 3, 1, '1PE.3.1', 'Wives, in the same way, submit yourselves to your husbands, so that even if they refuse to believe the word, they will be won over without words by the behavior of their wives'),
('1PE', 3, 2, '1PE.3.2', 'when they see your pure and reverent demeanor.'),
('1PE', 3, 3, '1PE.3.3', 'Your beauty should not come from outward adornment, such as braided hair or gold jewelry or fine clothes,'),
('1PE', 3, 4, '1PE.3.4', 'but from the inner disposition of your heart, the unfading beauty of a gentle and quiet spirit, which is precious in God’s sight.'),
('1PE', 3, 5, '1PE.3.5', 'For this is how the holy women of the past adorned themselves. They put their hope in God and were submissive to their husbands,'),
('1PE', 3, 6, '1PE.3.6', 'just as Sarah obeyed Abraham and called him lord. And you are her children if you do what is right and refuse to give way to fear.'),
('1PE', 3, 7, '1PE.3.7', 'Husbands, in the same way, treat your wives with consideration as a delicate vessel, and with honor as fellow heirs of the gracious gift of life, so that your prayers will not be hindered.'),
('1PE', 3, 8, '1PE.3.8', 'Finally, all of you, be like-minded and sympathetic, love as brothers, be tenderhearted and humble.'),
('1PE', 3, 9, '1PE.3.9', 'Do not repay evil with evil or insult with insult, but with blessing, because to this you were called so that you may inherit a blessing.'),
('1PE', 3, 10, '1PE.3.10', 'For, “Whoever would love life and see good days must keep his tongue from evil and his lips from deceitful speech.'),
('1PE', 3, 11, '1PE.3.11', 'He must turn from evil and do good; he must seek peace and pursue it.'),
('1PE', 3, 12, '1PE.3.12', 'For the eyes of the Lord are on the righteous, and His ears are inclined to their prayer. But the face of the Lord is against those who do evil.”'),
('1PE', 3, 13, '1PE.3.13', 'Who can harm you if you are zealous for what is good?'),
('1PE', 3, 14, '1PE.3.14', 'But even if you should suffer for what is right, you are blessed. “Do not fear what they fear; do not be shaken.”'),
('1PE', 3, 15, '1PE.3.15', 'But in your hearts sanctify Christ as Lord. Always be prepared to give a defense to everyone who asks you the reason for the hope that is in you. But respond with gentleness and respect,'),
('1PE', 3, 16, '1PE.3.16', 'keeping a clear conscience, so that those who slander you may be put to shame by your good behavior in Christ.'),
('1PE', 3, 17, '1PE.3.17', 'For it is better, if it is God’s will, to suffer for doing good than for doing evil.'),
('1PE', 3, 18, '1PE.3.18', 'For Christ also suffered for sins once for all, the righteous for the unrighteous, to bring you to God. He was put to death in the body but made alive in the Spirit,'),
('1PE', 3, 19, '1PE.3.19', 'in whom He also went and preached to the spirits in prison'),
('1PE', 3, 20, '1PE.3.20', 'who disobeyed long ago when God waited patiently in the days of Noah while the ark was being built. In the ark a few people, only eight souls, were saved through water.'),
('1PE', 3, 21, '1PE.3.21', 'And this water symbolizes the baptism that now saves you also—not the removal of dirt from the body, but the pledge of a clear conscience toward God—through the resurrection of Jesus Christ,'),
('1PE', 3, 22, '1PE.3.22', 'who has gone into heaven and is at the right hand of God, with angels, authorities, and powers subject to Him.'),
('1PE', 4, 1, '1PE.4.1', 'Therefore, since Christ suffered in His body, arm yourselves with the same resolve, because anyone who has suffered in his body is done with sin.'),
('1PE', 4, 2, '1PE.4.2', 'Consequently, he does not live out his remaining time on earth for human passions, but for the will of God.'),
('1PE', 4, 3, '1PE.4.3', 'For you have spent enough time in the past carrying out the same desires as the Gentiles: living in debauchery, lust, drunkenness, orgies, carousing, and detestable idolatry.'),
('1PE', 4, 4, '1PE.4.4', 'Because of this, they consider it strange of you not to plunge with them into the same flood of reckless indiscretion, and they heap abuse on you.'),
('1PE', 4, 5, '1PE.4.5', 'But they will have to give an account to Him who is ready to judge the living and the dead.'),
('1PE', 4, 6, '1PE.4.6', 'That is why the gospel was preached even to those who are now dead, so that they might be judged as men in the flesh, but live according to God in the spirit.'),
('1PE', 4, 7, '1PE.4.7', 'The end of all things is near. Therefore be clear-minded and sober, so that you can pray.'),
('1PE', 4, 8, '1PE.4.8', 'Above all, love one another deeply, because love covers over a multitude of sins.'),
('1PE', 4, 9, '1PE.4.9', 'Show hospitality to one another without complaining.'),
('1PE', 4, 10, '1PE.4.10', 'As good stewards of the manifold grace of God, each of you should use whatever gift he has received to serve one another.'),
('1PE', 4, 11, '1PE.4.11', 'If anyone speaks, he should speak as one conveying the words of God. If anyone serves, he should serve with the strength God provides, so that in all things God may be glorified through Jesus Christ, to whom be the glory and the power forever and ever. Amen.'),
('1PE', 4, 12, '1PE.4.12', 'Beloved, do not be surprised at the fiery trial that has come upon you, as though something strange were happening to you.'),
('1PE', 4, 13, '1PE.4.13', 'But rejoice that you share in the sufferings of Christ, so that you may be overjoyed at the revelation of His glory.'),
('1PE', 4, 14, '1PE.4.14', 'If you are insulted for the name of Christ, you are blessed, because the Spirit of glory and of God rests on you.'),
('1PE', 4, 15, '1PE.4.15', 'Indeed, none of you should suffer as a murderer or thief or wrongdoer, or even as a meddler.'),
('1PE', 4, 16, '1PE.4.16', 'But if you suffer as a Christian, do not be ashamed, but glorify God that you bear that name.'),
('1PE', 4, 17, '1PE.4.17', 'For it is time for judgment to begin with the family of God; and if it begins with us, what will the outcome be for those who disobey the gospel of God?'),
('1PE', 4, 18, '1PE.4.18', 'And, “If it is hard for the righteous to be saved, what will become of the ungodly and the sinner?”'),
('1PE', 4, 19, '1PE.4.19', 'So then, those who suffer according to God’s will should entrust their souls to their faithful Creator and continue to do good.'),
('1PE', 5, 1, '1PE.5.1', 'As a fellow elder, a witness of Christ’s sufferings, and a partaker of the glory to be revealed, I appeal to the elders among you:'),
('1PE', 5, 2, '1PE.5.2', 'Be shepherds of God’s flock that is among you, watching over them not out of compulsion, but willingly, as God would have you; not out of greed, but out of eagerness;'),
('1PE', 5, 3, '1PE.5.3', 'not lording it over those entrusted to you, but being examples to the flock.'),
('1PE', 5, 4, '1PE.5.4', 'And when the Chief Shepherd appears, you will receive the crown of glory that will never fade away.'),
('1PE', 5, 5, '1PE.5.5', 'Young men, in the same way, submit yourselves to your elders. And all of you, clothe yourselves with humility toward one another, because, “God opposes the proud, but gives grace to the humble.”'),
('1PE', 5, 6, '1PE.5.6', 'Humble yourselves, therefore, under God’s mighty hand, so that in due time He may exalt you.'),
('1PE', 5, 7, '1PE.5.7', 'Cast all your anxiety on Him, because He cares for you.'),
('1PE', 5, 8, '1PE.5.8', 'Be sober-minded and alert. Your adversary the devil prowls around like a roaring lion, seeking someone to devour.'),
('1PE', 5, 9, '1PE.5.9', 'Resist him, standing firm in your faith and in the knowledge that your brothers throughout the world are undergoing the same kinds of suffering.'),
('1PE', 5, 10, '1PE.5.10', 'And after you have suffered for a little while, the God of all grace, who has called you to His eternal glory in Christ, will Himself restore you, secure you, strengthen you, and establish you.'),
('1PE', 5, 11, '1PE.5.11', 'To Him be the power forever and ever. Amen.'),
('1PE', 5, 12, '1PE.5.12', 'Through Silvanus, whom I regard as a faithful brother, I have written to you briefly, encouraging you and testifying that this is the true grace of God. Stand firm in it.'),
('1PE', 5, 13, '1PE.5.13', 'The church in Babylon, chosen together with you, sends you greetings, as does my son Mark.'),
('1PE', 5, 14, '1PE.5.14', 'Greet one another with a kiss of love. Peace to all of you who are in Christ.'),
('2PE', 1, 1, '2PE.1.1', 'Simon Peter, a servant and apostle of Jesus Christ, To those who through the righteousness of our God and Savior Jesus Christ have received a faith as precious as ours:'),
('2PE', 1, 2, '2PE.1.2', 'Grace and peace be multiplied to you through the knowledge of God and of Jesus our Lord.'),
('2PE', 1, 3, '2PE.1.3', 'His divine power has given us everything we need for life and godliness through the knowledge of Him who called us by His own glory and excellence.'),
('2PE', 1, 4, '2PE.1.4', 'Through these He has given us His precious and magnificent promises, so that through them you may become partakers of the divine nature, now that you have escaped the corruption in the world caused by evil desires.'),
('2PE', 1, 5, '2PE.1.5', 'For this very reason, make every effort to add to your faith virtue; and to virtue, knowledge;'),
('2PE', 1, 6, '2PE.1.6', 'and to knowledge, self-control; and to self-control, perseverance; and to perseverance, godliness;'),
('2PE', 1, 7, '2PE.1.7', 'and to godliness, brotherly kindness; and to brotherly kindness, love.'),
('2PE', 1, 8, '2PE.1.8', 'For if you possess these qualities and continue to grow in them, they will keep you from being ineffective and unproductive in your knowledge of our Lord Jesus Christ.'),
('2PE', 1, 9, '2PE.1.9', 'But whoever lacks these traits is nearsighted to the point of blindness, having forgotten that he has been cleansed from his past sins.'),
('2PE', 1, 10, '2PE.1.10', 'Therefore, brothers, strive to make your calling and election sure. For if you practice these things you will never stumble,'),
('2PE', 1, 11, '2PE.1.11', 'and you will receive a lavish reception into the eternal kingdom of our Lord and Savior Jesus Christ.'),
('2PE', 1, 12, '2PE.1.12', 'Therefore I will always remind you of these things, even though you know them and are established in the truth you now have.'),
('2PE', 1, 13, '2PE.1.13', 'I think it is right to refresh your memory as long as I live in the tent of my body,'),
('2PE', 1, 14, '2PE.1.14', 'because I know that this tent will soon be laid aside, as our Lord Jesus Christ has made clear to me.'),
('2PE', 1, 15, '2PE.1.15', 'And I will make every effort to ensure that after my departure, you will be able to recall these things at all times.'),
('2PE', 1, 16, '2PE.1.16', 'For we did not follow cleverly devised fables when we made known to you the power and coming of our Lord Jesus Christ, but we were eyewitnesses of His majesty.'),
('2PE', 1, 17, '2PE.1.17', 'For He received honor and glory from God the Father when the voice came to Him from the Majestic Glory, saying, “This is My beloved Son, in whom I am well pleased.”'),
('2PE', 1, 18, '2PE.1.18', 'And we ourselves heard this voice from heaven when we were with Him on the holy mountain.'),
('2PE', 1, 19, '2PE.1.19', 'We also have the word of the prophets as confirmed beyond doubt. And you will do well to pay attention to it, as to a lamp shining in a dark place, until the day dawns and the morning star rises in your hearts.'),
('2PE', 1, 20, '2PE.1.20', 'Above all, you must understand that no prophecy of Scripture comes from one’s own interpretation.'),
('2PE', 1, 21, '2PE.1.21', 'For no such prophecy was ever brought forth by the will of man, but men spoke from God as they were carried along by the Holy Spirit.'),
('2PE', 2, 1, '2PE.2.1', 'Now there were also false prophets among the people, just as there will be false teachers among you. They will secretly introduce destructive heresies, even denying the Master who bought them—bringing swift destruction on themselves.'),
('2PE', 2, 2, '2PE.2.2', 'Many will follow in their depravity, and because of them the way of truth will be defamed.'),
('2PE', 2, 3, '2PE.2.3', 'In their greed, these false teachers will exploit you with deceptive words. The longstanding verdict against them remains in force, and their destruction does not sleep.'),
('2PE', 2, 4, '2PE.2.4', 'For if God did not spare the angels when they sinned, but cast them deep into hell, placing them in chains of darkness to be held for judgment;'),
('2PE', 2, 5, '2PE.2.5', 'if He did not spare the ancient world when He brought the flood on its ungodly people, but preserved Noah, a preacher of righteousness, among the eight;'),
('2PE', 2, 6, '2PE.2.6', 'if He condemned the cities of Sodom and Gomorrah to destruction, reducing them to ashes as an example of what is coming on the ungodly;'),
('2PE', 2, 7, '2PE.2.7', 'and if He rescued Lot, a righteous man distressed by the depraved conduct of the lawless'),
('2PE', 2, 8, '2PE.2.8', '(for that righteous man, living among them day after day, was tormented in his righteous soul by the lawless deeds he saw and heard)—'),
('2PE', 2, 9, '2PE.2.9', 'if all this is so, then the Lord knows how to rescue the godly from trials and to hold the unrighteous for punishment on the day of judgment.'),
('2PE', 2, 10, '2PE.2.10', 'Such punishment is specially reserved for those who indulge the corrupt desires of the flesh and despise authority. Bold and self-willed, they are unafraid to slander glorious beings.'),
('2PE', 2, 11, '2PE.2.11', 'Yet not even angels, though greater in strength and power, dare to bring such slanderous charges against them before the Lord.'),
('2PE', 2, 12, '2PE.2.12', 'These men are like irrational animals, creatures of instinct, born to be captured and destroyed. They blaspheme in matters they do not understand, and like such creatures, they too will be destroyed.'),
('2PE', 2, 13, '2PE.2.13', 'The harm they will suffer is the wages of their wickedness. They consider it a pleasure to carouse in broad daylight. They are blots and blemishes, reveling in their deception as they feast with you.'),
('2PE', 2, 14, '2PE.2.14', 'Their eyes are full of adultery; their desire for sin is never satisfied; they seduce the unstable. They are accursed children with hearts trained in greed.'),
('2PE', 2, 15, '2PE.2.15', 'They have left the straight way and wandered off to follow the way of Balaam son of Beor, who loved the wages of wickedness.'),
('2PE', 2, 16, '2PE.2.16', 'But he was rebuked for his transgression by a donkey, otherwise without speech, that spoke with a man’s voice and restrained the prophet’s madness.'),
('2PE', 2, 17, '2PE.2.17', 'These men are springs without water and mists driven by a storm. Blackest darkness is reserved for them.'),
('2PE', 2, 18, '2PE.2.18', 'With lofty but empty words, they appeal to the sensual passions of the flesh and entice those who are just escaping from others who live in error.'),
('2PE', 2, 19, '2PE.2.19', 'They promise them freedom, while they themselves are slaves to depravity. For a man is a slave to whatever has mastered him.'),
('2PE', 2, 20, '2PE.2.20', 'If indeed they have escaped the corruption of the world through the knowledge of our Lord and Savior Jesus Christ, only to be entangled and overcome by it again, their final condition is worse than it was at first.'),
('2PE', 2, 21, '2PE.2.21', 'It would have been better for them not to have known the way of righteousness than to have known it and then to turn away from the holy commandment passed on to them.'),
('2PE', 2, 22, '2PE.2.22', 'Of them the proverbs are true: “A dog returns to its vomit,” and, “A sow that is washed goes back to her wallowing in the mud.”'),
('2PE', 3, 1, '2PE.3.1', 'Beloved, this is now my second letter to you. Both of them are reminders to stir you to wholesome thinking'),
('2PE', 3, 2, '2PE.3.2', 'by recalling what was foretold by the holy prophets and commanded by our Lord and Savior through your apostles.'),
('2PE', 3, 3, '2PE.3.3', 'Most importantly, you must understand that in the last days scoffers will come, scoffing and following their own evil desires.'),
('2PE', 3, 4, '2PE.3.4', '“Where is the promise of His coming?” they will ask. “Ever since our fathers fell asleep, everything continues as it has from the beginning of creation.”'),
('2PE', 3, 5, '2PE.3.5', 'But they deliberately overlook the fact that long ago by God’s word the heavens existed and the earth was formed out of water and by water,'),
('2PE', 3, 6, '2PE.3.6', 'through which the world of that time perished in the flood.'),
('2PE', 3, 7, '2PE.3.7', 'And by that same word, the present heavens and earth are reserved for fire, being kept for the day of judgment and destruction of ungodly men.'),
('2PE', 3, 8, '2PE.3.8', 'Beloved, do not let this one thing escape your notice: With the Lord a day is like a thousand years, and a thousand years are like a day.'),
('2PE', 3, 9, '2PE.3.9', 'The Lord is not slow in keeping His promise as some understand slowness, but is patient with you, not wanting anyone to perish but everyone to come to repentance.'),
('2PE', 3, 10, '2PE.3.10', 'But the Day of the Lord will come like a thief. The heavens will disappear with a roar, the elements will be destroyed by fire, and the earth and its works will be laid bare.'),
('2PE', 3, 11, '2PE.3.11', 'Since everything will be destroyed in this way, what kind of people ought you to be? You ought to conduct yourselves in holiness and godliness'),
('2PE', 3, 12, '2PE.3.12', 'as you anticipate and hasten the coming of the day of God, when the heavens will be destroyed by fire and the elements will melt in the heat.'),
('2PE', 3, 13, '2PE.3.13', 'But in keeping with God’s promise, we are looking forward to a new heaven and a new earth, where righteousness dwells.'),
('2PE', 3, 14, '2PE.3.14', 'Therefore, beloved, as you anticipate these things, make every effort to be found at peace—spotless and blameless in His sight.'),
('2PE', 3, 15, '2PE.3.15', 'Consider also that our Lord’s patience brings salvation, just as our beloved brother Paul also wrote you with the wisdom God gave him.'),
('2PE', 3, 16, '2PE.3.16', 'He writes this way in all his letters, speaking in them about such matters. Some parts of his letters are hard to understand, which ignorant and unstable people distort, as they do the rest of the Scriptures, to their own destruction.'),
('2PE', 3, 17, '2PE.3.17', 'Therefore, beloved, since you already know these things, be on your guard so that you will not be carried away by the error of the lawless and fall from your secure standing.'),
('2PE', 3, 18, '2PE.3.18', 'But grow in the grace and knowledge of our Lord and Savior Jesus Christ. To Him be the glory both now and to the day of eternity. Amen.'),
('1JN', 1, 1, '1JN.1.1', 'That which was from the beginning, which we have heard, which we have seen with our own eyes, which we have gazed upon and touched with our own hands—this is the Word of life.'),
('1JN', 1, 2, '1JN.1.2', 'And this is the life that was revealed; we have seen it and testified to it, and we proclaim to you the eternal life that was with the Father and was revealed to us.'),
('1JN', 1, 3, '1JN.1.3', 'We proclaim to you what we have seen and heard, so that you also may have fellowship with us. And this fellowship of ours is with the Father and with His Son, Jesus Christ.'),
('1JN', 1, 4, '1JN.1.4', 'We write these things so that our joy may be complete.'),
('1JN', 1, 5, '1JN.1.5', 'And this is the message we have heard from Him and announce to you: God is light, and in Him there is no darkness at all.'),
('1JN', 1, 6, '1JN.1.6', 'If we say we have fellowship with Him yet walk in the darkness, we lie and do not practice the truth.'),
('1JN', 1, 7, '1JN.1.7', 'But if we walk in the light as He is in the light, we have fellowship with one another, and the blood of Jesus His Son cleanses us from all sin.'),
('1JN', 1, 8, '1JN.1.8', 'If we say we have no sin, we deceive ourselves, and the truth is not in us.'),
('1JN', 1, 9, '1JN.1.9', 'If we confess our sins, He is faithful and just to forgive us our sins and to cleanse us from all unrighteousness.'),
('1JN', 1, 10, '1JN.1.10', 'If we say we have not sinned, we make Him out to be a liar, and His word is not in us.'),
('1JN', 2, 1, '1JN.2.1', 'My little children, I am writing these things to you so that you will not sin. But if anyone does sin, we have an advocate before the Father—Jesus Christ, the Righteous One.'),
('1JN', 2, 2, '1JN.2.2', 'He Himself is the atoning sacrifice for our sins, and not only for ours but also for the sins of the whole world.'),
('1JN', 2, 3, '1JN.2.3', 'By this we can be sure that we have come to know Him: if we keep His commandments.'),
('1JN', 2, 4, '1JN.2.4', 'If anyone says, “I know Him,” but does not keep His commandments, he is a liar, and the truth is not in him.'),
('1JN', 2, 5, '1JN.2.5', 'But if anyone keeps His word, the love of God has been truly perfected in him. By this we know that we are in Him:'),
('1JN', 2, 6, '1JN.2.6', 'Whoever claims to abide in Him must walk as Jesus walked.'),
('1JN', 2, 7, '1JN.2.7', 'Beloved, I am not writing to you a new commandment, but an old one, which you have had from the beginning. This commandment is the message you have heard.'),
('1JN', 2, 8, '1JN.2.8', 'Then again, I am also writing to you a new commandment, which is true in Him and also in you. For the darkness is fading and the true light is already shining.'),
('1JN', 2, 9, '1JN.2.9', 'If anyone claims to be in the light but hates his brother, he is still in the darkness.'),
('1JN', 2, 10, '1JN.2.10', 'Whoever loves his brother remains in the light, and there is no cause of stumbling in him.'),
('1JN', 2, 11, '1JN.2.11', 'But whoever hates his brother is in the darkness and walks in the darkness. He does not know where he is going, because the darkness has blinded his eyes.'),
('1JN', 2, 12, '1JN.2.12', 'I am writing to you, little children, because your sins have been forgiven through His name.'),
('1JN', 2, 13, '1JN.2.13', 'I am writing to you, fathers, because you know Him who is from the beginning. I am writing to you, young men, because you have overcome the evil one. I have written to you, children, because you know the Father.'),
('1JN', 2, 14, '1JN.2.14', 'I have written to you, fathers, because you know Him who is from the beginning. I have written to you, young men, because you are strong, and the word of God abides in you, and you have overcome the evil one.'),
('1JN', 2, 15, '1JN.2.15', 'Do not love the world or anything in the world. If anyone loves the world, the love of the Father is not in him.'),
('1JN', 2, 16, '1JN.2.16', 'For all that is in the world—the desires of the flesh, the desires of the eyes, and the pride of life—is not from the Father but from the world.'),
('1JN', 2, 17, '1JN.2.17', 'The world is passing away, along with its desires; but whoever does the will of God remains forever.'),
('1JN', 2, 18, '1JN.2.18', 'Children, it is the last hour; and just as you have heard that the antichrist is coming, so now many antichrists have appeared. This is how we know it is the last hour.'),
('1JN', 2, 19, '1JN.2.19', 'They went out from us, but they did not belong to us. For if they had belonged to us, they would have remained with us. But their departure made it clear that none of them belonged to us.'),
('1JN', 2, 20, '1JN.2.20', 'You, however, have an anointing from the Holy One, and all of you know the truth.'),
('1JN', 2, 21, '1JN.2.21', 'I have not written to you because you lack knowledge of the truth, but because you have it, and because no lie comes from the truth.'),
('1JN', 2, 22, '1JN.2.22', 'Who is the liar, if it is not the one who denies that Jesus is the Christ? This is the antichrist, who denies the Father and the Son.'),
('1JN', 2, 23, '1JN.2.23', 'Whoever denies the Son does not have the Father, but whoever confesses the Son has the Father as well.'),
('1JN', 2, 24, '1JN.2.24', 'As for you, let what you have heard from the beginning remain in you. If it does, you will also remain in the Son and in the Father.'),
('1JN', 2, 25, '1JN.2.25', 'And this is the promise that He Himself made to us: eternal life.'),
('1JN', 2, 26, '1JN.2.26', 'I have written these things to you about those who are trying to deceive you.'),
('1JN', 2, 27, '1JN.2.27', 'And as for you, the anointing you received from Him remains in you, and you do not need anyone to teach you. But just as His true and genuine anointing teaches you about all things, so remain in Him as you have been taught.'),
('1JN', 2, 28, '1JN.2.28', 'And now, little children, remain in Christ, so that when He appears, we may be confident and unashamed before Him at His coming.'),
('1JN', 2, 29, '1JN.2.29', 'If you know that He is righteous, you also know that everyone who practices righteousness has been born of Him.'),
('1JN', 3, 1, '1JN.3.1', 'Behold what manner of love the Father has given to us, that we should be called children of God. And that is what we are! The reason the world does not know us is that it did not know Him.'),
('1JN', 3, 2, '1JN.3.2', 'Beloved, we are now children of God, and what we will be has not yet been revealed. We know that when Christ appears, we will be like Him, for we will see Him as He is.'),
('1JN', 3, 3, '1JN.3.3', 'And everyone who has this hope in Him purifies himself, just as Christ is pure.'),
('1JN', 3, 4, '1JN.3.4', 'Everyone who practices sin practices lawlessness as well. Indeed, sin is lawlessness.'),
('1JN', 3, 5, '1JN.3.5', 'But you know that Christ appeared to take away sins, and in Him there is no sin.'),
('1JN', 3, 6, '1JN.3.6', 'No one who remains in Him keeps on sinning. No one who continues to sin has seen Him or known Him.'),
('1JN', 3, 7, '1JN.3.7', 'Little children, let no one deceive you: The one who practices righteousness is righteous, just as Christ is righteous.'),
('1JN', 3, 8, '1JN.3.8', 'The one who practices sin is of the devil, because the devil has been sinning from the very start. This is why the Son of God was revealed, to destroy the works of the devil.'),
('1JN', 3, 9, '1JN.3.9', 'Anyone born of God refuses to practice sin, because God’s seed abides in him; he cannot go on sinning, because he has been born of God.'),
('1JN', 3, 10, '1JN.3.10', 'By this the children of God are distinguished from the children of the devil: Anyone who does not practice righteousness is not of God, nor is anyone who does not love his brother.'),
('1JN', 3, 11, '1JN.3.11', 'This is the message you have heard from the beginning: We should love one another.'),
('1JN', 3, 12, '1JN.3.12', 'Do not be like Cain, who belonged to the evil one and murdered his brother. And why did Cain slay him? Because his own deeds were evil, while those of his brother were righteous.'),
('1JN', 3, 13, '1JN.3.13', 'So do not be surprised, brothers, if the world hates you.'),
('1JN', 3, 14, '1JN.3.14', 'We know that we have passed from death to life, because we love our brothers. The one who does not love remains in death.'),
('1JN', 3, 15, '1JN.3.15', 'Everyone who hates his brother is a murderer, and you know that eternal life does not reside in a murderer.'),
('1JN', 3, 16, '1JN.3.16', 'By this we know what love is: Jesus laid down His life for us, and we ought to lay down our lives for our brothers.'),
('1JN', 3, 17, '1JN.3.17', 'If anyone with earthly possessions sees his brother in need, but withholds his compassion from him, how can the love of God abide in him?'),
('1JN', 3, 18, '1JN.3.18', 'Little children, let us love not in word and speech, but in action and truth.'),
('1JN', 3, 19, '1JN.3.19', 'And by this we will know that we belong to the truth, and will assure our hearts in His presence:'),
('1JN', 3, 20, '1JN.3.20', 'Even if our hearts condemn us, God is greater than our hearts, and He knows all things.'),
('1JN', 3, 21, '1JN.3.21', 'Beloved, if our hearts do not condemn us, we have confidence before God,'),
('1JN', 3, 22, '1JN.3.22', 'and we will receive from Him whatever we ask, because we keep His commandments and do what is pleasing in His sight.'),
('1JN', 3, 23, '1JN.3.23', 'And this is His commandment: that we should believe in the name of His Son, Jesus Christ, and we should love one another just as He commanded us.'),
('1JN', 3, 24, '1JN.3.24', 'Whoever keeps His commandments remains in God, and God in him. And by this we know that He remains in us: by the Spirit He has given us.'),
('1JN', 4, 1, '1JN.4.1', 'Beloved, do not believe every spirit, but test the spirits to see whether they are from God. For many false prophets have gone out into the world.'),
('1JN', 4, 2, '1JN.4.2', 'By this you will know the Spirit of God: Every spirit that confesses that Jesus Christ has come in the flesh is from God,'),
('1JN', 4, 3, '1JN.4.3', 'and every spirit that does not confess Jesus is not from God. This is the spirit of the antichrist, which you have heard is coming and which is already in the world at this time.'),
('1JN', 4, 4, '1JN.4.4', 'You, little children, are from God and have overcome them, because greater is He who is in you than he who is in the world.'),
('1JN', 4, 5, '1JN.4.5', 'They are of the world. That is why they speak from the world’s perspective, and the world listens to them.'),
('1JN', 4, 6, '1JN.4.6', 'We are from God. Whoever knows God listens to us; whoever is not from God does not listen to us. That is how we know the Spirit of truth and the spirit of deception.'),
('1JN', 4, 7, '1JN.4.7', 'Beloved, let us love one another, because love comes from God. Everyone who loves has been born of God and knows God.'),
('1JN', 4, 8, '1JN.4.8', 'Whoever does not love does not know God, because God is love.'),
('1JN', 4, 9, '1JN.4.9', 'This is how God’s love was revealed among us: God sent His one and only Son into the world, so that we might live through Him.'),
('1JN', 4, 10, '1JN.4.10', 'And love consists in this: not that we loved God, but that He loved us and sent His Son as the atoning sacrifice for our sins.'),
('1JN', 4, 11, '1JN.4.11', 'Beloved, if God so loved us, we also ought to love one another.'),
('1JN', 4, 12, '1JN.4.12', 'No one has ever seen God; but if we love one another, God remains in us, and His love is perfected in us.'),
('1JN', 4, 13, '1JN.4.13', 'By this we know that we remain in Him, and He in us: He has given us of His Spirit.'),
('1JN', 4, 14, '1JN.4.14', 'And we have seen and testify that the Father has sent His Son to be the Savior of the world.'),
('1JN', 4, 15, '1JN.4.15', 'If anyone confesses that Jesus is the Son of God, God abides in him, and he in God.'),
('1JN', 4, 16, '1JN.4.16', 'And we have come to know and believe the love that God has for us. God is love; whoever abides in love abides in God, and God in him.'),
('1JN', 4, 17, '1JN.4.17', 'In this way, love has been perfected among us, so that we may have confidence on the day of judgment; for in this world we are just like Him.'),
('1JN', 4, 18, '1JN.4.18', 'There is no fear in love, but perfect love drives out fear, because fear involves punishment. The one who fears has not been perfected in love.'),
('1JN', 4, 19, '1JN.4.19', 'We love because He first loved us.'),
('1JN', 4, 20, '1JN.4.20', 'If anyone says, “I love God,” but hates his brother, he is a liar. For anyone who does not love his brother, whom he has seen, cannot love God, whom he has not seen.'),
('1JN', 4, 21, '1JN.4.21', 'And we have this commandment from Him: Whoever loves God must love his brother as well.'),
('1JN', 5, 1, '1JN.5.1', 'Everyone who believes that Jesus is the Christ has been born of God, and everyone who loves the Father also loves those born of Him.'),
('1JN', 5, 2, '1JN.5.2', 'By this we know that we love the children of God: when we love God and keep His commandments.'),
('1JN', 5, 3, '1JN.5.3', 'For this is the love of God, that we keep His commandments. And His commandments are not burdensome,'),
('1JN', 5, 4, '1JN.5.4', 'because everyone born of God overcomes the world. And this is the victory that has overcome the world: our faith.'),
('1JN', 5, 5, '1JN.5.5', 'Who then overcomes the world? Only he who believes that Jesus is the Son of God.'),
('1JN', 5, 6, '1JN.5.6', 'This is the One who came by water and blood, Jesus Christ—not by water alone, but by water and blood. And it is the Spirit who testifies to this, because the Spirit is the truth.'),
('1JN', 5, 7, '1JN.5.7', 'For there are three that testify:'),
('1JN', 5, 8, '1JN.5.8', 'the Spirit, the water, and the blood—and these three are in agreement.'),
('1JN', 5, 9, '1JN.5.9', 'Even if we accept human testimony, the testimony of God is greater. For this is the testimony that God has given about His Son.'),
('1JN', 5, 10, '1JN.5.10', 'Whoever believes in the Son of God has this testimony within him; whoever does not believe God has made Him out to be a liar, because he has not believed in the testimony that God has given about His Son.'),
('1JN', 5, 11, '1JN.5.11', 'And this is that testimony: God has given us eternal life, and this life is in His Son.'),
('1JN', 5, 12, '1JN.5.12', 'Whoever has the Son has life; whoever does not have the Son of God does not have life.'),
('1JN', 5, 13, '1JN.5.13', 'I have written these things to you who believe in the name of the Son of God, so that you may know that you have eternal life.'),
('1JN', 5, 14, '1JN.5.14', 'And this is the confidence that we have before Him: If we ask anything according to His will, He hears us.'),
('1JN', 5, 15, '1JN.5.15', 'And if we know that He hears us in whatever we ask, we know that we already possess what we have asked of Him.'),
('1JN', 5, 16, '1JN.5.16', 'If anyone sees his brother committing a sin not leading to death, he should ask God, who will give life to those who commit this kind of sin. There is a sin that leads to death; I am not saying he should ask regarding that sin.'),
('1JN', 5, 17, '1JN.5.17', 'All unrighteousness is sin, yet there is sin that does not lead to death.'),
('1JN', 5, 18, '1JN.5.18', 'We know that anyone born of God does not keep on sinning; the One who was born of God protects him, and the evil one cannot touch him.'),
('1JN', 5, 19, '1JN.5.19', 'We know that we are of God, and that the whole world is under the power of the evil one.'),
('1JN', 5, 20, '1JN.5.20', 'And we know that the Son of God has come and has given us understanding, so that we may know Him who is true; and we are in Him who is true—in His Son Jesus Christ. He is the true God and eternal life.'),
('1JN', 5, 21, '1JN.5.21', 'Little children, keep yourselves from idols.'),
('2JN', 1, 1, '2JN.1.1', 'The elder, To the chosen lady and her children, whom I love in the truth—and not I alone, but also all who know the truth—'),
('2JN', 1, 2, '2JN.1.2', 'because of the truth that abides in us and will be with us forever:'),
('2JN', 1, 3, '2JN.1.3', 'Grace, mercy, and peace from God the Father and from Jesus Christ, the Son of the Father, will be with us in truth and love.'),
('2JN', 1, 4, '2JN.1.4', 'I was overjoyed to find some of your children walking in the truth, just as the Father has commanded us.'),
('2JN', 1, 5, '2JN.1.5', 'And now I urge you, dear lady—not as a new commandment to you, but one we have had from the beginning—that we love one another.'),
('2JN', 1, 6, '2JN.1.6', 'And this is love, that we walk according to His commandments. This is the very commandment you have heard from the beginning, that you must walk in love.'),
('2JN', 1, 7, '2JN.1.7', 'For many deceivers have gone out into the world, refusing to confess the coming of Jesus Christ in the flesh. Any such person is the deceiver and the antichrist.'),
('2JN', 1, 8, '2JN.1.8', 'Watch yourselves, so that you do not lose what we have worked for, but that you may be fully rewarded.'),
('2JN', 1, 9, '2JN.1.9', 'Anyone who runs ahead without remaining in the teaching of Christ does not have God. Whoever remains in His teaching has both the Father and the Son.'),
('2JN', 1, 10, '2JN.1.10', 'If anyone comes to you but does not bring this teaching, do not receive him into your home or even greet him.'),
('2JN', 1, 11, '2JN.1.11', 'Whoever greets such a person shares in his evil deeds.'),
('2JN', 1, 12, '2JN.1.12', 'I have many things to write to you, but I would prefer not to do so with paper and ink. Instead, I hope to come and speak with you face to face, so that our joy may be complete.'),
('2JN', 1, 13, '2JN.1.13', 'The children of your elect sister send you greetings.'),
('3JN', 1, 1, '3JN.1.1', 'The elder, To the beloved Gaius, whom I love in the truth:'),
('3JN', 1, 2, '3JN.1.2', 'Beloved, I pray that in every way you may prosper and enjoy good health, as your soul also prospers.'),
('3JN', 1, 3, '3JN.1.3', 'For I was overjoyed when the brothers came and testified about your devotion to the truth, in which you continue to walk.'),
('3JN', 1, 4, '3JN.1.4', 'I have no greater joy than to hear that my children are walking in the truth.'),
('3JN', 1, 5, '3JN.1.5', 'Beloved, you are faithful in what you are doing for the brothers, and especially since they are strangers to you.'),
('3JN', 1, 6, '3JN.1.6', 'They have testified to the church about your love. You will do well to send them on their way in a manner worthy of God.'),
('3JN', 1, 7, '3JN.1.7', 'For they went out on behalf of the Name, accepting nothing from the Gentiles.'),
('3JN', 1, 8, '3JN.1.8', 'Therefore we ought to support such men, so that we may be fellow workers for the truth.'),
('3JN', 1, 9, '3JN.1.9', 'I have written to the church about this, but Diotrephes, who loves to be first, will not accept our instruction.'),
('3JN', 1, 10, '3JN.1.10', 'So if I come, I will call attention to his malicious slander against us. And unsatisfied with that, he refuses to welcome the brothers and forbids those who want to do so, even putting them out of the church.'),
('3JN', 1, 11, '3JN.1.11', 'Beloved, do not imitate what is evil, but what is good. The one who does good is of God; the one who does evil has not seen God.'),
('3JN', 1, 12, '3JN.1.12', 'Demetrius has received a good testimony from everyone, and from the truth itself. We also testify for him, and you know that our testimony is true.'),
('3JN', 1, 13, '3JN.1.13', 'I have many things to write to you, but I would prefer not to do so with pen and ink.'),
('3JN', 1, 14, '3JN.1.14', 'Instead, I hope to see you soon and speak with you face to face. Peace to you. The friends here send you greetings. Greet each of our friends there by name.'),
('JUD', 1, 1, 'JUD.1.1', 'Jude, a servant of Jesus Christ and a brother of James, To those who are called, loved by God the Father, and kept in Jesus Christ:'),
('JUD', 1, 2, 'JUD.1.2', 'Mercy, peace, and love be multiplied to you.'),
('JUD', 1, 3, 'JUD.1.3', 'Beloved, although I made every effort to write to you about the salvation we share, I felt it necessary to write and urge you to contend earnestly for the faith entrusted once for all to the saints.'),
('JUD', 1, 4, 'JUD.1.4', 'For certain men have crept in among you unnoticed—ungodly ones who were designated long ago for condemnation. They turn the grace of our God into a license for immorality, and they deny our only Master and Lord, Jesus Christ.'),
('JUD', 1, 5, 'JUD.1.5', 'Although you are fully aware of this, I want to remind you that after Jesus had delivered His people out of the land of Egypt, He destroyed those who did not believe.'),
('JUD', 1, 6, 'JUD.1.6', 'And the angels who did not stay within their own domain but abandoned their proper dwelling—these He has kept in eternal chains under darkness, bound for judgment on that great day.'),
('JUD', 1, 7, 'JUD.1.7', 'In like manner, Sodom and Gomorrah and the cities around them, who indulged in sexual immorality and pursued strange flesh, are on display as an example of those who sustain the punishment of eternal fire.'),
('JUD', 1, 8, 'JUD.1.8', 'Yet in the same way these dreamers defile their bodies, reject authority, and slander glorious beings.'),
('JUD', 1, 9, 'JUD.1.9', 'But even the archangel Michael, when he disputed with the devil over the body of Moses, did not presume to bring a slanderous charge against him, but said, “The Lord rebuke you!”'),
('JUD', 1, 10, 'JUD.1.10', 'These men, however, slander what they do not understand, and like irrational animals, they will be destroyed by the things they do instinctively.'),
('JUD', 1, 11, 'JUD.1.11', 'Woe to them! They have traveled the path of Cain; they have rushed for profit into the error of Balaam; they have perished in Korah’s rebellion.'),
('JUD', 1, 12, 'JUD.1.12', 'These men are hidden reefs in your love feasts, shamelessly feasting with you but shepherding only themselves. They are clouds without water, carried along by the wind; fruitless trees in autumn, twice dead after being uprooted.'),
('JUD', 1, 13, 'JUD.1.13', 'They are wild waves of the sea, foaming up their own shame; wandering stars, for whom blackest darkness has been reserved forever.'),
('JUD', 1, 14, 'JUD.1.14', 'Enoch, the seventh from Adam, also prophesied about them: “Behold, the Lord is coming with myriads of His holy ones'),
('JUD', 1, 15, 'JUD.1.15', 'to execute judgment on everyone, and to convict all the ungodly of every ungodly act of wickedness and every harsh word spoken against Him by ungodly sinners.”'),
('JUD', 1, 16, 'JUD.1.16', 'These men are discontented grumblers, following after their own lusts; their mouths spew arrogance; they flatter others for their own advantage.'),
('JUD', 1, 17, 'JUD.1.17', 'But you, beloved, remember what was foretold by the apostles of our Lord Jesus Christ'),
('JUD', 1, 18, 'JUD.1.18', 'when they said to you, “In the last times there will be scoffers who will follow after their own ungodly desires.”'),
('JUD', 1, 19, 'JUD.1.19', 'These are the ones who cause divisions, who are worldly and devoid of the Spirit.'),
('JUD', 1, 20, 'JUD.1.20', 'But you, beloved, by building yourselves up in your most holy faith and praying in the Holy Spirit,'),
('JUD', 1, 21, 'JUD.1.21', 'keep yourselves in the love of God as you await the mercy of our Lord Jesus Christ to bring you eternal life.'),
('JUD', 1, 22, 'JUD.1.22', 'And indeed, have mercy on those who doubt;'),
('JUD', 1, 23, 'JUD.1.23', 'save others by snatching them from the fire; and to still others show mercy tempered with fear, hating even the clothing stained by the flesh.'),
('JUD', 1, 24, 'JUD.1.24', 'Now to Him who is able to keep you from stumbling and to present you unblemished in His glorious presence, with great joy—'),
('JUD', 1, 25, 'JUD.1.25', 'to the only God our Savior be glory, majesty, dominion, and authority through Jesus Christ our Lord before all time, and now, and for all eternity. Amen.'),
('REV', 1, 1, 'REV.1.1', 'This is the revelation of Jesus Christ, which God gave Him to show His servants what must soon come to pass. He made it known by sending His angel to His servant John,'),
('REV', 1, 2, 'REV.1.2', 'who testifies to everything he saw. This is the word of God and the testimony of Jesus Christ.'),
('REV', 1, 3, 'REV.1.3', 'Blessed is the one who reads aloud the words of this prophecy, and blessed are those who hear and obey what is written in it, because the time is near.'),
('REV', 1, 4, 'REV.1.4', 'John, To the seven churches in the province of Asia: Grace and peace to you from Him who is and was and is to come, and from the seven spirits before His throne,'),
('REV', 1, 5, 'REV.1.5', 'and from Jesus Christ, the faithful witness, the firstborn from the dead, and the ruler of the kings of the earth. To Him who loves us and has released us from our sins by His blood,'),
('REV', 1, 6, 'REV.1.6', 'who has made us to be a kingdom, priests to His God and Father—to Him be the glory and power forever and ever! Amen.'),
('REV', 1, 7, 'REV.1.7', 'Behold, He is coming with the clouds, and every eye will see Him—even those who pierced Him. And all the tribes of the earth will mourn because of Him. So shall it be! Amen.'),
('REV', 1, 8, 'REV.1.8', '“I am the Alpha and the Omega,” says the Lord God, who is and was and is to come—the Almighty.'),
('REV', 1, 9, 'REV.1.9', 'I, John, your brother and partner in the tribulation and kingdom and perseverance that are in Jesus, was on the island of Patmos because of the word of God and my testimony about Jesus.'),
('REV', 1, 10, 'REV.1.10', 'On the Lord’s day I was in the Spirit, and I heard behind me a loud voice like a trumpet,'),
('REV', 1, 11, 'REV.1.11', 'saying, “Write on a scroll what you see and send it to the seven churches: to Ephesus, Smyrna, Pergamum, Thyatira, Sardis, Philadelphia, and Laodicea.”'),
('REV', 1, 12, 'REV.1.12', 'Then I turned to see the voice that was speaking with me. And having turned, I saw seven golden lampstands,'),
('REV', 1, 13, 'REV.1.13', 'and among the lampstands was One like the Son of Man, dressed in a long robe, with a golden sash around His chest.'),
('REV', 1, 14, 'REV.1.14', 'The hair of His head was white like wool, as white as snow, and His eyes were like a blazing fire.'),
('REV', 1, 15, 'REV.1.15', 'His feet were like polished bronze refined in a furnace, and His voice was like the roar of many waters.'),
('REV', 1, 16, 'REV.1.16', 'He held in His right hand seven stars, and a sharp double-edged sword came from His mouth. His face was like the sun shining at its brightest.'),
('REV', 1, 17, 'REV.1.17', 'When I saw Him, I fell at His feet like a dead man. But He placed His right hand on me and said, “Do not be afraid. I am the First and the Last,'),
('REV', 1, 18, 'REV.1.18', 'the Living One. I was dead, and behold, now I am alive forever and ever! And I hold the keys of Death and of Hades.'),
('REV', 1, 19, 'REV.1.19', 'Therefore write down the things you have seen, the things that are, and the things that will happen after this.'),
('REV', 1, 20, 'REV.1.20', 'This is the mystery of the seven stars you saw in My right hand and of the seven golden lampstands: The seven stars are the angels of the seven churches, and the seven lampstands are the seven churches.'),
('REV', 2, 1, 'REV.2.1', '“To the angel of the church in Ephesus write: These are the words of Him who holds the seven stars in His right hand and walks among the seven golden lampstands.'),
('REV', 2, 2, 'REV.2.2', 'I know your deeds, your labor, and your perseverance. I know that you cannot tolerate those who are evil, and you have tested and exposed as liars those who falsely claim to be apostles.'),
('REV', 2, 3, 'REV.2.3', 'Without growing weary, you have persevered and endured many things for the sake of My name.'),
('REV', 2, 4, 'REV.2.4', 'But I have this against you: You have abandoned your first love.'),
('REV', 2, 5, 'REV.2.5', 'Therefore, keep in mind how far you have fallen. Repent and perform the deeds you did at first. But if you do not repent, I will come to you and remove your lampstand from its place.'),
('REV', 2, 6, 'REV.2.6', 'But you have this to your credit: You hate the works of the Nicolaitans, which I also hate.'),
('REV', 2, 7, 'REV.2.7', 'He who has an ear, let him hear what the Spirit says to the churches. To the one who overcomes, I will grant the right to eat from the tree of life in the Paradise of God.'),
('REV', 2, 8, 'REV.2.8', 'To the angel of the church in Smyrna write: These are the words of the First and the Last, who died and returned to life.'),
('REV', 2, 9, 'REV.2.9', 'I know your affliction and your poverty—though you are rich! And I am aware of the slander of those who falsely claim to be Jews, but are in fact a synagogue of Satan.'),
('REV', 2, 10, 'REV.2.10', 'Do not fear what you are about to suffer. Behold, the devil is about to throw some of you into prison to test you, and you will suffer tribulation for ten days. Be faithful even unto death, and I will give you the crown of life.'),
('REV', 2, 11, 'REV.2.11', 'He who has an ear, let him hear what the Spirit says to the churches. The one who overcomes will not be harmed by the second death.'),
('REV', 2, 12, 'REV.2.12', 'To the angel of the church in Pergamum write: These are the words of the One who holds the sharp, double-edged sword.'),
('REV', 2, 13, 'REV.2.13', 'I know where you live, where the throne of Satan sits, yet you hold fast to My name. You did not deny your faith in Me, even in the days of My faithful witness Antipas, who was killed among you where Satan dwells.'),
('REV', 2, 14, 'REV.2.14', 'But I have a few things against you, because some of you hold to the teaching of Balaam, who taught Balak to place a stumbling block before the Israelites so they would eat food sacrificed to idols and commit sexual immorality.'),
('REV', 2, 15, 'REV.2.15', 'In the same way, some of you also hold to the teaching of the Nicolaitans.'),
('REV', 2, 16, 'REV.2.16', 'Therefore repent! Otherwise I will come to you shortly and wage war against them with the sword of My mouth.'),
('REV', 2, 17, 'REV.2.17', 'He who has an ear, let him hear what the Spirit says to the churches. To the one who overcomes, I will give the hidden manna. I will also give him a white stone inscribed with a new name, known only to the one who receives it.'),
('REV', 2, 18, 'REV.2.18', 'To the angel of the church in Thyatira write: These are the words of the Son of God, whose eyes are like a blazing fire and whose feet are like polished bronze.'),
('REV', 2, 19, 'REV.2.19', 'I know your deeds—your love, your faith, your service, your perseverance—and your latest deeds are greater than your first.'),
('REV', 2, 20, 'REV.2.20', 'But I have this against you: You tolerate that woman Jezebel, who calls herself a prophetess. By her teaching she misleads My servants to be sexually immoral and to eat food sacrificed to idols.'),
('REV', 2, 21, 'REV.2.21', 'Even though I have given her time to repent of her immorality, she is unwilling.'),
('REV', 2, 22, 'REV.2.22', 'Behold, I will cast her onto a bed of sickness, and those who commit adultery with her will suffer great tribulation unless they repent of her deeds.'),
('REV', 2, 23, 'REV.2.23', 'Then I will strike her children dead, and all the churches will know that I am the One who searches minds and hearts, and I will repay each of you according to your deeds.'),
('REV', 2, 24, 'REV.2.24', 'But I say to the rest of you in Thyatira, who do not hold to her teaching and have not learned the so-called deep things of Satan: I will place no further burden upon you'),
('REV', 2, 25, 'REV.2.25', 'than to hold fast to what you have until I come.'),
('REV', 2, 26, 'REV.2.26', 'And to the one who overcomes and continues in My work until the end, I will give authority over the nations.'),
('REV', 2, 27, 'REV.2.27', 'He will rule them with an iron scepter and shatter them like pottery—just as I have received authority from My Father.'),
('REV', 2, 28, 'REV.2.28', 'And I will give him the morning star.'),
('REV', 2, 29, 'REV.2.29', 'He who has an ear, let him hear what the Spirit says to the churches.'),
('REV', 3, 1, 'REV.3.1', '“To the angel of the church in Sardis write: These are the words of the One who holds the seven spirits of God and the seven stars. I know your deeds; you have a reputation for being alive, yet you are dead.'),
('REV', 3, 2, 'REV.3.2', 'Wake up and strengthen what remains, which is about to die; for I have found your deeds incomplete in the sight of My God.'),
('REV', 3, 3, 'REV.3.3', 'Remember, then, what you have received and heard. Keep it and repent. If you do not wake up, I will come like a thief, and you will not know the hour when I will come upon you.'),
('REV', 3, 4, 'REV.3.4', 'But you do have a few people in Sardis who have not soiled their garments, and because they are worthy, they will walk with Me in white.'),
('REV', 3, 5, 'REV.3.5', 'Like them, he who overcomes will be dressed in white. And I will never blot out his name from the Book of Life, but I will confess his name before My Father and His angels.'),
('REV', 3, 6, 'REV.3.6', 'He who has an ear, let him hear what the Spirit says to the churches.'),
('REV', 3, 7, 'REV.3.7', 'To the angel of the church in Philadelphia write: These are the words of the One who is holy and true, who holds the key of David. What He opens no one can shut, and what He shuts no one can open.'),
('REV', 3, 8, 'REV.3.8', 'I know your deeds. Behold, I have placed before you an open door, which no one can shut. I know that you have only a little strength, yet you have kept My word and have not denied My name.'),
('REV', 3, 9, 'REV.3.9', 'As for those who belong to the synagogue of Satan, who claim to be Jews but are liars instead, I will make them come and bow down at your feet, and they will know that I love you.'),
('REV', 3, 10, 'REV.3.10', 'Because you have kept My command to persevere, I will also keep you from the hour of testing that is about to come upon the whole world, to test those who dwell on the earth.'),
('REV', 3, 11, 'REV.3.11', 'I am coming soon. Hold fast to what you have, so that no one will take your crown.'),
('REV', 3, 12, 'REV.3.12', 'The one who overcomes I will make a pillar in the temple of My God, and he will never again leave it. Upon him I will write the name of My God, and the name of the city of My God (the new Jerusalem that comes down out of heaven from My God), and My new name.'),
('REV', 3, 13, 'REV.3.13', 'He who has an ear, let him hear what the Spirit says to the churches.'),
('REV', 3, 14, 'REV.3.14', 'To the angel of the church in Laodicea write: These are the words of the Amen, the faithful and true Witness, the Originator of God’s creation.'),
('REV', 3, 15, 'REV.3.15', 'I know your deeds; you are neither cold nor hot. How I wish you were one or the other!'),
('REV', 3, 16, 'REV.3.16', 'So because you are lukewarm—neither hot nor cold—I am about to vomit you out of My mouth!'),
('REV', 3, 17, 'REV.3.17', 'You say, ‘I am rich; I have grown wealthy and need nothing.’ But you do not realize that you are wretched, pitiful, poor, blind, and naked.'),
('REV', 3, 18, 'REV.3.18', 'I counsel you to buy from Me gold refined by fire so that you may become rich, white garments so that you may be clothed and your shameful nakedness not exposed, and salve to anoint your eyes so that you may see.'),
('REV', 3, 19, 'REV.3.19', 'Those I love I rebuke and discipline. Therefore be earnest and repent.'),
('REV', 3, 20, 'REV.3.20', 'Behold, I stand at the door and knock. If anyone hears My voice and opens the door, I will come in and dine with him, and he with Me.'),
('REV', 3, 21, 'REV.3.21', 'To the one who overcomes, I will grant the right to sit with Me on My throne, just as I overcame and sat down with My Father on His throne.'),
('REV', 3, 22, 'REV.3.22', 'He who has an ear, let him hear what the Spirit says to the churches.”'),
('REV', 4, 1, 'REV.4.1', 'After this I looked and saw a door standing open in heaven. And the voice I had previously heard speak to me like a trumpet was saying, “Come up here, and I will show you what must happen after these things.”'),
('REV', 4, 2, 'REV.4.2', 'At once I was in the Spirit, and I saw a throne standing in heaven, with someone seated on it.'),
('REV', 4, 3, 'REV.4.3', 'The One seated there looked like jasper and carnelian, and a rainbow that gleamed like an emerald encircled the throne.'),
('REV', 4, 4, 'REV.4.4', 'Surrounding the throne were twenty-four other thrones, and on these thrones sat twenty-four elders dressed in white, with golden crowns on their heads.'),
('REV', 4, 5, 'REV.4.5', 'From the throne came flashes of lightning, rumblings, and peals of thunder. Before the throne burned seven torches of fire. These are the seven spirits of God.'),
('REV', 4, 6, 'REV.4.6', 'And before the throne was something like a sea of glass, as clear as crystal. In the center, around the throne, were four living creatures, covered with eyes in front and back.'),
('REV', 4, 7, 'REV.4.7', 'The first living creature was like a lion, the second like a calf, the third had a face like a man, and the fourth was like an eagle in flight.'),
('REV', 4, 8, 'REV.4.8', 'And each of the four living creatures had six wings and was covered with eyes all around and within. Day and night they never stop saying: “Holy, Holy, Holy, is the Lord God Almighty, who was and is and is to come!”'),
('REV', 4, 9, 'REV.4.9', 'And whenever the living creatures give glory, honor, and thanks to the One seated on the throne, who lives forever and ever,'),
('REV', 4, 10, 'REV.4.10', 'the twenty-four elders fall down before the One seated on the throne, and they worship Him who lives forever and ever. They cast their crowns before the throne, saying:'),
('REV', 4, 11, 'REV.4.11', '“Worthy are You, our Lord and God, to receive glory and honor and power, for You created all things; by Your will they exist and were created.”'),
('REV', 5, 1, 'REV.5.1', 'Then I saw a scroll in the right hand of the One seated on the throne. It had writing on both sides and was sealed with seven seals.'),
('REV', 5, 2, 'REV.5.2', 'And I saw a mighty angel proclaiming in a loud voice, “Who is worthy to break the seals and open the scroll?”'),
('REV', 5, 3, 'REV.5.3', 'But no one in heaven or on earth or under the earth was able to open the scroll or look inside it.'),
('REV', 5, 4, 'REV.5.4', 'And I began to weep bitterly, because no one was found worthy to open the scroll or look inside it.'),
('REV', 5, 5, 'REV.5.5', 'Then one of the elders said to me, “Do not weep! Behold, the Lion of the tribe of Judah, the Root of David, has triumphed to open the scroll and its seven seals.”'),
('REV', 5, 6, 'REV.5.6', 'Then I saw a Lamb who appeared to have been slain, standing in the center of the throne, encircled by the four living creatures and the elders. The Lamb had seven horns and seven eyes, which represent the seven spirits of God sent out into all the earth.'),
('REV', 5, 7, 'REV.5.7', 'And He came and took the scroll from the right hand of the One seated on the throne.'),
('REV', 5, 8, 'REV.5.8', 'When He had taken the scroll, the four living creatures and the twenty-four elders fell down before the Lamb. Each one had a harp, and they were holding golden bowls full of incense, which are the prayers of the saints.'),
('REV', 5, 9, 'REV.5.9', 'And they sang a new song: “Worthy are You to take the scroll and open its seals, because You were slain, and by Your blood You purchased for God those from every tribe and tongue and people and nation.'),
('REV', 5, 10, 'REV.5.10', 'You have made them to be a kingdom and priests to serve our God, and they will reign upon the earth.”'),
('REV', 5, 11, 'REV.5.11', 'Then I looked, and I heard the voices of many angels encircling the throne, and the living creatures and the elders. And their number was myriads of myriads and thousands of thousands.'),
('REV', 5, 12, 'REV.5.12', 'In a loud voice they were saying: “Worthy is the Lamb who was slain, to receive power and riches and wisdom and strength and honor and glory and blessing!”'),
('REV', 5, 13, 'REV.5.13', 'And I heard every creature in heaven and on earth and under the earth and in the sea, and all that is in them, saying: “To Him who sits on the throne and to the Lamb be praise and honor and glory and power forever and ever!”'),
('REV', 5, 14, 'REV.5.14', 'And the four living creatures said, “Amen,” and the elders fell down and worshiped.'),
('REV', 6, 1, 'REV.6.1', 'Then I watched as the Lamb opened one of the seven seals, and I heard one of the four living creatures say in a voice like thunder, “Come!”'),
('REV', 6, 2, 'REV.6.2', 'So I looked and saw a white horse, and its rider held a bow. And he was given a crown, and he rode out to overcome and conquer.'),
('REV', 6, 3, 'REV.6.3', 'And when the Lamb opened the second seal, I heard the second living creature say, “Come!”'),
('REV', 6, 4, 'REV.6.4', 'Then another horse went forth. It was bright red, and its rider was granted permission to take away peace from the earth and to make men slay one another. And he was given a great sword.'),
('REV', 6, 5, 'REV.6.5', 'And when the Lamb opened the third seal, I heard the third living creature say, “Come!” Then I looked and saw a black horse, and its rider held in his hand a pair of scales.'),
('REV', 6, 6, 'REV.6.6', 'And I heard what sounded like a voice from among the four living creatures, saying, “A quart of wheat for a denarius, and three quarts of barley for a denarius, and do not harm the oil and wine.”'),
('REV', 6, 7, 'REV.6.7', 'And when the Lamb opened the fourth seal, I heard the voice of the fourth living creature say, “Come!”'),
('REV', 6, 8, 'REV.6.8', 'Then I looked and saw a pale green horse. Its rider’s name was Death, and Hades followed close behind. And they were given authority over a fourth of the earth, to kill by sword, by famine, by plague, and by the beasts of the earth.'),
('REV', 6, 9, 'REV.6.9', 'And when the Lamb opened the fifth seal, I saw under the altar the souls of those who had been slain for the word of God and for the testimony they had upheld.'),
('REV', 6, 10, 'REV.6.10', 'And they cried out in a loud voice, “How long, O Lord, holy and true, until You judge those who dwell upon the earth and avenge our blood?”'),
('REV', 6, 11, 'REV.6.11', 'Then each of them was given a white robe and told to rest a little while longer until the full number of their fellow servants, their brothers, were killed, just as they had been killed.'),
('REV', 6, 12, 'REV.6.12', 'And I watched as the Lamb opened the sixth seal, and there was a great earthquake, and the sun became black like sackcloth of goat hair, and the whole moon turned blood red,'),
('REV', 6, 13, 'REV.6.13', 'and the stars of the sky fell to the earth like unripe figs dropping from a tree shaken by a great wind.'),
('REV', 6, 14, 'REV.6.14', 'The sky receded like a scroll being rolled up, and every mountain and island was moved from its place.'),
('REV', 6, 15, 'REV.6.15', 'Then the kings of the earth, the nobles, the commanders, the rich, the mighty, and every slave and free man hid in the caves and among the rocks of the mountains.'),
('REV', 6, 16, 'REV.6.16', 'And they said to the mountains and the rocks, “Fall on us and hide us from the face of the One seated on the throne, and from the wrath of the Lamb.'),
('REV', 6, 17, 'REV.6.17', 'For the great day of Their wrath has come, and who is able to withstand it?”'),
('REV', 7, 1, 'REV.7.1', 'After this I saw four angels standing at the four corners of the earth, holding back its four winds so that no wind would blow on land or sea or on any tree.'),
('REV', 7, 2, 'REV.7.2', 'And I saw another angel ascending from the east, with the seal of the living God. And he called out in a loud voice to the four angels who had been given power to harm the land and the sea:'),
('REV', 7, 3, 'REV.7.3', '“Do not harm the land or sea or trees until we have placed a seal on the foreheads of the servants of our God.”'),
('REV', 7, 4, 'REV.7.4', 'And I heard the number of those who were sealed, 144,000 from all the tribes of Israel:'),
('REV', 7, 5, 'REV.7.5', 'From the tribe of Judah 12,000 were sealed, from the tribe of Reuben 12,000, from the tribe of Gad 12,000,'),
('REV', 7, 6, 'REV.7.6', 'from the tribe of Asher 12,000, from the tribe of Naphtali 12,000, from the tribe of Manasseh 12,000,'),
('REV', 7, 7, 'REV.7.7', 'from the tribe of Simeon 12,000, from the tribe of Levi 12,000, from the tribe of Issachar 12,000,'),
('REV', 7, 8, 'REV.7.8', 'from the tribe of Zebulun 12,000, from the tribe of Joseph 12,000, and from the tribe of Benjamin 12,000.'),
('REV', 7, 9, 'REV.7.9', 'After this I looked and saw a multitude too large to count, from every nation and tribe and people and tongue, standing before the throne and before the Lamb. They were wearing white robes and holding palm branches in their hands.'),
('REV', 7, 10, 'REV.7.10', 'And they cried out in a loud voice: “Salvation to our God, who sits on the throne, and to the Lamb!”'),
('REV', 7, 11, 'REV.7.11', 'And all the angels stood around the throne and around the elders and the four living creatures. And they fell facedown before the throne and worshiped God,'),
('REV', 7, 12, 'REV.7.12', 'saying, “Amen! Blessing and glory and wisdom and thanks and honor and power and strength be to our God forever and ever! Amen.”'),
('REV', 7, 13, 'REV.7.13', 'Then one of the elders addressed me: “These in white robes,” he asked, “who are they, and where have they come from?”'),
('REV', 7, 14, 'REV.7.14', '“Sir,” I answered, “you know.” So he replied, “These are the ones who have come out of the great tribulation; they have washed their robes and made them white in the blood of the Lamb.'),
('REV', 7, 15, 'REV.7.15', 'For this reason, they are before the throne of God and serve Him day and night in His temple; and the One seated on the throne will spread His tabernacle over them.'),
('REV', 7, 16, 'REV.7.16', '‘Never again will they hunger, and never will they thirst; nor will the sun beat down upon them, nor any scorching heat.’'),
('REV', 7, 17, 'REV.7.17', 'For the Lamb in the center of the throne will be their shepherd. ‘He will lead them to springs of living water,’ and ‘God will wipe away every tear from their eyes.’”'),
('REV', 8, 1, 'REV.8.1', 'When the Lamb opened the seventh seal, there was silence in heaven for about half an hour.'),
('REV', 8, 2, 'REV.8.2', 'And I saw the seven angels who stand before God, and they were given seven trumpets.'),
('REV', 8, 3, 'REV.8.3', 'Then another angel, who had a golden censer, came and stood at the altar. He was given much incense to offer, along with the prayers of all the saints, on the golden altar before the throne.'),
('REV', 8, 4, 'REV.8.4', 'And the smoke of the incense, together with the prayers of the saints, rose up before God from the hand of the angel.'),
('REV', 8, 5, 'REV.8.5', 'Then the angel took the censer, filled it with fire from the altar, and hurled it to the earth; and there were peals of thunder, rumblings, flashes of lightning, and an earthquake.'),
('REV', 8, 6, 'REV.8.6', 'And the seven angels with the seven trumpets prepared to sound them.'),
('REV', 8, 7, 'REV.8.7', 'Then the first angel sounded his trumpet, and hail and fire mixed with blood were hurled down upon the earth. A third of the earth was burned up, along with a third of the trees and all the green grass.'),
('REV', 8, 8, 'REV.8.8', 'Then the second angel sounded his trumpet, and something like a great mountain burning with fire was thrown into the sea. A third of the sea turned to blood,'),
('REV', 8, 9, 'REV.8.9', 'a third of the living creatures in the sea died, and a third of the ships were destroyed.'),
('REV', 8, 10, 'REV.8.10', 'Then the third angel sounded his trumpet, and a great star burning like a torch fell from heaven and landed on a third of the rivers and on the springs of water.'),
('REV', 8, 11, 'REV.8.11', 'The name of the star is Wormwood. A third of the waters turned bitter like wormwood oil, and many people died from the bitter waters.'),
('REV', 8, 12, 'REV.8.12', 'Then the fourth angel sounded his trumpet, and a third of the sun and moon and stars were struck. A third of the stars were darkened, a third of the day was without light, and a third of the night as well.'),
('REV', 8, 13, 'REV.8.13', 'And as I observed, I heard an eagle flying overhead, calling in a loud voice, “Woe! Woe! Woe to those who dwell on the earth, because of the trumpet blasts about to be sounded by the remaining three angels!”'),
('REV', 9, 1, 'REV.9.1', 'Then the fifth angel sounded his trumpet, and I saw a star that had fallen from heaven to earth, and it was given the key to the pit of the Abyss.'),
('REV', 9, 2, 'REV.9.2', 'The star opened the pit of the Abyss, and smoke rose out of it like the smoke of a great furnace, and the sun and the air were darkened by the smoke from the pit.'),
('REV', 9, 3, 'REV.9.3', 'And out of the smoke, locusts descended on the earth, and they were given power like that of the scorpions of the earth.'),
('REV', 9, 4, 'REV.9.4', 'They were told not to harm the grass of the earth or any plant or tree, but only those who did not have the seal of God on their foreheads.'),
('REV', 9, 5, 'REV.9.5', 'The locusts were not given power to kill them, but only to torment them for five months, and their torment was like the stinging of a scorpion.'),
('REV', 9, 6, 'REV.9.6', 'In those days men will seek death and will not find it; they will long to die, but death will escape them.'),
('REV', 9, 7, 'REV.9.7', 'And the locusts looked like horses prepared for battle, with something like crowns of gold on their heads; and their faces were like the faces of men.'),
('REV', 9, 8, 'REV.9.8', 'They had hair like that of women, and teeth like those of lions.'),
('REV', 9, 9, 'REV.9.9', 'They also had breastplates like breastplates of iron, and the sound of their wings was like the roar of many horses and chariots rushing into battle.'),
('REV', 9, 10, 'REV.9.10', 'They had tails with stingers like scorpions, which had the power to injure people for five months.'),
('REV', 9, 11, 'REV.9.11', 'They were ruled by a king, the angel of the Abyss. His name in Hebrew is Abaddon, and in Greek it is Apollyon.'),
('REV', 9, 12, 'REV.9.12', 'The first woe has passed. Behold, two woes are still to follow.'),
('REV', 9, 13, 'REV.9.13', 'Then the sixth angel sounded his trumpet, and I heard a voice from the four horns of the golden altar before God'),
('REV', 9, 14, 'REV.9.14', 'saying to the sixth angel with the trumpet, “Release the four angels who are bound at the great river Euphrates.”'),
('REV', 9, 15, 'REV.9.15', 'So the four angels who had been prepared for this hour and day and month and year were released to kill a third of mankind.'),
('REV', 9, 16, 'REV.9.16', 'And the number of mounted troops was two hundred million; I heard their number.'),
('REV', 9, 17, 'REV.9.17', 'Now the horses and riders in my vision looked like this: The riders had breastplates the colors of fire, sapphire, and sulfur. The heads of the horses were like the heads of lions, and out of their mouths proceeded fire, smoke, and sulfur.'),
('REV', 9, 18, 'REV.9.18', 'A third of mankind was killed by the three plagues of fire, smoke, and sulfur that proceeded from their mouths.'),
('REV', 9, 19, 'REV.9.19', 'For the power of the horses was in their mouths and in their tails; indeed, their tails were like snakes, having heads with which to inflict harm.'),
('REV', 9, 20, 'REV.9.20', 'Now the rest of mankind who were not killed by these plagues still did not repent of the works of their hands. They did not stop worshiping demons and idols of gold, silver, bronze, stone, and wood, which cannot see or hear or walk.'),
('REV', 9, 21, 'REV.9.21', 'Furthermore, they did not repent of their murder, sorcery, sexual immorality, and theft.'),
('REV', 10, 1, 'REV.10.1', 'Then I saw another mighty angel coming down from heaven, wrapped in a cloud, with a rainbow above his head. His face was like the sun, and his legs were like pillars of fire.'),
('REV', 10, 2, 'REV.10.2', 'He held in his hand a small scroll, which lay open. He placed his right foot on the sea and his left foot on the land.'),
('REV', 10, 3, 'REV.10.3', 'Then he cried out in a loud voice like the roar of a lion. And when he cried out, the seven thunders sounded their voices.'),
('REV', 10, 4, 'REV.10.4', 'When the seven thunders had spoken, I was about to put it in writing. But I heard a voice from heaven saying, “Seal up what the seven thunders have said, and do not write it down.”'),
('REV', 10, 5, 'REV.10.5', 'Then the angel I had seen standing on the sea and on the land lifted up his right hand to heaven.'),
('REV', 10, 6, 'REV.10.6', 'And he swore by Him who lives forever and ever, who created heaven and everything in it, the earth and everything in it, and the sea and everything in it: “There will be no more delay!'),
('REV', 10, 7, 'REV.10.7', 'But in the days of the voice of the seventh angel, when he begins to sound his trumpet, the mystery of God will be fulfilled, just as He proclaimed to His servants the prophets.”'),
('REV', 10, 8, 'REV.10.8', 'Then the voice that I had heard from heaven spoke to me again, saying, “Go, take the small scroll that lies open in the hand of the angel standing on the sea and on the land.”'),
('REV', 10, 9, 'REV.10.9', 'And I went to the angel and said, “Give me the small scroll.” “Take it and eat it,” he said. “It will make your stomach bitter, but in your mouth it will be as sweet as honey.”'),
('REV', 10, 10, 'REV.10.10', 'So I took the small scroll from the angel’s hand and ate it, and it was as sweet as honey in my mouth. But when I had eaten it, my stomach turned bitter.'),
('REV', 10, 11, 'REV.10.11', 'And they told me, “You must prophesy again about many peoples and nations and tongues and kings.”'),
('REV', 11, 1, 'REV.11.1', 'Then I was given a measuring rod like a staff and was told, “Go and measure the temple of God and the altar, and count the number of worshipers there.'),
('REV', 11, 2, 'REV.11.2', 'But exclude the courtyard outside the temple. Do not measure it, because it has been given over to the nations, and they will trample the holy city for 42 months.'),
('REV', 11, 3, 'REV.11.3', 'And I will empower my two witnesses, and they will prophesy for 1,260 days, clothed in sackcloth.”'),
('REV', 11, 4, 'REV.11.4', 'These witnesses are the two olive trees and the two lampstands that stand before the Lord of the earth.'),
('REV', 11, 5, 'REV.11.5', 'If anyone wants to harm them, fire proceeds from their mouths and devours their enemies. In this way, anyone who wants to harm them must be killed.'),
('REV', 11, 6, 'REV.11.6', 'These witnesses have power to shut the sky so that no rain will fall during the days of their prophecy, and power to turn the waters into blood and to strike the earth with every kind of plague as often as they wish.'),
('REV', 11, 7, 'REV.11.7', 'When the two witnesses have finished their testimony, the beast that comes up from the Abyss will wage war with them, and will overpower and kill them.'),
('REV', 11, 8, 'REV.11.8', 'Their bodies will lie in the street of the great city—figuratively called Sodom and Egypt—where their Lord was also crucified.'),
('REV', 11, 9, 'REV.11.9', 'For three and a half days all peoples and tribes and tongues and nations will view their bodies and will not permit them to be laid in a tomb.'),
('REV', 11, 10, 'REV.11.10', 'And those who dwell on the earth will gloat over them and celebrate and send one another gifts, because these two prophets had tormented them.'),
('REV', 11, 11, 'REV.11.11', 'But after the three and a half days, the breath of life from God entered the two witnesses, and they stood on their feet, and great fear fell upon those who saw them.'),
('REV', 11, 12, 'REV.11.12', 'And the witnesses heard a loud voice from heaven saying, “Come up here.” And they went up to heaven in a cloud as their enemies watched them.'),
('REV', 11, 13, 'REV.11.13', 'And in that hour there was a great earthquake, and a tenth of the city collapsed. Seven thousand were killed in the quake, and the rest were terrified and gave glory to the God of heaven.'),
('REV', 11, 14, 'REV.11.14', 'The second woe has passed. Behold, the third woe is coming shortly.'),
('REV', 11, 15, 'REV.11.15', 'Then the seventh angel sounded his trumpet, and loud voices called out in heaven: “The kingdom of the world has become the kingdom of our Lord and of His Christ, and He will reign forever and ever.”'),
('REV', 11, 16, 'REV.11.16', 'And the twenty-four elders who sit on their thrones before God fell on their faces and worshiped God,'),
('REV', 11, 17, 'REV.11.17', 'saying: “We give thanks to You, O Lord God Almighty, the One who is and who was, because You have taken Your great power and have begun to reign.'),
('REV', 11, 18, 'REV.11.18', 'The nations were enraged, and Your wrath has come. The time has come to judge the dead and to reward Your servants the prophets, as well as the saints and those who fear Your name, both small and great—and to destroy those who destroy the earth.”'),
('REV', 11, 19, 'REV.11.19', 'Then the temple of God in heaven was opened, and the ark of His covenant appeared in His temple. And there were flashes of lightning, rumblings, peals of thunder, an earthquake, and a great hailstorm.'),
('REV', 12, 1, 'REV.12.1', 'And a great sign appeared in heaven: a woman clothed in the sun, with the moon under her feet and a crown of twelve stars on her head.'),
('REV', 12, 2, 'REV.12.2', 'She was pregnant and crying out in the pain and agony of giving birth.'),
('REV', 12, 3, 'REV.12.3', 'Then another sign appeared in heaven: a huge red dragon with seven heads, ten horns, and seven royal crowns on his heads.'),
('REV', 12, 4, 'REV.12.4', 'His tail swept a third of the stars from the sky, hurling them to the earth. And the dragon stood before the woman who was about to give birth, ready to devour her child as soon as she gave birth.'),
('REV', 12, 5, 'REV.12.5', 'And she gave birth to a son, a male child, who will rule all the nations with an iron scepter. And her child was caught up to God and to His throne.'),
('REV', 12, 6, 'REV.12.6', 'And the woman fled into the wilderness, where God had prepared a place for her to be nourished for 1,260 days.'),
('REV', 12, 7, 'REV.12.7', 'Then a war broke out in heaven: Michael and his angels fought against the dragon, and the dragon and his angels fought back.'),
('REV', 12, 8, 'REV.12.8', 'But the dragon was not strong enough, and no longer was any place found in heaven for him and his angels.'),
('REV', 12, 9, 'REV.12.9', 'And the great dragon was hurled down—that ancient serpent called the devil and Satan, the deceiver of the whole world. He was hurled to the earth, and his angels with him.'),
('REV', 12, 10, 'REV.12.10', 'And I heard a loud voice in heaven saying: “Now have come the salvation and the power and the kingdom of our God, and the authority of His Christ. For the accuser of our brothers has been thrown down—he who accuses them day and night before our God.'),
('REV', 12, 11, 'REV.12.11', 'They have conquered him by the blood of the Lamb and by the word of their testimony. And they did not love their lives so as to shy away from death.'),
('REV', 12, 12, 'REV.12.12', 'Therefore rejoice, O heavens, and you who dwell in them! But woe to the earth and the sea; with great fury the devil has come down to you, knowing he has only a short time.”'),
('REV', 12, 13, 'REV.12.13', 'And when the dragon saw that he had been thrown to the earth, he pursued the woman who had given birth to the male child.'),
('REV', 12, 14, 'REV.12.14', 'But the woman was given two wings of a great eagle to fly from the presence of the serpent to her place in the wilderness, where she was nourished for a time, and times, and half a time.'),
('REV', 12, 15, 'REV.12.15', 'Then from his mouth the serpent spewed water like a river to overtake the woman and sweep her away in the torrent.'),
('REV', 12, 16, 'REV.12.16', 'But the earth helped the woman and opened its mouth to swallow up the river that the dragon had poured from his mouth.'),
('REV', 12, 17, 'REV.12.17', 'And the dragon was enraged at the woman and went to make war with the rest of her children, who keep the commandments of God and hold to the testimony of Jesus. And the dragon stood on the shore of the sea.'),
('REV', 13, 1, 'REV.13.1', 'Then I saw a beast with ten horns and seven heads rising out of the sea. There were ten royal crowns on its horns and blasphemous names on its heads.'),
('REV', 13, 2, 'REV.13.2', 'The beast I saw was like a leopard, with the feet of a bear and the mouth of a lion. And the dragon gave the beast his power and his throne and great authority.'),
('REV', 13, 3, 'REV.13.3', 'One of the heads of the beast appeared to have been mortally wounded. But the mortal wound was healed, and the whole world marveled and followed the beast.'),
('REV', 13, 4, 'REV.13.4', 'They worshiped the dragon who had given authority to the beast, and they worshiped the beast, saying, “Who is like the beast, and who can wage war against it?”'),
('REV', 13, 5, 'REV.13.5', 'The beast was given a mouth to speak arrogant and blasphemous words, and authority to act for 42 months.'),
('REV', 13, 6, 'REV.13.6', 'And the beast opened its mouth to speak blasphemies against God and to slander His name and His tabernacle—those who dwell in heaven.'),
('REV', 13, 7, 'REV.13.7', 'Then the beast was permitted to wage war against the saints and to conquer them, and it was given authority over every tribe and people and tongue and nation.'),
('REV', 13, 8, 'REV.13.8', 'And all who dwell on the earth will worship the beast—all whose names have not been written from the foundation of the world in the Book of Life belonging to the Lamb who was slain.'),
('REV', 13, 9, 'REV.13.9', 'He who has an ear, let him hear:'),
('REV', 13, 10, 'REV.13.10', '“If anyone is destined for captivity, into captivity he will go; if anyone is to die by the sword, by the sword he must be killed.” Here is a call for the perseverance and faith of the saints.'),
('REV', 13, 11, 'REV.13.11', 'Then I saw another beast rising out of the earth. This beast had two horns like a lamb, but spoke like a dragon.'),
('REV', 13, 12, 'REV.13.12', 'And this beast exercised all the authority of the first beast and caused the earth and those who dwell in it to worship the first beast, whose mortal wound had been healed.'),
('REV', 13, 13, 'REV.13.13', 'And the second beast performed great signs, even causing fire from heaven to come down to earth in the presence of the people.'),
('REV', 13, 14, 'REV.13.14', 'Because of the signs it was given to perform on behalf of the first beast, it deceived those who dwell on the earth, telling them to make an image to the beast that had been wounded by the sword and yet had lived.'),
('REV', 13, 15, 'REV.13.15', 'The second beast was permitted to give breath to the image of the first beast, so that the image could speak and cause all who refused to worship it to be killed.'),
('REV', 13, 16, 'REV.13.16', 'And the second beast required all people, small and great, rich and poor, free and slave, to receive a mark on their right hand or on their forehead,'),
('REV', 13, 17, 'REV.13.17', 'so that no one could buy or sell unless he had the mark—the name of the beast or the number of its name.'),
('REV', 13, 18, 'REV.13.18', 'Here is a call for wisdom: Let the one who has insight calculate the number of the beast, for it is the number of a man, and that number is 666.'),
('REV', 14, 1, 'REV.14.1', 'Then I looked and saw the Lamb standing on Mount Zion, and with Him 144,000 who had His name and His Father’s name written on their foreheads.'),
('REV', 14, 2, 'REV.14.2', 'And I heard a sound from heaven like the roar of many waters and the loud rumbling of thunder. And the sound I heard was like harpists strumming their harps.'),
('REV', 14, 3, 'REV.14.3', 'And they sang a new song before the throne and before the four living creatures and the elders. And no one could learn the song except the 144,000 who had been redeemed from the earth.'),
('REV', 14, 4, 'REV.14.4', 'These are the ones who have not been defiled with women, for they are virgins. They follow the Lamb wherever He goes. They have been redeemed from among men as firstfruits to God and to the Lamb.'),
('REV', 14, 5, 'REV.14.5', 'And no lie was found in their mouths; they are blameless.'),
('REV', 14, 6, 'REV.14.6', 'Then I saw another angel flying overhead, with the eternal gospel to proclaim to those who dwell on the earth—to every nation and tribe and tongue and people.'),
('REV', 14, 7, 'REV.14.7', 'And he said in a loud voice, “Fear God and give Him glory, because the hour of His judgment has come. Worship the One who made the heavens and the earth and the sea and the springs of waters.”'),
('REV', 14, 8, 'REV.14.8', 'Then a second angel followed, saying, “Fallen, fallen is Babylon the great, who has made all the nations drink the wine of the passion of her immorality.”'),
('REV', 14, 9, 'REV.14.9', 'And a third angel followed them, calling out in a loud voice, “If anyone worships the beast and its image and receives its mark on his forehead or on his hand,'),
('REV', 14, 10, 'REV.14.10', 'he too will drink the wine of God’s anger, poured undiluted into the cup of His wrath. And he will be tormented in fire and sulfur in the presence of the holy angels and of the Lamb.'),
('REV', 14, 11, 'REV.14.11', 'And the smoke of their torment rises forever and ever. Day and night there is no rest for those who worship the beast and its image, or for anyone who receives the mark of its name.”'),
('REV', 14, 12, 'REV.14.12', 'Here is a call for the perseverance of the saints, who keep the commandments of God and the faith of Jesus.'),
('REV', 14, 13, 'REV.14.13', 'And I heard a voice from heaven telling me to write, “Blessed are the dead—those who die in the Lord from this moment on.” “Yes,” says the Spirit, “they will rest from their labors, for their deeds will follow them.”'),
('REV', 14, 14, 'REV.14.14', 'And I looked and saw a white cloud, and seated on the cloud was One like the Son of Man, with a golden crown on His head and a sharp sickle in His hand.'),
('REV', 14, 15, 'REV.14.15', 'Then another angel came out of the temple, crying out in a loud voice to the One seated on the cloud, “Swing Your sickle and reap, because the time has come to harvest, for the crop of the earth is ripe.”'),
('REV', 14, 16, 'REV.14.16', 'So the One seated on the cloud swung His sickle over the earth, and the earth was harvested.'),
('REV', 14, 17, 'REV.14.17', 'Then another angel came out of the temple in heaven, and he too had a sharp sickle.'),
('REV', 14, 18, 'REV.14.18', 'Still another angel, with authority over the fire, came from the altar and called out in a loud voice to the angel with the sharp sickle, “Swing your sharp sickle and gather the clusters of grapes from the vine of the earth, because its grapes are ripe.”'),
('REV', 14, 19, 'REV.14.19', 'So the angel swung his sickle over the earth and gathered the grapes of the earth, and he threw them into the great winepress of God’s wrath.'),
('REV', 14, 20, 'REV.14.20', 'And the winepress was trodden outside the city, and the blood that flowed from it rose as high as the bridles of the horses for a distance of 1,600 stadia.'),
('REV', 15, 1, 'REV.15.1', 'Then I saw another great and marvelous sign in heaven: seven angels with the seven final plagues, with which the wrath of God is completed.'),
('REV', 15, 2, 'REV.15.2', 'And I saw something like a sea of glass mixed with fire, beside which stood those who had conquered the beast and its image and the number of its name. They were holding harps from God,'),
('REV', 15, 3, 'REV.15.3', 'and they sang the song of God’s servant Moses and of the Lamb: “Great and wonderful are Your works, O Lord God Almighty! Just and true are Your ways, O King of the nations!'),
('REV', 15, 4, 'REV.15.4', 'Who will not fear You, O Lord, and glorify Your name? For You alone are holy. All nations will come and worship before You, for Your righteous acts have been revealed.”'),
('REV', 15, 5, 'REV.15.5', 'After this I looked, and the temple—the tabernacle of the Testimony—was opened in heaven.'),
('REV', 15, 6, 'REV.15.6', 'And out of the temple came the seven angels with the seven plagues, dressed in clean and bright linen and girded with golden sashes around their chests.'),
('REV', 15, 7, 'REV.15.7', 'Then one of the four living creatures gave the seven angels seven golden bowls full of the wrath of God, who lives forever and ever.'),
('REV', 15, 8, 'REV.15.8', 'And the temple was filled with smoke from the glory of God and from His power; and no one could enter the temple until the seven plagues of the seven angels were completed.'),
('REV', 16, 1, 'REV.16.1', 'Then I heard a loud voice from the temple saying to the seven angels, “Go, pour out on the earth the seven bowls of God’s wrath.”'),
('REV', 16, 2, 'REV.16.2', 'So the first angel went and poured out his bowl on the earth, and loathsome, malignant sores broke out on those who had the mark of the beast and worshiped its image.'),
('REV', 16, 3, 'REV.16.3', 'And the second angel poured out his bowl into the sea, and it turned to blood like that of the dead, and every living thing in the sea died.'),
('REV', 16, 4, 'REV.16.4', 'And the third angel poured out his bowl into the rivers and springs of water, and they turned to blood.'),
('REV', 16, 5, 'REV.16.5', 'And I heard the angel of the waters say: “Righteous are You, O Holy One, who is and was, because You have brought these judgments.'),
('REV', 16, 6, 'REV.16.6', 'For they have spilled the blood of saints and prophets, and You have given them blood to drink, as they deserve.”'),
('REV', 16, 7, 'REV.16.7', 'And I heard the altar reply: “Yes, Lord God Almighty, true and just are Your judgments.”'),
('REV', 16, 8, 'REV.16.8', 'Then the fourth angel poured out his bowl on the sun, and it was given power to scorch the people with fire.'),
('REV', 16, 9, 'REV.16.9', 'And the people were scorched by intense heat, and they cursed the name of God, who had authority over these plagues. Yet they did not repent and give Him glory.'),
('REV', 16, 10, 'REV.16.10', 'And the fifth angel poured out his bowl on the throne of the beast, and its kingdom was plunged into darkness, and men began to gnaw their tongues in anguish'),
('REV', 16, 11, 'REV.16.11', 'and curse the God of heaven for their pains and sores. Yet they did not repent of their deeds.'),
('REV', 16, 12, 'REV.16.12', 'And the sixth angel poured out his bowl on the great river Euphrates, and its water was dried up to prepare the way for the kings of the East.'),
('REV', 16, 13, 'REV.16.13', 'And I saw three unclean spirits that looked like frogs coming out of the mouths of the dragon, the beast, and the false prophet.'),
('REV', 16, 14, 'REV.16.14', 'These are demonic spirits that perform signs and go out to all the kings of the earth, to assemble them for battle on the great day of God the Almighty.'),
('REV', 16, 15, 'REV.16.15', '“Behold, I am coming like a thief. Blessed is the one who remains awake and clothed, so that he will not go naked and let his shame be exposed.”'),
('REV', 16, 16, 'REV.16.16', 'And they assembled the kings in the place that in Hebrew is called Armageddon.'),
('REV', 16, 17, 'REV.16.17', 'Then the seventh angel poured out his bowl into the air, and a loud voice came from the throne in the temple, saying, “It is done!”'),
('REV', 16, 18, 'REV.16.18', 'And there were flashes of lightning, rumblings, peals of thunder, and a great earthquake the likes of which had not occurred since men were upon the earth—so mighty was the great quake.'),
('REV', 16, 19, 'REV.16.19', 'The great city was split into three parts, and the cities of the nations collapsed. And God remembered Babylon the great and gave her the cup of the wine of the fury of His wrath.'),
('REV', 16, 20, 'REV.16.20', 'Then every island fled, and no mountain could be found.'),
('REV', 16, 21, 'REV.16.21', 'And great hailstones weighing almost a hundred pounds each rained down on them from above. And men cursed God for the plague of hail, because it was so horrendous.'),
('REV', 17, 1, 'REV.17.1', 'Then one of the seven angels with the seven bowls came and said to me, “Come, I will show you the punishment of the great prostitute, who sits on many waters.'),
('REV', 17, 2, 'REV.17.2', 'The kings of the earth were immoral with her, and those who dwell on the earth were intoxicated with the wine of her immorality.”'),
('REV', 17, 3, 'REV.17.3', 'And the angel carried me away in the Spirit into a wilderness, where I saw a woman sitting on a scarlet beast that was covered with blasphemous names and had seven heads and ten horns.'),
('REV', 17, 4, 'REV.17.4', 'The woman was dressed in purple and scarlet, and adorned with gold and precious stones and pearls. She held in her hand a golden cup full of abominations and the impurities of her sexual immorality.'),
('REV', 17, 5, 'REV.17.5', 'And on her forehead a mysterious name was written: BABYLON THE GREAT, THE MOTHER OF PROSTITUTES AND OF THE ABOMINATIONS OF THE EARTH.'),
('REV', 17, 6, 'REV.17.6', 'I could see that the woman was drunk with the blood of the saints and witnesses for Jesus. And I was utterly amazed at the sight of her.'),
('REV', 17, 7, 'REV.17.7', '“Why are you so amazed?” said the angel. “I will tell you the mystery of the woman and of the beast that carries her, which has the seven heads and ten horns.'),
('REV', 17, 8, 'REV.17.8', 'The beast that you saw—it was, and now is no more, but is about to come up out of the Abyss and go to its destruction. And those who dwell on the earth whose names were not written in the Book of Life from the foundation of the world will marvel when they see the beast that was, and is not, and yet will be.'),
('REV', 17, 9, 'REV.17.9', 'This calls for a mind with wisdom. The seven heads are seven mountains on which the woman sits.'),
('REV', 17, 10, 'REV.17.10', 'There are also seven kings. Five have fallen, one is, and the other has not yet come. But when he does come, he must remain for only a little while.'),
('REV', 17, 11, 'REV.17.11', 'The beast that was, and now is not, is an eighth king, who belongs to the other seven and is going into destruction.'),
('REV', 17, 12, 'REV.17.12', 'The ten horns you saw are ten kings who have not yet received a kingdom, but will receive one hour of authority as kings along with the beast.'),
('REV', 17, 13, 'REV.17.13', 'These kings have one purpose: to yield their power and authority to the beast.'),
('REV', 17, 14, 'REV.17.14', 'They will make war against the Lamb, and the Lamb will triumph over them, because He is Lord of lords and King of kings; and He will be accompanied by His called and chosen and faithful ones.”'),
('REV', 17, 15, 'REV.17.15', 'Then the angel said to me, “The waters you saw, where the prostitute was seated, are peoples and multitudes and nations and tongues.'),
('REV', 17, 16, 'REV.17.16', 'And the ten horns and the beast that you saw will hate the prostitute. They will leave her desolate and naked, and they will eat her flesh and burn her with fire.'),
('REV', 17, 17, 'REV.17.17', 'For God has put it into their hearts to carry out His purpose by uniting to give their kingdom to the beast, until the words of God are fulfilled.'),
('REV', 17, 18, 'REV.17.18', 'And the woman you saw is the great city that rules over the kings of the earth.”'),
('REV', 18, 1, 'REV.18.1', 'After this I saw another angel descending from heaven with great authority, and the earth was illuminated by his glory.'),
('REV', 18, 2, 'REV.18.2', 'And he cried out in a mighty voice: “Fallen, fallen is Babylon the great! She has become a lair for demons and a haunt for every unclean spirit, every unclean bird, and every detestable beast.'),
('REV', 18, 3, 'REV.18.3', 'All the nations have drunk the wine of the passion of her immorality. The kings of the earth were immoral with her, and the merchants of the earth have grown wealthy from the extravagance of her luxury.”'),
('REV', 18, 4, 'REV.18.4', 'Then I heard another voice from heaven say: “Come out of her, My people, so that you will not share in her sins or contract any of her plagues.'),
('REV', 18, 5, 'REV.18.5', 'For her sins are piled up to heaven, and God has remembered her iniquities.'),
('REV', 18, 6, 'REV.18.6', 'Give back to her as she has done to others; pay her back double for what she has done; mix her a double portion in her own cup.'),
('REV', 18, 7, 'REV.18.7', 'As much as she has glorified herself and lived in luxury, give her the same measure of torment and grief. In her heart she says, ‘I sit as queen; I am not a widow and will never see grief.’'),
('REV', 18, 8, 'REV.18.8', 'Therefore her plagues will come in one day—death and grief and famine—and she will be consumed by fire, for mighty is the Lord God who judges her.”'),
('REV', 18, 9, 'REV.18.9', 'Then the kings of the earth who committed sexual immorality and lived in luxury with her will weep and wail at the sight of the smoke rising from the fire that consumes her.'),
('REV', 18, 10, 'REV.18.10', 'In fear of her torment, they will stand at a distance and cry out: “Woe, woe to the great city, the mighty city of Babylon! For in a single hour your judgment has come.”'),
('REV', 18, 11, 'REV.18.11', 'And the merchants of the earth will weep and mourn over her, because there is no one left to buy their cargo—'),
('REV', 18, 12, 'REV.18.12', 'cargo of gold, silver, precious stones, and pearls; of fine linen, purple, silk, and scarlet; of all kinds of citron wood and every article of ivory, precious wood, bronze, iron, and marble;'),
('REV', 18, 13, 'REV.18.13', 'of cinnamon, spice, incense, myrrh, and frankincense; of wine, olive oil, fine flour, and wheat; of cattle, sheep, horses, and carriages; of bodies and souls of slaves.'),
('REV', 18, 14, 'REV.18.14', 'And they will say: “The fruit of your soul’s desire has departed from you; all your luxury and splendor have vanished, never to be seen again.”'),
('REV', 18, 15, 'REV.18.15', 'The merchants who sold these things and gained their wealth from her will stand at a distance, in fear of her torment. They will weep and mourn,'),
('REV', 18, 16, 'REV.18.16', 'saying: “Woe, woe to the great city, clothed in fine linen and purple and scarlet, adorned with gold and precious stones and pearls!'),
('REV', 18, 17, 'REV.18.17', 'For in a single hour such fabulous wealth has been destroyed!” Every shipmaster, passenger, and sailor, and all who make their living from the sea, will stand at a distance'),
('REV', 18, 18, 'REV.18.18', 'and cry out at the sight of the smoke rising from the fire that consumes her. “What city was ever like this great city?” they will exclaim.'),
('REV', 18, 19, 'REV.18.19', 'Then they will throw dust on their heads as they weep and mourn and cry out: “Woe, woe to the great city, where all who had ships on the sea were enriched by her wealth! For in a single hour she has been destroyed.”'),
('REV', 18, 20, 'REV.18.20', 'Rejoice over her, O heaven, and you saints and apostles and prophets, because God has pronounced for you His judgment against her.'),
('REV', 18, 21, 'REV.18.21', 'Then a mighty angel picked up a stone the size of a great millstone and cast it into the sea, saying: “With such violence the great city of Babylon will be cast down, never to be seen again.'),
('REV', 18, 22, 'REV.18.22', 'And the sound of harpists and musicians, of flute players and trumpeters, will never ring out in you again. Nor will any craftsmen of any trade be found in you again, nor the sound of a millstone be heard in you again.'),
('REV', 18, 23, 'REV.18.23', 'The light of a lamp will never shine in you again, and the voices of a bride and bridegroom will never call out in you again. For your merchants were the great ones of the earth, because all the nations were deceived by your sorcery.”'),
('REV', 18, 24, 'REV.18.24', 'And there was found in her the blood of prophets and saints, and of all who had been slain on the earth.'),
('REV', 19, 1, 'REV.19.1', 'After this I heard a sound like the roar of a great multitude in heaven, shouting: “Hallelujah! Salvation and glory and power belong to our God!'),
('REV', 19, 2, 'REV.19.2', 'For His judgments are true and just. He has judged the great prostitute who corrupted the earth with her immorality. He has avenged the blood of His servants that was poured out by her hand.”'),
('REV', 19, 3, 'REV.19.3', 'And a second time they called out: “Hallelujah! Her smoke rises forever and ever.”'),
('REV', 19, 4, 'REV.19.4', 'And the twenty-four elders and the four living creatures fell down and worshiped God who sits on the throne, saying: “Amen, Hallelujah!”'),
('REV', 19, 5, 'REV.19.5', 'Then a voice came from the throne, saying: “Praise our God, all you who serve Him, and those who fear Him, small and great alike!”'),
('REV', 19, 6, 'REV.19.6', 'And I heard a sound like the roar of a great multitude, like the rushing of many waters, and like a mighty rumbling of thunder, crying out: “Hallelujah! For the Lord our God the Almighty reigns.'),
('REV', 19, 7, 'REV.19.7', 'Let us rejoice and be glad and give Him the glory. For the marriage of the Lamb has come, and His bride has made herself ready.'),
('REV', 19, 8, 'REV.19.8', 'She was given clothing of fine linen, bright and pure.” For the fine linen she wears is the righteous acts of the saints.'),
('REV', 19, 9, 'REV.19.9', 'Then the angel told me to write, “Blessed are those who are invited to the marriage supper of the Lamb.” And he said to me, “These are the true words of God.”'),
('REV', 19, 10, 'REV.19.10', 'So I fell at his feet to worship him. But he told me, “Do not do that! I am a fellow servant with you and your brothers who rely on the testimony of Jesus. Worship God! For the testimony of Jesus is the spirit of prophecy.”'),
('REV', 19, 11, 'REV.19.11', 'Then I saw heaven standing open, and there before me was a white horse. And its rider is called Faithful and True. With righteousness He judges and wages war.'),
('REV', 19, 12, 'REV.19.12', 'He has eyes like blazing fire, and many royal crowns on His head. He has a name written on Him that only He Himself knows.'),
('REV', 19, 13, 'REV.19.13', 'He is dressed in a robe dipped in blood, and His name is The Word of God.'),
('REV', 19, 14, 'REV.19.14', 'The armies of heaven, dressed in fine linen, white and pure, follow Him on white horses.'),
('REV', 19, 15, 'REV.19.15', 'And from His mouth proceeds a sharp sword with which to strike down the nations, and He will rule them with an iron scepter. He treads the winepress of the fury of the wrath of God the Almighty.'),
('REV', 19, 16, 'REV.19.16', 'And He has a name written on His robe and on His thigh: KING OF KINGS AND LORD OF LORDS.'),
('REV', 19, 17, 'REV.19.17', 'Then I saw an angel standing in the sun, and he cried out in a loud voice to all the birds flying overhead, “Come, gather together for the great supper of God,'),
('REV', 19, 18, 'REV.19.18', 'so that you may eat the flesh of kings and commanders and mighty men, of horses and riders, of everyone slave and free, small and great.”'),
('REV', 19, 19, 'REV.19.19', 'Then I saw the beast and the kings of the earth with their armies assembled to wage war against the One seated on the horse, and against His army.'),
('REV', 19, 20, 'REV.19.20', 'But the beast was captured along with the false prophet, who on its behalf had performed signs deceiving those who had the mark of the beast and worshiped its image. Both the beast and the false prophet were thrown alive into the fiery lake of burning sulfur.'),
('REV', 19, 21, 'REV.19.21', 'And the rest were killed with the sword that proceeded from the mouth of the One seated on the horse. And all the birds gorged themselves on their flesh.'),
('REV', 20, 1, 'REV.20.1', 'Then I saw an angel coming down from heaven with the key to the Abyss, holding in his hand a great chain.'),
('REV', 20, 2, 'REV.20.2', 'He seized the dragon, that ancient serpent who is the devil and Satan, and bound him for a thousand years.'),
('REV', 20, 3, 'REV.20.3', 'And he threw him into the Abyss, shut it, and sealed it over him, so that he could not deceive the nations until the thousand years were complete. After that, he must be released for a brief period of time.'),
('REV', 20, 4, 'REV.20.4', 'Then I saw the thrones, and those seated on them had been given authority to judge. And I saw the souls of those who had been beheaded for their testimony of Jesus and for the word of God, and those who had not worshiped the beast or its image and had not received its mark on their foreheads or hands. And they came to life and reigned with Christ for a thousand years.'),
('REV', 20, 5, 'REV.20.5', 'The rest of the dead did not come back to life until the thousand years were complete. This is the first resurrection.'),
('REV', 20, 6, 'REV.20.6', 'Blessed and holy are those who share in the first resurrection! The second death has no power over them, but they will be priests of God and of Christ and will reign with Him for a thousand years.'),
('REV', 20, 7, 'REV.20.7', 'When the thousand years are complete, Satan will be released from his prison,'),
('REV', 20, 8, 'REV.20.8', 'and will go out to deceive the nations in the four corners of the earth—Gog and Magog—to assemble them for battle. Their number is like the sand of the seashore.'),
('REV', 20, 9, 'REV.20.9', 'And they marched across the broad expanse of the earth and surrounded the camp of the saints and the beloved city. But fire came down from heaven and consumed them.'),
('REV', 20, 10, 'REV.20.10', 'And the devil who had deceived them was thrown into the lake of fire and sulfur, into which the beast and the false prophet had already been thrown. There they will be tormented day and night forever and ever.'),
('REV', 20, 11, 'REV.20.11', 'Then I saw a great white throne and the One seated on it. Earth and heaven fled from His presence, and no place was found for them.'),
('REV', 20, 12, 'REV.20.12', 'And I saw the dead, great and small, standing before the throne. And books were opened, and one of them was the Book of Life. And the dead were judged according to their deeds, as recorded in the books.'),
('REV', 20, 13, 'REV.20.13', 'The sea gave up its dead, and Death and Hades gave up their dead, and each one was judged according to his deeds.'),
('REV', 20, 14, 'REV.20.14', 'Then Death and Hades were thrown into the lake of fire. This is the second death—the lake of fire.'),
('REV', 20, 15, 'REV.20.15', 'And if anyone was found whose name was not written in the Book of Life, he was thrown into the lake of fire.'),
('REV', 21, 1, 'REV.21.1', 'Then I saw a new heaven and a new earth, for the first heaven and earth had passed away, and the sea was no more.'),
('REV', 21, 2, 'REV.21.2', 'I saw the holy city, the new Jerusalem, coming down out of heaven from God, prepared as a bride adorned for her husband.'),
('REV', 21, 3, 'REV.21.3', 'And I heard a loud voice from the throne saying: “Behold, the dwelling place of God is with man, and He will dwell with them. They will be His people, and God Himself will be with them as their God.'),
('REV', 21, 4, 'REV.21.4', '‘He will wipe away every tear from their eyes,’ and there will be no more death or mourning or crying or pain, for the former things have passed away.”'),
('REV', 21, 5, 'REV.21.5', 'And the One seated on the throne said, “Behold, I make all things new.” Then He said, “Write this down, for these words are faithful and true.”'),
('REV', 21, 6, 'REV.21.6', 'And He told me, “It is done! I am the Alpha and the Omega, the Beginning and the End. To the thirsty I will give freely from the spring of the water of life.'),
('REV', 21, 7, 'REV.21.7', 'The one who overcomes will inherit all things, and I will be his God, and he will be My son.'),
('REV', 21, 8, 'REV.21.8', 'But to the cowardly and unbelieving and abominable and murderers and sexually immoral and sorcerers and idolaters and all liars, their place will be in the lake that burns with fire and sulfur. This is the second death.”'),
('REV', 21, 9, 'REV.21.9', 'Then one of the seven angels with the seven bowls full of the seven final plagues came and said to me, “Come, I will show you the bride, the wife of the Lamb.”'),
('REV', 21, 10, 'REV.21.10', 'And he carried me away in the Spirit to a mountain great and high, and showed me the holy city of Jerusalem coming down out of heaven from God,'),
('REV', 21, 11, 'REV.21.11', 'shining with the glory of God. Its radiance was like a most precious jewel, like a jasper, as clear as crystal.'),
('REV', 21, 12, 'REV.21.12', 'The city had a great and high wall with twelve gates inscribed with the names of the twelve tribes of Israel, and twelve angels at the gates.'),
('REV', 21, 13, 'REV.21.13', 'There were three gates on the east, three on the north, three on the south, and three on the west.'),
('REV', 21, 14, 'REV.21.14', 'The wall of the city had twelve foundations bearing the names of the twelve apostles of the Lamb.'),
('REV', 21, 15, 'REV.21.15', 'The angel who spoke with me had a golden measuring rod to measure the city and its gates and walls.'),
('REV', 21, 16, 'REV.21.16', 'The city lies foursquare, with its width the same as its length. And he measured the city with the rod, and all its dimensions were equal—12,000 stadia in length and width and height.'),
('REV', 21, 17, 'REV.21.17', 'And he measured its wall to be 144 cubits, by the human measure the angel was using.'),
('REV', 21, 18, 'REV.21.18', 'The wall was made of jasper, and the city itself of pure gold, as pure as glass.'),
('REV', 21, 19, 'REV.21.19', 'The foundations of the city walls were adorned with every kind of precious stone: The first foundation was jasper, the second sapphire, the third chalcedony, the fourth emerald,'),
('REV', 21, 20, 'REV.21.20', 'the fifth sardonyx, the sixth carnelian, the seventh chrysolite, the eighth beryl, the ninth topaz, the tenth chrysoprase, the eleventh jacinth, and the twelfth amethyst.'),
('REV', 21, 21, 'REV.21.21', 'And the twelve gates were twelve pearls, with each gate consisting of a single pearl. The main street of the city was pure gold, as clear as glass.'),
('REV', 21, 22, 'REV.21.22', 'But I saw no temple in the city, because the Lord God Almighty and the Lamb are its temple.'),
('REV', 21, 23, 'REV.21.23', 'And the city has no need of sun or moon to shine on it, because the glory of God illuminates the city, and the Lamb is its lamp.'),
('REV', 21, 24, 'REV.21.24', 'By its light the nations will walk, and into it the kings of the earth will bring their glory.'),
('REV', 21, 25, 'REV.21.25', 'Its gates will never be shut at the end of the day, because there will be no night there.'),
('REV', 21, 26, 'REV.21.26', 'And into the city will be brought the glory and honor of the nations.'),
('REV', 21, 27, 'REV.21.27', 'But nothing unclean will ever enter it, nor anyone who practices an abomination or a lie, but only those whose names are written in the Lamb’s Book of Life.'),
('REV', 22, 1, 'REV.22.1', 'Then the angel showed me a river of the water of life, as clear as crystal, flowing from the throne of God and of the Lamb'),
('REV', 22, 2, 'REV.22.2', 'down the middle of the main street of the city. On either side of the river stood a tree of life, bearing twelve kinds of fruit and yielding a fresh crop for each month. And the leaves of the tree are for the healing of the nations.'),
('REV', 22, 3, 'REV.22.3', 'No longer will there be any curse. The throne of God and of the Lamb will be within the city, and His servants will worship Him.'),
('REV', 22, 4, 'REV.22.4', 'They will see His face, and His name will be on their foreheads.'),
('REV', 22, 5, 'REV.22.5', 'There will be no more night in the city, and they will have no need for the light of a lamp or of the sun. For the Lord God will shine on them, and they will reign forever and ever.'),
('REV', 22, 6, 'REV.22.6', 'Then the angel said to me, “These words are faithful and true. The Lord, the God of the spirits of the prophets, has sent His angel to show His servants what must soon take place.”'),
('REV', 22, 7, 'REV.22.7', '“Behold, I am coming soon. Blessed is the one who keeps the words of prophecy in this book.”'),
('REV', 22, 8, 'REV.22.8', 'And I, John, am the one who heard and saw these things. And when I had heard and seen them, I fell down to worship at the feet of the angel who had shown me these things.'),
('REV', 22, 9, 'REV.22.9', 'But he said to me, “Do not do that! I am a fellow servant with you and your brothers the prophets, and with those who keep the words of this book. Worship God!”'),
('REV', 22, 10, 'REV.22.10', 'Then he told me, “Do not seal up the words of prophecy in this book, because the time is near.'),
('REV', 22, 11, 'REV.22.11', 'Let the unrighteous continue to be unrighteous, and the vile continue to be vile; let the righteous continue to practice righteousness, and the holy continue to be holy.”'),
('REV', 22, 12, 'REV.22.12', '“Behold, I am coming soon, and My reward is with Me, to give to each one according to what he has done.'),
('REV', 22, 13, 'REV.22.13', 'I am the Alpha and the Omega, the First and the Last, the Beginning and the End.”'),
('REV', 22, 14, 'REV.22.14', 'Blessed are those who wash their robes, so that they may have the right to the tree of life and may enter the city by its gates.'),
('REV', 22, 15, 'REV.22.15', 'But outside are the dogs, the sorcerers, the sexually immoral, the murderers, the idolaters, and everyone who loves and practices falsehood.'),
('REV', 22, 16, 'REV.22.16', '“I, Jesus, have sent My angel to give you this testimony for the churches. I am the Root and the Offspring of David, the bright Morning Star.”'),
('REV', 22, 17, 'REV.22.17', 'The Spirit and the bride say, “Come!” Let the one who hears say, “Come!” And let the one who is thirsty come, and the one who desires the water of life drink freely.'),
('REV', 22, 18, 'REV.22.18', 'I testify to everyone who hears the words of prophecy in this book: If anyone adds to them, God will add to him the plagues described in this book.'),
('REV', 22, 19, 'REV.22.19', 'And if anyone takes away from the words of this book of prophecy, God will take away his share in the tree of life and the holy city, which are described in this book.'),
('REV', 22, 20, 'REV.22.20', 'He who testifies to these things says, “Yes, I am coming soon.” Amen. Come, Lord Jesus!'),
('REV', 22, 21, 'REV.22.21', 'The grace of the Lord Jesus be with all the saints. Amen.')
) as x(osis, chapter, verse, ref, body)
join public.books b on b.osis_code = x.osis
join public.bible_versions v on v.id = b.version_id and v.code = 'BSB'
join public.chapters c on c.book_id = b.id and c.number = x.chapter
on conflict (chapter_id, number) do update set osis_ref = excluded.osis_ref, text = excluded.text;
